 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10102"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/L0-downstream-operations"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The downstream business function that creates, manages, and optimizes the commercial value of petroleum products and services through market strategy, customer and channel management, supply and trading, commercial planning and scheduling, pricing, sales, and order-to-cash activities."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Spans the commercial hydrocarbon lifecycle from supply acquisition and commercial optimization through product positioning, customer order capture, allocation, fulfilment coordination, invoicing, payment, and commercial performance management. It coordinates with refining, midstream, distribution, finance, and enterprise IT, but does not itself encompass their underlying physical operations or enterprise-wide technology services."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 1
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Planning And Optimization Includes Processes Such As Demand Forecasting, Local And Regional Optimization, Backcasting And Inventory Management Across The Value Chain."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Planning & Scheduling"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 2
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Demand forecasting processes for commercial planning across the value chain."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Demand Forecasting"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Q1 decision (the decision owner, 2026-09-19, Option A): the L4 carries the same label as its L3 parent (CM-1-1-1) and is its only child; authored in place as the operational forecast-production cycle, with the L3 remaining the domain umbrella — no tree change, consistent with the restraint precedent on PTC-001; a later naming pass may disambiguate the duplicate prefLabels. Q2 decision (the decision owner, 2026-09-19, Option A): binding constraint on the future definition of CM-1-2-6-2-3 — it must be scoped as Supply And Trading's operational demand forecasting within Refined Product Supply Chain Management and must not claim ownership of the approved commercial planning forecast; same decide-versus-advise pattern as PTC-002. Evidence basis: the planning-cycle forecast (monthly, product/market level; IEA OMR and EIA STEO practice) is distinct from operational network demand forecasting (short-notice, terminal/station level; Mota et al. 2017). APQC 10240 'Evaluate and revise demand forecasting approach' is REVIEW LINK only; approach-governance content sits closest to CM-1-3-5-1-2, not here. Step 3d naming pass (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Demand Forecasting' to 'Produce Demand Forecast' — critical semantic-collision resolution. Prior label not retained as altLabel: the L3 keeps it as prefLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10240"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-iea-omr-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Product Demand Forecasting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop, agree, and publish the recurring product demand forecast that downstream commercial planning runs on — expected demand by product, market, location, and period — by combining a statistical baseline with customer input and market intelligence, and monitor forecast performance so the published forecast remains a reliable planning basis."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce Demand Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring demand-forecast production cycle: preparing forecasting master data and history, developing the statistical baseline, adjusting it with customer input and market intelligence, publishing the approved forecast with its component-level breakdown, and monitoring forecast performance. Its output is the single approved demand forecast consumed by Regional Optimization, Refinery Optimization, and Supply And Trading. Excludes deciding how demand is met — supply, production, inventory, and allocation choices are owned by Regional Optimization (CM-1-1-2); excludes capturing or committing customer orders, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7); excludes Supply And Trading's operational refined-product demand forecasting (Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand, CM-1-2-6-2-3), bounded per the batch 03 decision; excludes designing and agreeing the cross-functional forecasting process with sales, owned by Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process (CM-1-3-5-1-2). For a given planning cycle, Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) completes approval and release of the demand-forecast version before Regional Optimization (CM-1-1-2) uses that version as an approved planning input. Forecasting and optimization remain iterative across versions and cycles. Capture Product Demand Requirements (CM-1-1-4-7-1) assembles the refinery case's demand requirements from the demand forecast published by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1). Receive Demand Forecast (CM-1-2-1-1-2) incorporates the demand forecast published by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) into the trading forward view.\nIn scope: Prepare and validate forecasting inputs | develop the statistical baseline forecast | incorporate customer input and market intelligence | publish the approved forecast and component-level forecast plan | monitor forecast accuracy, bias, and adjustment effect\nOut of scope: Supply, production, inventory, and allocation decisions (Regional Optimization, CM-1-1-2) | customer order capture and commitment (Order Management, CM-1-3-7) | trading-side receipt and use of the published forecast (Receive Demand Forecast, CM-1-2-1-1-2) | Supply And Trading operational refined-product demand forecasting (Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand, CM-1-2-6-2-3) | sales forecasting process design (Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process, CM-1-3-5-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cleansed demand history"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "customer plans and commitments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market intelligence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "product and market master data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved and published demand forecast with component-level forecast plan"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce and maintain the single approved product demand forecast that downstream commercial planning runs on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/priorPreferredLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Demand Forecasting"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10252"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Data Preparation"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Prepare and validate the reference data and demand history that each forecast cycle depends on — product and market hierarchies, customer and location groupings, units of measure, and the historical demand series cleansed of outliers and one-off distortions — so the statistical baseline is built from accurate, planning-consistent inputs."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Fourth of the four parallel master-data nodes; consolidation under a governed master-data capability is parked for the EPM Data Governance workstream per the decision recorded on CM-1-1-2-12 (2026-09-18) and deliberately not resolved here — the boundary to CM-1-1-2-12 was already established from its approved out_of_scope. APQC 10252 'Maintain master data' is a WEAK distribution-master-data candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Prepare Master Data To Create Demand Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers per-cycle readiness of forecasting inputs: maintaining forecast-specific reference data, aligning product and market hierarchies to planning definitions, and cleansing demand history for outliers, supply disruptions, and other events that would distort the baseline. Excludes supply-planning reference and parameter data, owned by Maintain Supply Planning Master Data (CM-1-1-2-12); excludes production-scheduling master data, owned by Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data (CM-1-1-7-2-1); excludes customer, price, product, tax, and location master data, owned by Manage Commercial Master Data Stewardship under Order Management (CM-1-3-7-1); excludes enterprise master-data policy and governance, which sit with the Data Governance workstream.\nIn scope: Maintain forecast-specific reference data | align product and market hierarchies to planning definitions | cleanse and adjust demand history for distorting events | validate data readiness for the forecast cycle\nOut of scope: Supply-planning master data (Maintain Supply Planning Master Data, CM-1-1-2-12) | production-scheduling master data (Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data, CM-1-1-7-2-1) | customer, price, product, tax, and location master data (Manage Commercial Master Data Stewardship, CM-1-3-7-1) | enterprise master-data policy and governance (Data Governance workstream) | statistical model development (Develop Statistical Baseline, CM-1-1-1-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "customer and location groupings"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "product and market hierarchy definitions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "raw sales and lifting history"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "recorded demand-distorting events"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "validated forecasting dataset and reference data for the cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Ensure each forecast cycle starts from validated reference data and cleansed demand history."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20043"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-iea-omr-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Baseline Forecasting"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Statistical Baseline Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Generate the objective statistical baseline forecast of product demand from cleansed history and demonstrated demand drivers, selecting and tuning forecasting methods by product and market segment before any judgmental input is applied."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). APQC 20043 'Develop baseline forecasts' scored STRONG but was REJECTED at the Step 3b human gate as circular validation (APQC validating APQC); authored independently per that rejection. Driver-based statistical modeling of fuels demand (economic activity, prices, weather) follows the practice documented in EIA STEO product-consumption modules; monthly product-level demand assessment follows IEA OMR practice. 'Baseline' is used in the demand-planning sense — the pre-judgment statistical forecast — not the plan-baseline sense used in backcasting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop Statistical Baseline"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers producing the unbiased statistical starting point of the forecast cycle: choosing and parameterizing forecasting methods, generating the baseline at the agreed hierarchy levels, and documenting model fit and known limitations. The baseline is deliberately judgment-free — commercial knowledge enters in the adjustment step. Excludes adjusting the forecast with customer input and market intelligence, owned by Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence (CM-1-1-1-1-3); excludes publication and disaggregation, owned by Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan (CM-1-1-1-1-4); excludes measuring forecast performance, owned by Monitor Demand Forecasting Performance and Reporting (CM-1-1-1-1-5).\nIn scope: Select and tune statistical forecasting methods by segment | generate the baseline forecast at agreed hierarchy levels | apply demonstrated demand drivers | document model fit and limitations\nOut of scope: Judgmental adjustment of the forecast (CM-1-1-1-1-3) | forecast publication and disaggregation (CM-1-1-1-1-4) | forecast performance measurement (CM-1-1-1-1-5) | trading revenue and asset forecasting (Forecasting & Optimization, CM-1-2-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/rejected"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "demand driver variables"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "historical model performance"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "validated forecasting dataset"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "statistical baseline forecast by product and market segment"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce the objective, judgment-free statistical starting point for the demand forecast."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10106"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-iea-omr-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consensus Forecast Adjustment"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Judgmental Forecast Adjustment"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Review and adjust the statistical baseline with demand knowledge the models cannot see — customer plans and commitments, sales and marketing input, and market and competitive intelligence — recording each adjustment and its rationale so the agreed forecast reflects the best available view of demand."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Written as the consensus/enrichment step of standard demand-planning practice; the IEA OMR's monthly demand revisions on new market information are the reference pattern for judgment applied over a statistical basis. Adjustments are recorded with rationale specifically so CM-1-1-1-1-5 can measure whether they added accuracy — the adjustment record is part of the process, not an implementation detail. APQC 10106 'Perform customer and market intelligence analysis' is REVIEW LINK; it describes the intelligence capability this step consumes, not this step itself."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Adjust Forecast Incorporating Customer Input and Market Intelligence"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the judgmental overlay and agreement step of the forecast cycle: gathering structured input from customer-facing and market-facing teams, challenging and applying adjustments to the baseline, and recording who changed what and why so performance monitoring can attribute accuracy effects. Excludes producing the statistical baseline itself (CM-1-1-1-1-2); excludes gathering market and customer intelligence as an ongoing capability — this step consumes intelligence, it does not own its production; excludes negotiating or committing the underlying customer volumes, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7) and sales.\nIn scope: Collect structured customer and market input | review and challenge the statistical baseline | apply and document adjustments with rationale | agree the adjusted forecast for publication\nOut of scope: Statistical baseline generation (CM-1-1-1-1-2) | ownership of market and customer intelligence production | customer negotiation and order commitment (Order Management, CM-1-3-7) | publication of the agreed forecast (CM-1-1-1-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "customer plans and commitments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market and competitive intelligence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sales and marketing input"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "statistical baseline forecast"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "agreed adjusted forecast with documented adjustment rationale"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Turn the statistical baseline into the agreed forecast by applying documented customer and market knowledge."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10306"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Publication"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Publish Demand Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approve and publish the agreed demand forecast as the versioned planning basis, and translate it into the component-level forecast plan — the detailed breakdown by product grade or component, location, and period — that downstream planning processes consume."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). 'Component level' is read as the detailed disaggregated planning level — product grade or blend component, location, and period — required by the consuming planning processes; the definition states the function without fixing a single technical reading. APQC 10306 'Generate line level plan' scored STRONG but was REJECTED at the Step 3b human gate as circular validation with an unrelated citation; authored independently. The published, versioned forecast is the contemporaneous baseline that CM-1-1-1-1-5 measures against — consistent with the locked backcasting discipline."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the release step of the forecast cycle: final approval, version identification, disaggregation of the agreed forecast to the component level used by planning, and distribution to its consumers. The published version is the fixed reference that both planning and forecast-performance measurement run against. Excludes acting on the forecast — supply, production, inventory, and allocation decisions are owned by Regional Optimization (CM-1-1-2) and Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4); excludes the consumers' own receipt and case-assembly steps, owned by Receive Demand Forecast (CM-1-2-1-1-2) and Capture Product Demand Requirements (CM-1-1-4-7-1). For a given forecast cycle and version, Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan (CM-1-1-1-1-4) publishes and makes the approved forecast available before Regional Optimization (CM-1-1-2) uses that version as an approved planning input. Other optimization work may proceed independently; subsequent forecast revisions can prompt another optimization run. Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan (CM-1-1-1-1-4) supplies the approved versioned component-level demand forecast that Capture Product Demand Requirements (CM-1-1-4-7-1) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Approve and version the forecast for release | disaggregate to the component-level forecast plan | distribute the published forecast to consuming processes | maintain the published version as the fixed reference for the period\nOut of scope: Supply and allocation decisions (Regional Optimization, CM-1-1-2) | refinery case-basis assembly (Capture Product Demand Requirements, CM-1-1-4-7-1) | trading-side receipt (Receive Demand Forecast, CM-1-2-1-1-2) | forecast adjustment (CM-1-1-1-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/rejected"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "agreed adjusted forecast"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "planning calendar"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "product component and grade structures"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published versioned demand forecast and component-level forecast plan"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Release one versioned, detailed demand forecast that all downstream planning consumes."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16574"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Accuracy Monitoring"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Performance Measurement"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Measure and report how well published demand forecasts predicted actual demand — tracking accuracy, bias, and the effect of adjustments at agreed levels and lags — and feed the findings back into forecasting methods and adjustment behavior."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 03 (2026-09-19). Measures the forecast against actual demand using the as-published version as the fixed comparison basis — the same contemporaneous-baseline discipline locked for Regional and Distribution Backcasting, applied to the demand side. EIA's published STEO forecast-accuracy evaluations are the reference practice for measuring product-demand forecasts against realized data. Specific accuracy metrics and thresholds are deliberately not named; they belong to the KPI workstream, not the process definition. APQC 16574 'Monitor and report performance' is a WEAK marketing-channel candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.1.1.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Monitor Demand Forecasting Performance and Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers recurring forecast-performance measurement and reporting: comparing actual demand with the forecast as published for that period, analyzing error and bias by segment and lag, evaluating whether judgmental adjustments improved accuracy, reporting results, and recommending method and process improvements. Actuals are compared with the contemporaneously published forecast version, not a later revision. Excludes explaining supply-plan versus actual outcomes, owned by Regional Backcasting (CM-1-1-5) and Distribution Backcasting (CM-1-1-6); excludes agreeing the cross-functional forecasting process design with sales, owned by Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process (CM-1-3-5-1-2).\nIn scope: Compare actual demand with the published forecast version | analyze forecast error and bias by segment and lag | evaluate the accuracy effect of judgmental adjustments | report performance and recommend improvements\nOut of scope: Plan-versus-actual supply and distribution variance analysis (Regional Backcasting, CM-1-1-5; Distribution Backcasting, CM-1-1-6) | forecasting process design and agreement (Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process, CM-1-3-5-1-2) | making the forecast adjustments themselves (CM-1-1-1-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "actual demand history"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "adjustment records with rationale"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published forecast versions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "forecast performance report with improvement recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish whether published forecasts are getting more or less reliable, and why, so the forecasting cycle improves."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19569"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Optimize the integrated regional supply, demand, production, inventory, and product-movement plan to maximize commercial margin and reliably fulfill customer commitments within refinery, terminal, transportation, product-quality, and contractual constraints."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Regional Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Regional Optimization determines the commercially preferred regional supply-and-disposition plan, including demand allocation, supply sourcing, product placement, inventory positioning, exchanges, and inter-regional movements. It does not directly operate refinery units, terminals, pipelines, vessels, trucks, or retail/wholesale delivery activities; those functions provide capabilities, constraints, and execution feedback to the optimization cycle."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/rejected"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-3-7"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
