 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Retired per PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), decided by the decision owner 2026-09-18. The node carries no local meaning: its Step 3b provenance is a WEAK match against the APQC element “Manage employee development”, and under Option A all three of its children leave. Nothing remains to define, so it is retired rather than defined or left pending. The node itself is still present in downstream_process_map.json — removing it is a Step 3d tree change, not a workbook change. Retired here means “will not be defined”, not “gone from the tree”. Step 3d PTC-001 tree pass (2026-09-21): tombstoned as owl:deprecated — removed from active navigation, retained for lineage (PTC-001 / PTC-001-B traceability). Physical removal is a later explicit retirement decision once PTC-001-B is resolved."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean",
    "@value": true
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.4.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial Development"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/lifecycleStatus": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/lifecycle-status/retired"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-6-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. The decision owner accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. It cannot be moved yet — verified against downstream_process_map.json, the destination domain has no decomposition at all, so there is no parent to move it to. Set to blocked rather than left pending so it is not read as queued for definition. Revived by the Step 3d tree pass, not by a definition batch. Destination undecided: Finance or a future strategy domain. The decision owner ruled out creating a Strategy L1, since the ten L1 definitions are approved baseline and changing the L1 set is a charter-level decision. Step 3d PTC-001 tree pass (2026-09-21): stays blocked under PTC-001-B — enterprise strategy-ownership decision (options: Corporate Planning within Finance / Corporate Strategy / executive cross-functional governance). Parent Commercial Development tombstoned (owl:deprecated) pending PTC-001-B resolution."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.4.6.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop Strategic Business Plan"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/holdReason": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. The decision owner accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. It cannot be moved yet — verified against downstream_process_map.json, the destination domain has no decomposition at all, so there is no parent to move it to. Set to blocked rather than left pending so it is not read as queued for definition. Revived by the Step 3d tree pass, not by a definition batch. Destination undecided: Finance or a future strategy domain. The decision owner ruled out creating a Strategy L1, since the ten L1 definitions are approved baseline and changing the L1 set is a charter-level decision. Step 3d PTC-001 tree pass (2026-09-21): stays blocked under PTC-001-B — enterprise strategy-ownership decision (options: Corporate Planning within Finance / Corporate Strategy / executive cross-functional governance). Parent Commercial Development tombstoned (owl:deprecated) pending PTC-001-B resolution."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/holdStatus": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/hold-status/implementation-hold"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-6-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10943"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/L2-financial-planning-and-performance-management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop, coordinate, consolidate, challenge, approve, publish, monitor, and refresh enterprise and business-unit budgets in accordance with the approved financial-planning calendar, planning assumptions, delegated authorities, and financial-control requirements. Operating domains own their underlying demand, volume, margin, capacity, operating-cost, capital, and resource assumptions; Finance owns the financial planning process, consolidation, control, and reporting framework."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. The decision owner accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. Decided 2026-09-18: no split — one node under Finance. The refinery's operational input to budgeting is already carried by the Refinery Optimization case basis (CM-1-1-4-7-1 to -6) and the Refinery Planning outputs, so a second node would duplicate batch 02. Moved to Finance L2 'Financial Planning and Performance Management' by the Step 3d PTC-001 tree pass (2026-09-21); level 5 → 3; old notation CM 1.1.4.6.2 kept as historical provenance. Definition authored 2026-09-21 under the tree-pass mini-batch. 'approve' in the definition refers to the budget-review/approval workflow the process administers; final approval authority remains with the applicable delegated authority per the locked boundary."
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source note (SRC-APQC-PCF-001): PCF Finance & accounting sections as the structural consistency reference (discovery/comparison only)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.4.6.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Plan Budgets"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develops, coordinates, consolidates, challenges, publishes, monitors, and refreshes enterprise and business-unit budgets in accordance with the approved financial-planning calendar, planning assumptions, delegated authorities, and financial-control requirements. Operating domains own their underlying demand, volume, margin, capacity, operating-cost, capital, and resource assumptions and supply their plans and forecasts as inputs; Finance owns the budget process, consolidation, control framework, and reporting. The process produces the budget envelopes that functional allocation processes distribute within their own plans; final approval remains with the applicable delegated authority.\nIn scope: budget development, consolidation, challenge, and version governance | budget publication and refresh | budget monitoring against actuals | administration of the budget review and approval workflow\nOut of scope: enterprise strategic direction, portfolio choices, and capital allocation decisions (pending PTC-001-B) | underlying demand, volume, margin, capacity, operating-cost, capital, and resource assumptions (operating domains) | final budget approval (applicable delegated authority) | distribution of an approved envelope within a domain plan (e.g., marketing communications resource allocation, CM-1-3-5-3-5) | transaction recording, accounting, and treasury"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "actual results against current budgets"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved financial-planning calendar and planning assumptions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "business-unit plans, forecasts, and assumption sets from operating domains"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved, published, version-governed enterprise and business-unit budgets | budget variance monitoring reports"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Deliver the published, version-governed enterprise and business-unit budgets that authorize spending and investment for the plan period."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Finance"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-6-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Parked by PTC-001 (step3c-parked-tree-changes.md), 2026-09-18. The decision owner accepted Option A: this node leaves Refinery Planning. Renamed 2026-09-21 by the Step 3d PTC-001 tree pass (naming-pass discipline: prior name 'Manage Site Specific Business Risk' retained as altLabel and in migration metadata); moved to Refining L2 'Refinery Performance and Risk Coordination', level 5 → 3. 'Coordinate' is deliberate: this process coordinates ownership, treatment, monitoring, and escalation of site business risks — it does not set enterprise risk policy or own specialist controls. The taxonomy holds no enterprise risk capability; this row must not be read as one."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/17462"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-er-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-osha-psm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Site Specific Business Risk"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/L2-refinery-performance-and-risk-coordination"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify, assess, document, prioritize, coordinate treatment of, monitor, and escalate site-specific business risks affecting refinery objectives, production reliability, cost, schedule, asset availability, supply, product disposition, and local stakeholder commitments, in accordance with enterprise risk policy, delegated authority, and specialist-control requirements."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source note (SRC-APQC-PCF-001): structural consistency reference (discovery/comparison only)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source note (SRC-EPA-ER-001): emergency-response boundary: release and emergency response sit with EHS"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source note (SRC-OSHA-PSM-001): process-safety boundary: site business risk excludes EHS/process-safety management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.4.6.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate Site Business Risk Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinates site-level risk ownership, treatment, monitoring, and escalation; it does not set enterprise risk appetite or policy, replace EHS / process-safety management, administer insurance, approve capital, manage financial-market risk, conduct Internal Audit, or own Legal, Compliance, Security, Cybersecurity, or business-continuity authorities. The process is event-driven when new or changed risks, incidents, material threshold breaches, or escalation conditions arise; it also performs periodic monitoring and review of existing site-risk ownership, treatment plans, and status.\nIn scope: identification, assessment, documentation, and prioritization of site-specific business risks | coordination of risk ownership and treatment | risk monitoring and escalation\nOut of scope: enterprise risk appetite and policy | EHS and process-safety management | insurance administration | capital approval | financial-market risk | Internal Audit | Legal, Compliance, Security, Cybersecurity, and business-continuity authorities | operation of refinery units"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "enterprise risk policy, delegated authorities, and specialist-control requirements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "refinery performance data against refinery objectives"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "site risk registers, risk assessments, and incident records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "assigned site-risk ownership and coordinated treatment plans | monitored risk status with escalations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Ensure every site business risk has an owner, a treatment plan, and a monitored status — and that what the site cannot resolve is escalated through delegated authority."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refining"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-7",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19569"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cmu-refplan-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-snf-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery Economic Optimization"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery LP Optimization"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery Plan Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Run the recurring economic-optimization cycle that produces the refinery production plan — assembling the case basis, building and running optimization cases, analyzing scenarios, and selecting the economically preferred production case for approval."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Parent-versus-child distinctness resolved per the decision owner's decision (2026-09-18, Option 1): Refinery Planning (CM-1-1-4) owns the approved plan and its commercial targets; this node owns the recurring optimization run cycle that produces the candidate plan. Without that split the two primary purposes were near-identical. The eight existing L5 children — six “Capture …” nodes, Evaluate Crude & Feedstock, and Perform Scenario Analysis — are coherent under this reading as case-basis assembly and case analysis. “Capture Monthly Operating Plan” (CM-1-1-4-7-7) appears to name a document rather than a process and is flagged for review in the L5 batch, not resolved here. Avoided naming a specific optimization application; “LP” appears only as an alternate label because it is established industry shorthand."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.4.7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the optimization cycle inside Refinery Planning and Optimization: gathering the demand, crude availability, price, constraint, inventory, and current-plan basis for a case; building and running the optimization model; comparing alternatives through scenario analysis; and recommending the economically preferred case. Accountability for the approved production plan and its commercial targets remains with Refinery Planning and Optimization. Excludes detailed unit-operation scheduling, tank and transfer line-ups, blend execution, and process control, owned by Refining; excludes optimization-model and application administration, owned by Process Excellence & IT.\nIn scope: Assemble case basis from demand, crude availability, price, constraints, inventory, and current plan | build and run optimization cases | scenario and sensitivity analysis | compare production alternatives on margin | recommend the economically preferred production case\nOut of scope: Approval and ownership of the production plan and its commercial targets (Refinery Planning and Optimization) | detailed unit scheduling, tank line-ups, and blend execution (Refining, Refinery Production Planning and Scheduling) | process control and operational departures from plan (Refining) | optimization application administration and model platform support (Process Excellence & IT) | real-time and closed-loop unit optimization (Refining)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/constrainedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-3-7"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-2-10"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "crude and feedstock availability and assays"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "crude, feedstock, and product prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current approved operating plan"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "inventory position"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "product demand requirements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "refinery capacity and operating constraints"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/plannedChildNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Build Optimization Case"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Recommend Preferred Production Case"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Validate Case Basis"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "recommended economically preferred refinery production case with supporting scenario analysis"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce and recommend the economically preferred refinery production case for the planning period."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-7-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11331"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-bjce-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-lfmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Demand Basis"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Demand Basis Capture"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Product Demand Requirements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4-7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assemble the demand requirements that the refinery production case must satisfy — by product, volume, quality grade, location, and delivery period — drawing on the approved demand forecast, firm contractual commitments, and internal transfer requirements for the planning period."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 02 (2026-09-18). Read as a case-basis assembly step inside the CM-1-1-4-7 Refinery Optimization run cycle: this node establishes one input of the optimization case, it does not own the underlying business decision or the source data. Sibling “Capture …” nodes were defined together so their boundaries partition the case basis without overlap. “Requirements” is read as the obligations the plan must meet, not as product specification requirements. Verb kept as the taxonomy label “Capture”; “Receive Demand Forecast” (CM-1-2-1-1-2) is the existing precedent for a consume-not-produce node."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.4.7.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Product Demand Requirements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers converting demand signals into the demand basis of an optimization case: selecting the applicable forecast version, adding firm contractual and internal transfer obligations, reconciling units and product grades to planning definitions, and confirming the basis with the demand owner. Excludes producing or owning the forecast itself, which belongs to Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) and Refined Product Demand Management (CM-1-2-6-2). Excludes capturing or committing customer orders, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7).\nIn scope: Select the applicable approved demand forecast version | add firm contractual and term commitments | add internal and inter-refinery transfer requirements | reconcile product grades, units, and periods to planning definitions | confirm the agreed demand basis for the case\nOut of scope: Producing or owning the demand forecast, owned by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) | forecasting refined product demand, owned by Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand (CM-1-2-6-2-3) | capturing and committing customer orders, owned by Order Management (CM-1-3-7) | negotiating the underlying customer commitment, owned by Commercial & Marketing sales | placing supply against demand, owned by Allocate Finished Products (CM-1-1-2-11)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
