    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20882"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-snf-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Schedule-Level Resource Assignment"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assign and confirm the schedule-level shared resources each day's plan depends on — tankage assumptions, movement and rack windows, berth and loading slots, and other capacity the schedule reserves — so the daily scheduling basis is physically feasible before it is issued."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). 'Resources' read as schedule-level shared capacity — tankage, windows, slots — not personnel rostering or maintenance crews; the capacity-reservation sentence was added at the decision owner's direction to protect the boundary where capacity allocation could be confused with refinery operations. APQC 20882 is an IT-services candidate; false lexical match, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Schedule Resources"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers schedule-level resource assignment: checking availability, reserving and assigning capacity against the day's plan, resolving conflicts among competing schedule needs, and confirming feasibility. Resource assignment represents capacity reservations and schedule assumptions; it does not direct tank line-ups, valve states, transfers, or other operating configurations. Excludes physical line-ups, transfers, and operation of the resources, owned by Refining and Midstream per the locked rules; excludes maintenance resource and crew planning, owned by Refining's engineering and maintenance functions — outage windows enter the schedule through Manage The Interface to Planning, Operations, Engineering & Maintenance (CM-1-1-7-2-6).\nIn scope: Check and reserve schedule-level capacity | assign resources to the day's plan | resolve competing schedule resource conflicts | confirm physical feasibility of the daily basis\nOut of scope: Physical line-ups, valve states, and resource operation (Refining, Midstream) | maintenance and crew planning (Refining) | outage window intake (CM-1-1-7-2-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "competing schedule demands"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "daily plan"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "resource availability and outage windows"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "confirmed resource assignments for the daily basis"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Make sure the day's plan has the capacity it assumes."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10774"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-api-mpms-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm31-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Production and Yield Accounting"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery Material Balance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Close the refinery's daily production balance — reconciling measured feed receipts, unit charges and yields, blending, shipments, fuel and loss, and inventory changes into an accounted material balance — and actualize production against the schedule so planning, scheduling, and backcasting run on verified actuals."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Production accounting is the refinery's daily material balance and yield actualization — distinct from network stock reconciliation (batch 04) and from financial inventory accounting. APQC 10774 'Perform inventory accounting' scored STRONG but is financial asset accounting; treated as a false match, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform Production Accounting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers daily production and yield accounting per refinery hydrocarbon-management practice (EI HM 31): assembling measured quantities, balancing the site by unit and material, attributing imbalance and apparent loss for investigation, and publishing the day's actuals. Excludes owning the physical measurement basis, which sits with Measure Inventory (CM-1-1-3-7-4) with readings taken by asset operators; excludes periodic network book-to-physical stock reconciliation, owned by Perform Inventory Reconciliation (CM-1-1-3-7-5), which this balance feeds; excludes financial and cost accounting, owned by Finance under the locked rule. Perform Production Accounting (CM-1-1-7-1-3) supplies the verified daily refinery material balance and production actuals that Perform Inventory Reconciliation (CM-1-1-3-7-5) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Assemble measured receipts, charges, yields, shipments, and inventory changes | balance the site by unit and material daily | attribute imbalance and apparent loss for investigation | publish actualized production against schedule\nOut of scope: Measurement basis and standards (CM-1-1-3-7-4) | network book-to-physical reconciliation (CM-1-1-3-7-5) | financial and cost accounting (Finance)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "measured quantities and movement tickets"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "shipment and inventory records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "unit charge and yield data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "closed daily production balance with actualized yields"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Deliver a verified daily account of what the refinery actually received, made, shipped, and lost."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10303"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-bjce-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cmu-refplan-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-snf-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery Production Scheduling"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and maintain the refinery production schedule that implements the approved monthly plan — sequencing campaigns, schedule-level unit commitments, blends, and movements over the scheduling horizon, managing schedule exceptions, and coordinating the interfaces the schedule depends on — so the plan becomes a current schedule that provides the approved basis for refinery execution."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Q1 decision (the decision owner, 2026-09-19): the refinery planning-scheduling-operations hierarchy is approved. CM-1-1-7 owns the refinery production-scheduling layer: translating approved refinery plans into dated, feasible campaign, production, movement, and resource schedules; managing schedule exceptions and cross-functional interfaces; and maintaining schedule-level performance visibility. Refining owns detailed unit-operation scheduling and all operational execution, including process-control decisions, line-ups, transfers, blend execution, utility operation, and immediate safety/reliability departures from the schedule. Supported by the planning/scheduling/operations separation documented in SNF R29/08 and Moro (BJCE); the locked rule's 'detailed unit-operation scheduling' is the operations layer, not this one. APQC 10303 is a WEAK generic candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Production Scheduling"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the refinery scheduling layer between planning and operations: maintaining scheduling master data, reviewing the production wheel and run lengths, creating the dated sequencing plan, managing exceptions, measuring scheduling performance, and managing interfaces to planning, operations, and engineering and maintenance. Under the approved planning-scheduling-operations hierarchy, Refining owns detailed unit-operation scheduling and all operational execution; this L4 owns the production schedule that provides the approved basis for that execution. Excludes the monthly plan itself, owned by Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4); excludes the daily scheduling basis, owned by Daily Execution Planning (CM-1-1-7-1). For each scheduling horizon, Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4) makes the applicable approved plan or authorized revision available before Production Scheduling (CM-1-1-7-2) releases the corresponding executable schedule. Scheduling preparation may overlap planning, and feasibility feedback may trigger plan revisions.\nIn scope: Maintain the scheduling basis and master data | maintain the production wheel and run lengths | create and refresh the dated sequencing plan | manage schedule exceptions and interfaces | measure scheduling performance\nOut of scope: Monthly production plan (CM-1-1-4) | unit-operation scheduling and execution (Refining) | daily instruction issuance (CM-1-1-7-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/weekly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved monthly plan"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "execution feedback"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "outage and turnaround windows"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production wheel and constraints"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current production schedule providing the approved basis for execution"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Turn the approved monthly plan into a current schedule that provides the approved basis for refinery execution."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10252"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Scheduling Master Data Maintenance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Create, maintain, and retire the reference and parameter data the production scheduling model depends on — unit capacities and constraints, product and recipe definitions, transition and changeover rules, tankage parameters, and scheduling calendars — so scheduling results remain accurate and reproducible."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). One of the four parallel master-data nodes named in CM-1-1-2-12's approved note (2026-09-18); the parked consolidation question applies here as well and is deliberately not resolved. Whether refinery scheduling runs on a dedicated scheduling system whose master-data ownership needs linking to a later system-integration workstream is a follow-up noted in the batch 06 PR. APQC 10252 scored STRONG but is distribution master data; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Maintain Production Scheduling Master Data"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers stewardship of production-scheduling-specific reference and parameter data over its lifecycle: requesting and validating changes, applying effective dates, and confirming scheduling results remain consistent after a change. Excludes supply-planning master data, owned by Maintain Supply Planning Master Data (CM-1-1-2-12); excludes demand-forecast data preparation (CM-1-1-1-1-1); excludes customer, price, product, tax, and location master data (Manage Commercial Master Data Stewardship, CM-1-3-7-1); excludes enterprise master-data policy and governance, which sit with the Data Governance workstream.\nIn scope: Maintain unit capacity, constraint, and recipe data | maintain transition and changeover rules | apply and validate effective-dated changes | confirm scheduling consistency after changes\nOut of scope: Supply-planning master data (CM-1-1-2-12) | demand-forecast data preparation (CM-1-1-1-1-1) | commercial master data (CM-1-3-7-1) | enterprise master-data policy (Data Governance workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "change requests from scheduling and operations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "effective-dating rules"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "unit test-run and constraint updates"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "validated scheduling reference and parameter data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the scheduling model's reference data true to the real refinery."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12916"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-bjce-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Campaign Sequence and Run-Length Review"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Product Wheel Review"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Review and maintain the production wheel — the recurring sequence of product campaigns — and each campaign's run length, balancing transition losses and changeover costs against inventory, demand coverage, and unit constraints, so the schedule is built on an economically sound campaign structure."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). 'Production wheel' is the standard campaign-scheduling structure where sequence-dependent changeovers matter — directly relevant to specialty and blended product lines. Whether the wheel structure applies across all units or only campaign-oriented lines is a follow-up noted in the batch 06 PR. APQC 12916 is a WEAK review-link; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Review Production Wheel and Run Length"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the periodic review of campaign sequence and duration: the transition structure (which product can follow which at what cost), wheel cycle time, run lengths per product against demand and storage, and wheel exceptions for demand shifts and outages. Excludes building the dated schedule itself, owned by Create Production Scheduling and Sequencing Plan (CM-1-1-7-2-3); excludes plan-period product mix decisions, owned by Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4); excludes executing transitions, owned by Refining.\nIn scope: Maintain the campaign transition structure and costs | set wheel cycle time and run lengths | review the wheel against demand, inventory, and constraints | approve wheel exceptions\nOut of scope: Dated schedule construction (CM-1-1-7-2-3) | plan-period product mix (CM-1-1-4) | transition execution (Refining)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "demand and inventory coverage by product"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "transition cost and constraint data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "unit campaign performance"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "maintained production wheel with approved run lengths"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the campaign structure the schedule runs on economically sound."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10223"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-bjce-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-snf-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Build Production Schedule"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Sequencing Plan Development"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Build the dated production schedule and sequencing plan for the scheduling horizon — assigning campaigns, schedule-level unit commitments, blends, and movements to dates and sequences within the approved plan, the production wheel, and current constraints — producing the schedule that provides the approved basis for refinery execution."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). 'Schedule-level unit commitments' used at the decision owner's direction in place of 'unit operations' to preserve the boundary: the schedule commits what a unit should produce and when, never how it is operated. The scheduling-layer output per SNF/BJCE practice; the operations layer is Refining's per the locked rule. APQC 10223 'Create materials plan' is a WEAK generic candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Create Production Scheduling and Sequencing Plan"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers constructing and refreshing the dated schedule: sequencing within wheel and transition rules, scheduling blends and movements at schedule level, validating feasibility against constraints and outage windows, and publishing the schedule. Excludes unit-operation scheduling and tank and transfer line-ups, owned by Refining per the locked rule; excludes daily instruction updates (CM-1-1-7-1-1); excludes the plan targets themselves (CM-1-1-4).\nIn scope: Sequence campaigns, schedule-level unit commitments, blends, and movements to dates | validate feasibility against constraints and outage windows | publish and refresh the dated schedule | reconcile the schedule to the approved plan\nOut of scope: Unit-operation scheduling and line-ups (Refining) | daily instruction issuance (CM-1-1-7-1-1) | monthly plan targets (CM-1-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/weekly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved monthly plan"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "outage windows"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production wheel and run lengths"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "scheduling master data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published dated production schedule and sequencing plan"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce the dated, feasible schedule that implements the plan."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-4"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10224"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-bjce-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Schedule Exception Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Detect, assess, and resolve deviations from the production schedule — unit upsets, feed or quality surprises, outage changes, and demand shifts — deciding schedule responses, triggering rescheduling, and escalating deviations that break the approved plan to planning."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Refining decides safe operational departures (locked); this node owns the schedule response, not the operational decision. APQC 10224 STRONG with no validator; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Production Schedule Exceptions"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the schedule exception rhythm: monitoring execution feedback against the schedule, assessing deviation impact, deciding and coordinating the schedule response, triggering rescheduling through Create Production Scheduling and Sequencing Plan (CM-1-1-7-2-3), escalating plan-level breaks to Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4), and recording exception causes for performance measurement. The operational decision to depart from the schedule for safety, reliability, or immediate process conditions belongs to Refining under the locked rule; this process manages the schedule consequence of such departures. Manage Production Schedule Exceptions (CM-1-1-7-2-4) supplies recorded production-schedule exception causes and responses that Measure Production Scheduling Performance (CM-1-1-7-2-5) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Monitor execution against schedule and detect deviations | assess deviation impact | decide and coordinate schedule responses | escalate plan-breaking deviations to planning | record exception causes\nOut of scope: Operational departures for safety and reliability (Refining) | rescheduling construction (CM-1-1-7-2-3) | plan revision (CM-1-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "execution feedback and deviation reports"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "impact assessments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "schedule and plan constraints"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "decided schedule responses and escalations with recorded causes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the schedule valid when reality diverges from it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10314"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-bjce-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Schedule Adherence Measurement"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Scheduling Performance Measurement"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Measure and report how well execution followed the issued production schedule and how stable the schedule itself was — adherence, rescheduling frequency, and exception causes at agreed levels — feeding improvements back into scheduling practice and master data."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Horizon set to 'continuous' per the batch 05 precedent (the decision owner's -8-4 edit) — continuous operational monitoring with periodic reporting and review; the controlled vocabulary takes a single value, so the cadence is recorded here. Specific metrics deliberately not named (KPI workstream). APQC 10314 is a WEAK generic candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Measure Production Scheduling Performance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers schedule-performance measurement against the schedule as issued, keeping the contemporaneous-baseline discipline: adherence and stability analysis, exception-cause patterns, and improvement recommendations to scheduling practice, the wheel, and master data. Excludes plan-versus-actual variance explanation, owned by Regional Backcasting (CM-1-1-5) under its locked rule; excludes asset and yield performance ownership, which belongs to Refining with actuals supplied by production accounting; excludes enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream).\nIn scope: Measure adherence to the issued schedule | measure schedule stability and rescheduling frequency | analyze exception-cause patterns | recommend improvements to practice, wheel, and master data\nOut of scope: Plan-versus-actual backcasting (Regional Backcasting, CM-1-1-5) | asset and yield performance ownership (Refining) | enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "actualized production from production accounting"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "issued schedules and revisions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "recorded exception causes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "scheduling performance report with improvement recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish whether the schedule is being followed and whether it is worth following."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10734"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ascm-cscp-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-snf-refps-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Scheduling Interface Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Run the structured coordination between production scheduling and its counterparties — feasibility and deviation feedback to Refinery Planning and Optimization, executability alignment with refinery operations, and outage, turnaround, and maintenance windows from engineering and maintenance — so the schedule and its neighbors stay mutually consistent."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Modeled as the recurring coordination process per the process-concept rule, not a role or an organizational unit. APQC 10734 'Manage treasury operations' is an unrelated false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.2.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage The Interface to Planning, Operations, Engineering & Maintenance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers recurring interface management: scheduled coordination and handoffs, intake of maintenance and turnaround windows into the schedule, executability confirmation with operations, feasibility feedback to planning, and documentation of interface agreements. Excludes the counterparties' own work: plan targets (Refinery Planning and Optimization, CM-1-1-4), maintenance planning and turnaround execution (Refining; refinery maintenance capability to be modeled in R2), and operational execution (Refining). The concept is the recurring coordination process, not an organizational liaison role. Manage The Interface to Planning, Operations, Engineering & Maintenance (CM-1-1-7-2-6) supplies confirmed interface agreements, maintenance windows, and executability constraints that Create Production Scheduling and Sequencing Plan (CM-1-1-7-2-3) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Run scheduled coordination and handoffs | intake outage, turnaround, and maintenance windows | confirm schedule executability with operations | feed feasibility and deviations back to planning\nOut of scope: Plan targets (CM-1-1-4) | maintenance planning and turnaround execution (Refining; refinery maintenance capability to be modeled in R2) | operational execution (Refining)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/weekly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "maintenance and turnaround plans"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operations executability feedback"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "plan updates and constraints"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "consistent interface agreements and window intake into the schedule"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the schedule and its neighboring functions mutually consistent."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20682"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm31-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-emtr-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Energy & Utilities Optimization"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Refinery Energy Economics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Optimize energy, utility, and emissions-allowance economics within refinery planning and scheduling by setting sourcing strategies, economic targets, and allowance-position recommendations that inform the production schedule."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Q2 decision (the decision owner, Option A, narrowed): defined explicitly as the economic and scheduling layer of energy and utilities — the bare label could suggest ownership of utility systems, which belong to Refining. EHS reports (locked rule); the trading function executes; Finance records the accounting treatment of allowances and credits. Whether energy contracting is centralized or delegated to site commercial teams is a follow-up noted in the batch 06 PR. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Energy & Utility Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers planning- and scheduling-level energy economics: evaluating internal generation versus purchased-energy options; incorporating energy, utility, and carbon costs into refinery planning and production scheduling; establishing economic operating targets and constraints for schedule development; maintaining an emissions-allowance and credit position; and preparing recommendations for allowance banking, purchase, or sale. Refining operates and controls utility systems, including boilers, cogeneration, steam, fuel-gas, power-distribution, and energy-recovery equipment. EHS & Government Reporting owns regulatory emissions monitoring, calculation, submission, and reporting under its locked rule. The relevant commercial or trading function owns energy contracting and allowance-trade negotiation and execution. Energy & Utility Management (CM-1-1-7-3) provides energy and utility economic targets and recommendations that inform schedule development by Production Scheduling (CM-1-1-7-2).\nIn scope: Evaluate internal generation versus purchased-energy options | incorporate energy, utility, and carbon costs into planning and scheduling | establish economic operating targets and constraints for schedule development | maintain the emissions-allowance and credit position and prepare banking, purchase, and sale recommendations\nOut of scope: Utility system operation and control (Refining) | regulatory emissions monitoring and reporting (EHS & Government Reporting) | energy contracting and allowance-trade execution (commercial and trading owner) | financial accounting treatment of allowances and credits (Finance)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "energy prices and contract terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production schedule and emissions position"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "utility system capabilities and constraints"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "energy sourcing strategy, economic targets, and allowance-position recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Minimize energy cost and carbon exposure from the planning side, within reliable operations."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10113"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm31-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Energy Make-versus-Buy Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Decide the economically optimal mix of self-generated and externally purchased energy — fuel gas, fuel oil, steam, and power, including cogeneration versus grid supply — for the planning period, within reliability, contractual, and emissions constraints."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). APQC 10113 is an unrelated strategy candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Optimize Internal vs. External Energy Sources"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring sourcing optimization: comparing marginal costs of internal generation against purchases, setting the sourcing plan by utility, respecting contract terms and reliability minimums, and reflecting emissions-allowance cost in the choice. Excludes negotiating energy supply contracts, owned by the commercial owner of energy supply; excludes operating generation and distribution assets, owned by Refining; excludes the sitewide balance targets, owned by Optimize Plant Energy Balance (CM-1-1-7-3-2).\nIn scope: Compare marginal costs of internal generation versus purchase | set the sourcing plan by utility and period | respect contractual and reliability constraints | reflect allowance cost in sourcing choices\nOut of scope: Energy contract negotiation (commercial owner of energy supply) | generation and distribution operation (Refining) | sitewide balance targets (CM-1-1-7-3-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "allowance prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "internal generation costs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "purchased energy prices and terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "reliability requirements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "period energy sourcing plan"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Choose the cheapest reliable energy mix the refinery can run on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12979"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm31-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Energy Balance Target Setting"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Site Energy Balance Planning"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish and maintain planning and scheduling targets for the refinery's sitewide energy balance — such as expected steam, fuel-gas, power, and energy-recovery requirements — so production schedules reflect energy cost, availability, emissions exposure, and operating constraints."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). Rewritten at the decision owner's direction before approval: the original draft's 'set the targets the refinery runs to' and 'minimizing purchased energy, flaring, and losses' read as operational control — this node sets planning and scheduling targets and recommendations only; real-time balancing and dispatch are Refining's. APQC 12979 'Optimize plant units' is a WEAK review-link; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.3.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Optimize Plant Energy Balance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers integrating energy-balance assumptions and economic targets into the production schedule; assessing deviations that materially affect scheduled energy cost or emissions exposure; and recommending schedule-level adjustments. Refining owns real-time utility balancing, equipment dispatch, process control, flaring response, and execution of energy-balance moves. Excludes sourcing mix decisions, owned by Optimize Internal vs. External Energy Sources (CM-1-1-7-3-1); excludes energy-efficiency capital projects, owned by Refining and engineering. Optimize Plant Energy Balance (CM-1-1-7-3-2) provides energy-balance assumptions, economic targets, and recommended schedule adjustments to inform Production Scheduling (CM-1-1-7-2); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Integrate energy-balance assumptions and economic targets into the schedule | assess deviations affecting scheduled energy cost or emissions exposure | recommend schedule-level adjustments | maintain energy-balance planning assumptions\nOut of scope: Real-time utility balancing, dispatch, process control, and flaring response (Refining) | sourcing mix decisions (CM-1-1-7-3-1) | energy-efficiency capital projects (Refining, engineering)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operating constraints"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production schedule"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "site energy balance data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sourcing plan"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "energy-balance planning targets and schedule-level recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Give the schedule sound energy-balance assumptions and targets, and flag deviations that change its economics."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 06 (2026-09-19). The decide-versus-advise pattern applies twice: EHS owns the regulator-facing report (locked rule); trading owns execution; Finance records the accounting treatment. 'Emissions allowances and credits' used throughout because programs use different, not always interchangeable, instruments. Preferred normalized label 'Manage and Support Emissions Trading' (plural) queued for the naming pass per the decision owner. Program mechanics (cap, allowances, trading, banking, true-up) per EPA emissions-trading practice as reference evidence; applicability is jurisdiction- and program-specific. APQC 19562 'Manage support utilities' is a WEAK lexical match; comparative evidence only. Step 3d naming pass — normalization-only mechanical Batch 6 (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Manage and Support Emission Trading' to 'Manage and Support Emissions Trading'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19562"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm31-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-emtr-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Emissions Allowance Position Management"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage and Support Emission Trading"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-7-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage the refinery's emissions-allowance and credit position from the planning side — tracking emissions against allowances by program and period, forecasting surplus or shortfall from the production and energy plans, and supporting allowance purchase, sale, and banking decisions — so compliance obligations are met at the best economic outcome."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.1.7.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage and Support Emissions Trading"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers allowance position management per emissions-trading program mechanics: maintaining the position by program, forecasting surplus and shortfall from schedule and energy plans, preparing the economic case for trades and banking, incorporating allowance prices into scheduling and energy decisions, and supporting compliance true-up. Excludes regulatory emissions monitoring and reporting, owned by EHS & Government Reporting under its locked rule; excludes trade negotiation and execution, owned by the trading function (Supply And Trading where modeled); excludes the financial accounting treatment of allowances and credits, owned by Finance. 'Support' in the label reflects this advisory position: the node prepares and supports the decisions without executing trades or filing reports. Manage and Support Emissions Trading (CM-1-1-7-3-3) provides the emissions-allowance position and forecasts that inform Optimize Internal vs. External Energy Sources (CM-1-1-7-3-1).\nIn scope: Maintain the allowance and credit position by program | forecast surplus and shortfall from plans | prepare the economic case for trades and banking | support compliance true-up and reflect allowance cost in decisions\nOut of scope: Regulatory emissions monitoring and reporting (EHS & Government Reporting) | trade negotiation and execution (trading function) | financial accounting of allowances and credits (Finance) | emissions-reduction capital projects (Refining, engineering)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "allowance holdings and prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "emissions forecasts from production and energy plans"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "program rules and compliance deadlines"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "managed allowance position with trade and banking recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the allowance position known, forecast, and economically managed without owning the trade or the report."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Supply And Trading Includes Processes Such As Managing Supply, Demand And Trading Of Crude Oil And Refined Products. It Involves Trading As Well As Planning & Managing Movements In The Most Efficient Way, Including Primary & Secondary Distribution."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Supply And Trading"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 2
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading management consists of processes performed in the front office such as forecasting, pre-trade analysis, managing counterparty credit and contracts, executing and capturing trades."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading Management"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/assuredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-5-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-5-4-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19569"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Pre-Trade Forecasting & Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The front-office capability to assemble and maintain a forward commercial view of supply, demand, generation, renewables, market conditions, and revenue, and to identify how the asset portfolio can be used commercially within approved plans and constraints."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). Q1 decision (the decision owner, Option A): capability — it comprises distinct forecast-intake, renewable-position forecasting, asset-optimization, and revenue-projection processes that collectively enable a current front-office forward view and commercially optimized asset position; it is not a single sequential process. Same test as the batch 04 Inventory L4. Front-office framing per the approved Trading Management (CM-1-2-1) definition; 'market conditions' made explicit at the decision owner's direction so the forward-curve context is not read as physical volumes only. Q2 boundary recorded on CM-1-2-1-1-4. APQC 19569 'Perform real-time optimization' is process-control software; no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecasting & Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers receiving and consolidating production, demand, and power-generation forecasts from their owning processes; producing the renewables forward view; identifying and valuing commercial use of asset flexibility; and projecting trading revenue, margin, and exposure. This capability consumes forecasts rather than owning their production: the approved demand forecast is owned by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) per the batch 03 decision, and production plans and schedules by Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4) and Refinery Production Planning and Scheduling (CM-1-1-7). Excludes trade execution and capture, owned by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3); excludes setting the regional or refinery plans, owned under the locked Regional Optimization and Refinery Planning and Optimization rules; excludes risk measurement and limits, owned by Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3). Forecasting & Optimization (CM-1-2-1-1) provides the consolidated forward commercial view and asset-opportunity assessments to inform Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Receive and consolidate production, demand, and generation forecasts | develop the renewables forward view | identify and value commercial use of asset flexibility | project trading revenue, margin, and exposure\nOut of scope: Forecast production ownership (CM-1-1-1-1, CM-1-1-4, CM-1-1-7) | trade execution and capture (CM-1-2-1-3) | regional and refinery plan setting (locked rules) | risk measurement and limits (CM-1-2-2-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/capability"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "generation forecasts"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market prices and forward curves"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production plans and schedules"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published demand forecast"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current trading forward view and asset-optimization recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep trading running on a current forward commercial view and an identified, valued set of asset opportunities."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12901"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Production Forecast Intake"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Receive and incorporate the refinery production plans and schedules into the trading forward view — validating completeness, translating volumes into tradable supply by product, location, and period, and refreshing the view as plans and schedules change."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). A consume-not-produce node, per the precedent batch 02 recorded on its sibling CM-1-2-1-1-2. APQC 12901 'Forecast equity crude production' is a WEAK review-link; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Receive Production Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the intake side only: receiving the approved production plan and current schedule from Refinery Planning and Optimization (CM-1-1-4) and Refinery Production Planning and Scheduling (CM-1-1-7), reconciling product, location, and period granularity to what the trading books use, and flagging material changes to traders. It consumes these plans and does not produce or alter them — their owners hold that right. Excludes the demand-side intake, owned by Receive Demand Forecast (CM-1-2-1-1-2).\nIn scope: Receive the approved plan and current schedule | validate completeness and version | translate volumes to tradable supply granularity | flag material changes to trading\nOut of scope: Producing or altering the plan or schedule (CM-1-1-4, CM-1-1-7) | demand forecast intake (CM-1-2-1-1-2) | trading decisions on the supply (Trade Capture, strategy processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved production plan"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current production schedule"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "product and location mappings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production supply view refreshed in the trading forward view"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the trading view current with what the refinery is currently planned and scheduled to produce."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20634"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Demand Forecast Intake"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Receive the published demand forecast and incorporate it into the trading forward view — validating the version, translating product, market, and period detail into the granularity trading uses, and refreshing trading assumptions when a new version publishes."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). Batch 02 already cited this node as 'the existing precedent for a consume-not-produce node'; authored to honor that reading and the batch 03 Q2 decision (Produce Demand Forecast owns the approved forecast). APQC 20634 scored STRONG but is IT-service demand; false lexical match, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Receive Demand Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the intake of the approved commercial planning forecast, which is owned by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) and released by Publish Forecast and Generate Component Level Forecast Plan (CM-1-1-1-1-4) per the batch 03 decision — this node consumes the published version and must not claim its production. Excludes Supply And Trading's own operational refined-product demand forecasting (Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand, CM-1-2-6-2-3), which serves the supply-chain-management context under the batch 03 constraint. Excludes adjusting or overriding the forecast — trading views that differ from the published forecast are trading positions, not forecast revisions.\nIn scope: Receive and validate the published forecast version | translate to trading granularity | refresh trading assumptions on new versions | flag material forecast changes to trading\nOut of scope: Forecast production and ownership (CM-1-1-1-1) | operational refined-product demand forecasting (CM-1-2-6-2-3) | forecast adjustment or override (trading positions are not forecast revisions)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published versioned demand forecast"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "trading granularity mappings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "demand assumptions refreshed in the trading forward view"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep trading assumptions aligned to the current published demand forecast."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10129"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-rfs-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Renewables Position Forecasting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and maintain a forward view of renewable-fuel volumes, renewable-energy output or procurement, compliance obligations, and associated program-specific environmental attributes or credits — such as Renewable Identification Numbers where applicable — so commercial, trading, and compliance stakeholders can anticipate expected shortfalls, surpluses, and deadlines."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction to treat environmental instruments as program-specific: RINs (RFS-type fuel programs) and RECs (renewable power programs) arise under different program architectures with different eligibility, lifecycle, compliance, and market rules and are not interchangeable. Which instruments are genuinely in scope (RINs, RECs, low-carbon fuel credits, allowances, guarantees of origin) is a follow-up noted in the batch 07 PR. EPA RFS practice is US-specific reference evidence for RVO and RIN mechanics only. APQC 10129 is an unrelated sales-forecast candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Renewables"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers forecasting renewable-fuel production, blending, acquisition, and obligation exposure; expected generation, acquisition, retirement, or need for program-specific environmental attributes and credits; and the resulting forward long and short positions by program and compliance period. Excludes regulatory monitoring, filing, attestation, and submission, owned by EHS & Government Reporting under its locked rule; excludes execution of credit purchases, sales, transfers, or retirements, owned by the trading processes; excludes accounting actualization of issued, acquired, sold, retired, or expired instruments, owned by Perform RINs/REC Actualization (CM-1-2-3-1-7). Program applicability is jurisdiction-specific. Forecast Renewables (CM-1-2-1-1-3) provides renewables forward positions, expected shortfalls, surpluses, and obligation forecasts to inform Perform Asset Optimization (CM-1-2-1-1-4); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Forecast renewable-fuel volumes and obligation exposure | forecast generation, acquisition, retirement, and need for program-specific attributes and credits | maintain forward long and short positions by program and compliance period | flag expected shortfalls, surpluses, and deadlines\nOut of scope: Regulatory monitoring, filing, attestation, and submission (EHS & Government Reporting) | credit purchase, sale, transfer, and retirement execution (trading processes) | credit actualization (CM-1-2-3-1-7)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "instrument holdings and prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "production and blending plans"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "program obligations and rules"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "forward renewables position by program and compliance period"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Know the renewables obligation and instrument position before the deadline does."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19253"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Asset-Backed Trading Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assess and optimize the commercial use of approved asset flexibility — including storage, transportation and terminal capacity, supply commitments, exchanges, and generation availability — against market conditions, identifying and valuing opportunities and providing recommendations to approved trading strategies within established plans and constraints."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). Q2 decision (the decision owner, Option A, narrowed): approved plans define the base; this process identifies, values, and recommends commercial use of the flexibility those plans leave open — it does not initiate strategies (Trading Strategy Management owns the strategy lifecycle) and does not own dispatch ('generation availability', not dispatch, at the decision owner's direction). Whether the desk may submit pre-authorized strategy-linked trade orders, rather than only recommend, is a follow-up to be modeled through the future Trade Capture relationship, noted in the batch 07 PR. APQC 19253 'Perform asset maintenance' scored STRONG but is maintenance; false lexical match, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform Asset Optimization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers evaluating storage economics and time spreads; capacity utilization, release, and throughput opportunities; exchange and location-arbitrage opportunities; and the commercial value of generation availability. It identifies and quantifies trading opportunities within approved regional, refinery, and scheduling plans. Excludes changing physical plans, owned under the locked Regional Optimization and Refinery Planning and Optimization rules; excludes operating or dispatching assets, owned by Refining, Midstream, and the relevant system operators; excludes defining or approving trading strategies, owned by Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4); excludes negotiating, executing, capturing, or settling trades, owned by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) and the Settlements cluster; excludes risk-limit setting and risk measurement, owned by Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3). Perform Asset Optimization (CM-1-2-1-1-4) provides asset-optimization analysis and recommendations that inform Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4); strategy decisions remain with Trading Strategy Management.\nIn scope: Evaluate storage, capacity, exchange, and generation-availability economics against the market | identify and quantify opportunities within approved plans | value opportunities and their sensitivities | provide recommendations to approved trading strategies\nOut of scope: Physical plan changes (Regional Optimization, Refinery Planning and Optimization — locked) | asset operation and dispatch (Refining, Midstream, system operators) | trading strategy definition and approval (CM-1-2-1-4) | trade negotiation, execution, capture, and settlement (CM-1-2-1-3, Settlements) | risk-limit setting and risk measurement (CM-1-2-2-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved plans"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "asset capacities and constraints"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "forward view of supply, demand, and generation"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market prices and forward curves"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "valued asset-optimization opportunities and recommendations to approved strategies"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify and value the market opportunities the asset portfolio's approved flexibility offers."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10129"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forward Trading Economics Outlook"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading Revenue Projection"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Project the trading organization's expected economics — projected trading revenue, gross margin, and economic exposure from current positions, planned flows, the forward view, and market prices — so management and strategy decisions rest on a current forward-looking outlook."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). Reframed at the decision owner's direction as revenue, gross margin, and economic exposure — in a trading environment expected value, exposure, and scenario sensitivity matter alongside accounting-defined revenue; Finance's ownership of official financial forecasting and governed P&L is unchanged. Whether optionality valuation and mark-to-market scenario impact are in scope, or only expected physical-trading margin, is a follow-up noted in the batch 07 PR. APQC 10129 is an unrelated sales-forecast candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Revenue"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the front-office economic projection: projected revenue, gross margin, and exposure by book, strategy, and period, refreshed on market and position changes, with sensitivity to price scenarios. Excludes financial forecasting, budgeting, and reporting ownership, which sit with Finance under the locked rule; excludes official, controlled position and realized/unrealized P&L reporting, owned by Perform Position & P&L Analysis (CM-1-2-2-3-9) and the Accounting cluster (CM-1-2-4-2) — this is a forward-looking planning projection, not the governed result.\nIn scope: Project revenue, gross margin, and exposure by book, strategy, and period | refresh projections on market and position changes | run price-scenario sensitivities | supply the economic outlook to management and strategy\nOut of scope: Financial forecasting and budgeting (Finance) | official, controlled position and realized/unrealized P&L reporting (CM-1-2-2-3-9, CM-1-2-4-2) | trading decisions themselves (strategy and capture processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/monthly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current positions and planned flows"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "forward view and market prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "price scenarios"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "projected trading revenue, gross margin, and exposure outlook"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Provide management and strategy owners with a current forward-looking view of projected trading revenue, gross margin, and economic exposure."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10129"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Generation Forecast Intake"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Receive and incorporate power generation forecasts — from company cogeneration and any contracted or merchant generation — into the trading forward view, validating them and translating expected generation into tradable positions by period."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). Third of the three consume-not-produce intake siblings; dispatch and grid-operations exclusion worded per the decision owner's batch 07 edit for precision. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.1.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Receive Power Generation Forecast"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the intake side only: generation forecasts are produced by the asset operators (Refining for cogeneration) or external suppliers; this node consumes them into the forward view, reconciles period granularity, and flags material changes. Excludes producing generation forecasts (asset operators and suppliers); excludes physical generation dispatch and grid/system operations, owned by the asset operators and the relevant system authorities; excludes power trade execution and settlement, owned by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) and the Settlements cluster. Receive Power Generation Forecast (CM-1-2-1-1-6) supplies validated generation forecasts translated into tradable positions by period that Perform Asset Optimization (CM-1-2-1-1-4) consumes when valuing generation availability.\nIn scope: Receive and validate generation forecasts | translate expected generation to tradable positions by period | refresh the forward view on forecast changes | flag material generation changes to trading\nOut of scope: Generation forecast production (asset operators, suppliers) | physical generation dispatch and grid/system operations (asset operators, system authorities) | power trade execution and settlement (CM-1-2-1-3, Settlements)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cogeneration and contracted generation forecasts"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "period granularity mappings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "generation positions refreshed in the trading forward view"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Keep the trading view current with expected power generation."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20682"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty & Contract Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer trading counterparties and commercial agreements through their lifecycle — onboarding and maintaining counterparty records; establishing, maintaining, terminating, and novating master agreements, standing agreements, and relevant transaction frameworks; managing specialized agreement types; and monitoring contractual obligations — so trading occurs with authorized counterparties under current, governed terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Q1 decision (the decision owner, Option A): process — lifecycle stages applied to two entity kinds plus type variants and control activities, per the batch 08 variant test. This taxonomy locates the commercial lifecycle-administration process under Trading Management; actual execution may involve Trading, Credit Risk, Regulatory & Compliance, Legal, Finance Operations, or Shared Services according to the enterprise operating model. The negotiate, administer, capture, use/actualize/settle pattern from batch 08 is a taxonomy heuristic, not a universal sequential lifecycle: some agreements are frameworks rather than tradable deals, some deals execute under existing agreements, and some contractual rights are used without a separately captured transaction. APQC 20682 is an unrelated IT candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Contract Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the controlled lifecycle administration of trading counterparties (create, maintain, terminate or novate) and trading agreements (create, maintain, terminate or novate), the specialized administration of lease, carrier, and storage contracts, the counterparty and agreement consequences of merger-and-acquisition events, and contract monitoring. Accommodates physical contracts, master agreements such as ISDA-type frameworks, transaction confirmations governed by a master agreement, capacity and lease arrangements, and spot transactions governed by standard terms or market rules rather than a bespoke contract record. Excludes legal drafting, legal review, and legal-risk management, owned by Legal & Corporate Communications under its locked rule; excludes credit reviews, limits, and collateral, owned by Credit Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-1); excludes commercial negotiation of agreements where a negotiating owner exists (for example Negotiate Storage / Throughput Agreements, CM-1-2-7-1-3); excludes deal capture (Trade Capture, CM-1-2-1-3) and deal-level confirmation (CM-1-2-2-2). When the trade is confirmed under a governing agreement administered by the source, Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2) supplies current governing master-agreement terms and applicable confirmation provisions that Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Onboard, maintain, and terminate or novate counterparties | establish, maintain, and terminate or novate agreements and master agreements | administer lease, carrier, and storage contract specializations | handle M&A consequences for counterparties and agreements | monitor contractual obligations\nOut of scope: Legal services and legal-risk management (Legal & Corporate Communications) | credit reviews, limits, and collateral (CM-1-2-2-1) | agreement negotiation where separately owned (CM-1-2-7-1) | deal capture and confirmation (CM-1-2-1-3, CM-1-2-2-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "contract obligations and calendars"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "corporate event notices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty applications and due-diligence results"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "negotiated agreement terms"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed counterparty and agreement records through their lifecycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading occurs with authorized counterparties under current, governed terms."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10147"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty Onboarding"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate onboarding of a prospective trading counterparty by collecting required legal-entity, tax, settlement, and commercial documentation; initiating and recording required compliance, sanctions/KYC, legal, and credit clearances through their accountable owners; and creating the authorized counterparty and settlement records once required approvals are complete."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction to distinguish process coordination from independent verification: this process validates completeness and reconciles data; Compliance, Legal, and Credit retain independent decision rights. Which function operationally performs onboarding (Trading, middle office, Legal Operations, Compliance, Shared Services, or an MDM team) is a follow-up noted in the batch 09 PR. Trading counterparty records here versus commercial customer master data at CM-1-3-7-1 is the record boundary. APQC 10147 is an unrelated budget candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Create New Counterparty"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers counterparty onboarding coordination: documentation collection and completeness validation, initiation and tracking of required clearances through their owning processes, setup of the counterparty record with settlement instructions and hierarchy links, and activation for trading once approvals are complete. Credit reviews and limits are owned by Perform Counterparty Credit Reviews (CM-1-2-2-1-1) and Manage Credit Limits (CM-1-2-2-1-2); compliance policy by Regulatory & Compliance (CM-1-2-4-3); legal review by Legal & Corporate Communications. Excludes independent KYC/sanctions determination, beneficial-owner due diligence, and regulatory-risk acceptance, which sit with the appropriate Regulatory & Compliance or Legal process when its detailed taxonomy is authored. Excludes commercial customer master data, owned by Manage Commercial Master Data Stewardship under Order Management (CM-1-3-7-1) — trading counterparty records live here.\nIn scope: Collect and validate completeness of counterparty documentation | initiate and record required clearances through their accountable owners | create the counterparty record and settlement details once approvals complete | activate the counterparty for trading\nOut of scope: Independent KYC/sanctions determination, beneficial-owner due diligence, and regulatory-risk acceptance (Regulatory & Compliance / Legal) | credit reviews and limit setting (CM-1-2-2-1-1, CM-1-2-2-1-2) | legal review (Legal & Corporate Communications) | commercial customer master data (CM-1-3-7-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "clearance outcomes from accountable owners"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty applications and legal documentation"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "settlement instructions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "activated counterparty records with recorded clearances"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No trading with an unverified or incompletely cleared counterparty."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/requires": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-10",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12944"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm32-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Storage Contract Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer storage and throughput contracts through their life — recorded capacity, injection and withdrawal rights, fee structures, amendments, and renewals — so storage deals, inventory administration, and settlement operate against current, correct contract terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). The storage split (negotiate, administer, capture, use, settle) is stated on all participating nodes; the conditional-capture wording was added at the decision owner's direction — not every storage contract produces a distinct captured deal, and where none exists the contract record here is the governed source of rights and charges. APQC 12944 is the third-party-bulk-storage candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.10"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Storage Contract"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the contract-administration position in the storage split: negotiation is owned by Negotiate Storage / Throughput Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-3); where storage capacity is commercially traded, allocated, acquired, released, or represented as a distinct transaction it is captured by Capture Storage Deals (CM-1-2-1-3-5), and otherwise the contract record maintained here remains the governed source for contractual storage rights and charges; company stock in the facilities is administered by Manage Third Party Storage (CM-1-1-3-7-11); storage charges settle at Settle Terminal/Storage (CM-1-2-4-1-14). This node maintains the contract record itself — terms, rights, fees, versions, renewals — and keeps the others supplied with current terms.\nIn scope: Maintain storage and throughput contract records, rights, and fees | administer amendments and renewals | keep terms synchronized with deals, inventory administration, and settlement | track expiries and renewal windows\nOut of scope: Negotiation (CM-1-2-7-1-3) | capacity deal capture where a distinct transaction exists (CM-1-2-1-3-5) | third-party storage inventory administration (CM-1-1-3-7-11) | storage settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "amendment requests"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "deal and settlement feedback"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "negotiated storage terms"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current storage contract records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Storage rights and fees in the systems match the contract in force."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-11",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10291"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Contract Obligation Monitoring"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Monitor active agreements against their terms — tracking obligations, commitments, expiries, renewal windows, and utilization against contracted volumes and service levels — surfacing issues to the responsible owners before they become breaches or lapses."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Monitoring surfaces; the lifecycle siblings act — the same detect-versus-decide split established in batch 04. APQC 10291 comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.11"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Monitor Contracts"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers contract-obligation monitoring across the portfolio: obligation and commitment tracking, expiry and renewal-window alerting, utilization against contracted volumes, and escalation of at-risk items to the contract, commercial, or legal owner. Excludes trading compliance monitoring, owned by Regulatory & Compliance (Monitor External Trading Compliance, CM-1-2-4-3-2; Monitor Internal Trading Compliance, CM-1-2-4-3-3); excludes dispute handling (CM-1-2-2-2-5, CM-1-2-4-1-17); excludes acting on the findings — amendments and renewals run through Manage Existing Contract (CM-1-2-1-2-6). When Monitor Contracts (CM-1-2-1-2-11) identifies an expiry, renewal window, or obligation finding that requires consideration of an amendment, extension, or renewal, it refers the finding to Manage Existing Contract (CM-1-2-1-2-6) for assessment and the applicable approval process.\nIn scope: Track obligations, commitments, and service levels against terms | alert on expiries and renewal windows | monitor utilization against contracted volumes | escalate at-risk items to responsible owners\nOut of scope: Trading compliance monitoring (CM-1-2-4-3-2, CM-1-2-4-3-3) | dispute handling (CM-1-2-2-2-5, CM-1-2-4-1-17) | amendments and renewals (CM-1-2-1-2-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "commitment schedules"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "contract terms and calendars"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "utilization and delivery data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "monitored obligations with escalated at-risk items"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No agreement lapses, breaches, or under-uses unnoticed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty Record Maintenance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Maintain active counterparty records through their life — processing changes to legal identity, ownership, settlement details, and documentation, keeping records synchronized with credit and compliance status, and periodically reconfirming record accuracy."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). APQC 11743 is an unrelated routing candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Existing Counterparty"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers ongoing counterparty record maintenance: change processing, periodic reconfirmation, documentation refresh, and synchronization with credit and compliance outcomes owned by their processes. Excludes the credit and compliance judgments themselves (CM-1-2-2-1, CM-1-2-4-3); excludes termination and novation, owned by Terminate/Novate Counterparty (CM-1-2-1-2-3); excludes M&A-driven changes, owned by Manage M&A Activity (CM-1-2-1-2-4). Manage Existing Counterparty (CM-1-2-1-2-2) maintains the current counterparty identity, settlement-detail, and documentation base that Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) needs to operate its defined process path.\nIn scope: Process counterparty record changes | refresh documentation periodically | synchronize records with credit and compliance status | reconfirm record accuracy on a defined cadence\nOut of scope: Credit and compliance judgments (CM-1-2-2-1, CM-1-2-4-3) | termination and novation (CM-1-2-1-2-3) | M&A-driven changes (CM-1-2-1-2-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "change notices and documentation"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "credit and compliance status updates"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current, reconfirmed counterparty records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty records stay true to the counterparty."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10208"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty Offboarding & Novation Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate the administrative counterparty offboarding or transfer — confirming that affected positions, agreements, collateral, payment instructions, and reporting responsibilities have been closed, settled, transferred, or queued for legally effective novation — and deactivate or transition counterparty records with preserved history."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction: 'legally effective novation' names the legal event (Legal owns its documents); 'administrative transfer' names the operational record change this process owns — the two are never conflated. Novation terminology per the CFTC glossary; master-agreement close-out mechanics per ISDA documentation as reference evidence for applicable OTC frameworks. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Terminate/Novate Counterparty"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers controlled exit and transfer coordination: verifying no unresolved positions, obligations, disputes, or collateral remain or are queued for legally effective novation; coordinating consents, effective dates, and counterparty communication; and executing the administrative record transfer or deactivation with audit history. The legally effective novation is the legal event, executed through documents owned by Legal & Corporate Communications; this process performs the administrative transfer of records once that event is effective. Collateral release is owned by Manage Collateral (CM-1-2-2-1-3); settlement of remaining obligations by the Settlements cluster (CM-1-2-4-1).\nIn scope: Verify positions, agreements, collateral, and reporting responsibilities are closed, settled, transferred, or queued for legally effective novation | coordinate consents, effective dates, and communication | execute the administrative transfer or deactivation | preserve record history\nOut of scope: Legal execution of novation and termination documents (Legal & Corporate Communications) | collateral release (CM-1-2-2-1-3) | settlement of remaining obligations (CM-1-2-4-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "master agreement terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "novation consents and effective dates"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "open position and obligation reports"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cleanly transferred or deactivated counterparty records with preserved history"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty exits leave nothing open and nothing lost."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/requires": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-4"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20729"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "M&A Counterparty & Contract Transition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer the counterparty, agreement, trade-record, and obligation consequences of merger, acquisition, divestiture, restructuring, or legal-entity change events affecting either a trading counterparty or the company's own trading entities — coordinating, recording, and operationalizing the resulting novations, assignments, renamings, and record transfers once required legal documentation and approvals are complete."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Q2 decision (the decision owner, Option A): both directions — counterparty-side and company-side corporate events — because both land as the same administrative novation, assignment, and transfer work; restructuring and legal-entity changes included at the decision owner's direction. The process coordinates, records, and operationalizes; it never executes legal documents. The Step 3b human gate already confirmed the mergers-and-acquisitions reading (APQC 20729 rejected as a false token match); authored consistent with that rejection."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage M&A Activity"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers event-driven M&A consequence administration in both directions: identifying affected counterparties, agreements, and open positions when a corporate event occurs; planning and coordinating the resulting legal-entity renames and identifier changes, counterparty-master updates, assignments, consent requests, novations, trade and portfolio transfers, and changes to payment, settlement, collateral, tax, and reporting entities; and verifying continuity of obligations throughout. Excludes corporate-development strategy, target identification, due diligence, valuation, transaction negotiation, financing, regulatory merger approval, and legal execution of transaction or novation documents; credit reassessment of surviving entities is owned by Credit Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-1); updates to delegated authority follow Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3-2). When assessment of a corporate event under Manage M&A Activity (CM-1-2-1-2-4) results in an authorized instruction to offboard a counterparty or process a change of counterparty through the applicable transfer or novation procedure, that instruction invokes Terminate/Novate Counterparty (CM-1-2-1-2-3). A corporate event alone does not trigger termination or novation; applicable legal, credit, and consent requirements remain in force. When assessment of a corporate event under Manage M&A Activity (CM-1-2-1-2-4) results in an authorized instruction to terminate or novate an affected agreement, that instruction invokes Terminate/Novate Contract (CM-1-2-1-2-7). A corporate event alone does not trigger the action; contractual rights, approvals, and required consents remain applicable.\nIn scope: Identify counterparties, agreements, and positions affected by a corporate event | plan and coordinate renames, assignments, novations, and transfers | operationalize record changes once legal documentation and approvals are complete | verify continuity of obligations, collateral, and reporting\nOut of scope: Corporate-development strategy, diligence, valuation, negotiation, financing, and regulatory merger approval (outside the taxonomy) | legal execution of transaction and novation documents (Legal & Corporate Communications) | credit reassessment (CM-1-2-2-1) | delegated-authority updates (CM-1-2-2-3-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/rejected"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "affected counterparty and agreement inventories"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "completed legal documentation"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "corporate event notices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "novation and assignment consents"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "completed administrative transitions with valid records and continuous obligations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Corporate events never leave a trade, agreement, or obligation pointing at the wrong entity."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10147"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Contract Establishment"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish new trading agreements in the contract record — capturing negotiated terms, verifying required approvals and legal review are complete, linking the agreement to its counterparty and settlement basis, and activating it — so transactions governed by the agreement can be captured, confirmed, actualized, and settled against controlled terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Purpose reworded at the decision owner's direction to avoid an absolute gate: agreements required under enterprise policy must be recorded and approved before dependent transactions are processed, but spot-market, exchange-traded, and standing-terms transactions may be governed by standard terms or market rules rather than a bespoke contract record. Master-agreement structure (agreement, schedule, confirmations, credit support) per ISDA documentation as reference evidence for applicable OTC frameworks. APQC 10147 is an unrelated budget candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Create New Contract"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers agreement establishment: recording master agreements (such as ISDA-type frameworks), general terms and conditions, and standing commercial contracts; verifying legal review and required approvals occurred with their owners; linking agreements to counterparty records; and activating them for use. Negotiation and legal drafting are owned by the commercial negotiating owner and Legal & Corporate Communications; deal-level transactions under an agreement are captured by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) and confirmed by Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2); pre-trade authorization of individual transactions is owned by Obtain Trade Approval (CM-1-2-1-3-2), not by contract activation.\nIn scope: Record negotiated agreement and master agreement terms | verify legal review and approvals are complete | link agreements to counterparties and settlement basis | activate agreements for use\nOut of scope: Commercial negotiation (negotiating owner) | legal drafting and review (Legal & Corporate Communications) | deal capture under the agreement (CM-1-2-1-3) | pre-trade authorization of transactions (CM-1-2-1-3-2) | deal confirmation (CM-1-2-2-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "legal review outcomes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "negotiated terms"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "activated, governed agreement records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Ensure agreements required for trading are recorded, approved, current, and linked to the appropriate counterparty before dependent transactions are captured or processed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Contract Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Maintain active agreements through their life — processing approved amendments, extensions, and renewals, keeping recorded terms synchronized with what the parties have agreed, and managing agreement documentation and versions — so the contract record always reflects the operative agreement."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). The administers-approved-changes sentence added at the decision owner's direction: record updates follow agreement and approval; this process never independently changes terms. APQC 11743 is an unrelated routing candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Existing Contract"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers ongoing agreement administration: amendment and renewal processing with required approvals, version and document control, term synchronization with trading and settlement systems, and administration of agreement-linked references. This process administers approved commercial and legal changes; it does not negotiate terms, draft legal amendments, or determine legal enforceability — the record is updated after commercial and legal agreement and approval, never independently. Excludes renegotiation of commercial terms (negotiating owner, with Legal & Corporate Communications for legal changes); excludes termination and novation (CM-1-2-1-2-7); excludes obligation monitoring (Monitor Contracts, CM-1-2-1-2-11).\nIn scope: Process approved amendments, extensions, and renewals | control agreement versions and documents | synchronize recorded terms with trading and settlement systems | administer agreement-linked references\nOut of scope: Commercial renegotiation (negotiating owner) | legal drafting and enforceability determination (Legal & Corporate Communications) | termination and novation (CM-1-2-1-2-7) | obligation monitoring (CM-1-2-1-2-11)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "agreed term changes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approval outcomes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved amendment and renewal requests"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-11"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-7"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current, version-controlled agreement records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The contract record always reflects the operative agreement."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-11"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-7",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10208"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Contract Termination & Novation Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "End or transfer an agreement in a controlled way — confirming obligations under it are fulfilled, settled, or queued for legally effective novation, executing the administrative termination or transfer steps, and closing the agreement record with its history preserved."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). Same administrative-versus-legally-effective distinction as CM-1-2-1-2-3. Close-out mechanics per ISDA documentation as reference evidence for applicable OTC frameworks; novation per the CFTC glossary. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Terminate/Novate Contract"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers controlled agreement exit: verifying open deals, deliveries, and payments under the agreement are complete or queued for legally effective novation, coordinating effective dates and consents, applying master-agreement close-out mechanics where relevant, and archiving the record. Legal execution of termination and novation documents is owned by Legal & Corporate Communications; close-out settlement amounts by the Settlements cluster (CM-1-2-4-1); disputes follow their dispute processes (CM-1-2-2-2-5, CM-1-2-4-1-17).\nIn scope: Verify obligations are fulfilled, settled, or queued for legally effective novation | coordinate consents and effective dates | execute administrative termination or transfer | archive the agreement record with history\nOut of scope: Legal document execution (Legal & Corporate Communications) | close-out settlement (CM-1-2-4-1) | dispute resolution (CM-1-2-2-2-5, CM-1-2-4-1-17)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "consents and effective dates"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "master agreement terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "open obligation reports"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cleanly terminated or transferred agreement records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreements end clean or transfer whole."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-4"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-8",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Lease Purchase Contract Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer crude and condensate lease purchase contracts — first-purchase arrangements at the lease or wellhead — through their life: recorded terms, price and deduction bases, division-of-interest references, amendments, and renewals, so lease purchases actualize and settle against current, correct contract terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). 'Lease' read in the crude-marketing sense — first-purchase contracts at the lease or wellhead — corroborated by the Perform Lease Actualization and Settle First Purchaser/Leases siblings; not real-estate or equipment leasing. Scope caveat added at the decision owner's direction; whether lease-purchase activity is genuinely in scope for the downstream organization or inherited from an integrated enterprise taxonomy is a follow-up noted in the batch 09 PR. APQC 11743 is an unrelated routing candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.8"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Lease Contract"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the contract-administration side of lease purchasing: maintaining lease contract records with their pricing, gravity and quality adjustment, deduction, and interest-distribution references; processing amendments and renewals; and keeping terms synchronized with actualization and settlement. Included only where the downstream Supply & Trading organization purchases crude or condensate at the lease/wellhead or administers associated first-purchaser arrangements; exploration and production leasehold management, land administration, and upstream royalty accounting remain outside scope. Lease volume actualization is owned by Perform Lease Actualization (CM-1-2-3-1-6); first-purchaser settlement by Settle First Purchaser/Leases (CM-1-2-4-1-6); royalty and interest payment execution by Manage Marketing Interests & Royalty Payments (CM-1-2-4-2-3).\nIn scope: Maintain lease purchase contract records and pricing bases | administer amendments and renewals | keep division-of-interest and deduction references current | synchronize terms with actualization and settlement\nOut of scope: Exploration and production leasehold management, land administration, and upstream royalty accounting (outside scope) | lease volume actualization (CM-1-2-3-1-6) | first-purchaser settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-6) | royalty and interest payments (CM-1-2-4-2-3) | negotiation of lease purchase terms (commercial owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "amendment requests"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "division-of-interest data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "lease contract terms and pricing bases"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current lease purchase contract records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Lease purchases settle against the terms actually in force."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-9",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10291"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-doe-rppl-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Carrier Contract Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer contracts with pipeline, marine, rail, and truck carriers through their life — recorded rates, capacity commitments, service terms, amendments, and renewals — so transportation deals, nominations, and freight settlement operate against current, correct carrier terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 09 (2026-09-19). The carrier-versus-product-transport rule was sharpened at the decision owner's direction: supply/trading-movement carrier agreements here; customer-facing delivery agreements at CM-1-2-7-1-2 — a decision-log-worthy rule that prevents duplication by transport mode alone. Confirming the intended boundary with the products branch is a follow-up noted in the batch 09 PR. APQC 10291 'Manage contracts' scored 0.8 STRONG with no validator; supporting comparative evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.2.9"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Carrier Contracts"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the contract-administration side of carrier relationships across modes: maintaining carrier contract records, rate and accessorial references, and commitment terms; processing amendments and renewals; and keeping terms synchronized with capacity deals and settlement. Boundary rule with the products branch: carrier capacity, tariff, freight-rate, charter, pipeline, railcar, trucking, and network-access agreements that support supply and trading movements are administered here; customer-facing and commercial product-delivery agreements, including delivery terms linked to product sale and marketing arrangements, belong to Manage Product Transport Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-2). Transportation capacity deals are captured by Capture Transportation Deals (CM-1-2-1-3-9); nominations by Plan & Execute Nominations (CM-1-1-3-6-1); mode-specific settlement by the Settlements cluster; demurrage by Demurrage Management (CM-1-2-4-4).\nIn scope: Maintain carrier contract records, rates, and commitments by mode | administer amendments and renewals | keep terms synchronized with deals and settlement | track carrier contract expiries and renewal windows\nOut of scope: Customer-facing product-delivery agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-2) | transportation deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-9) | nominations and capacity use (CM-1-1-3-6-1) | freight settlement and demurrage (CM-1-2-4-1, CM-1-2-4-4) | physical movement execution (Midstream, distribution operator, carrier)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "amendment requests"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "carrier contract terms and rates"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "deal and settlement feedback"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current carrier contract records by mode"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Freight moves and settles against the carrier terms actually in force."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/14095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Deal Capture"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trade Entry & Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform the controlled pre-trade analysis, authorization, and post-execution recording of trades in the trading system — capturing complete commercial, operational, and regulatory terms by deal type and submitting required creation-data reports — so authorized transactions are available to confirmation, risk, actualization, settlement, and accounting processes."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Q1 decision (the decision owner, Option A): process — the children form a per-transaction lifecycle (analyze, authorize, capture by deal type, report) with the eight capture nodes as instrument-specific variants of one controlled deal-entry activity; the Produce Demand Forecast process precedent applies, not the batch 04 capability test. Reworded at the decision owner's direction to distinguish trade execution from trade capture: this process controls what happens before, at, and immediately after execution and records the trade; it does not execute it. Whether the enterprise's system of record supports a single deal record or a governed golden-deal model across systems is a follow-up noted in the batch 08 PR. APQC 14095 'Document trade' is a WEAK international-trade candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trade Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the per-transaction lifecycle: analyzing prospective deals, obtaining approval within the delegation of authority, capturing executed physical, exchange, storage, environmental, financial, structured, transportation, and transmission deals after execution, and reporting creation data to swap data repositories where an applicable regime requires it. Trading strategies and approved asset-optimization opportunities inform prospective transactions; the authorized trader or delegated execution role executes a transaction only after required pre-trade controls and approvals have been satisfied — capture is the controlled record-creation activity, not the act of purchasing or selling. Excludes trade confirmation and matching with counterparties, owned by Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2); excludes risk measurement and limits (Market Risk Management, CM-1-2-2-3); excludes actualization (CM-1-2-3-1) and settlement (CM-1-2-4-1); excludes counterparty and contract lifecycle administration (Contract Management, CM-1-2-1-2).\nIn scope: Analyze prospective deals before execution | obtain trade approval within the delegation of authority | capture executed deals by type with full commercial, operational, and regulatory terms | report creation data where an applicable regime requires it\nOut of scope: Trade execution as an act of purchasing or selling (authorized trader or delegated execution role) | strategy definition (CM-1-2-1-4, CM-1-2-1-1-4) | confirmation and matching (CM-1-2-2-2) | risk measurement and limits (CM-1-2-2-3) | actualization and settlement (CM-1-2-3-1, CM-1-2-4-1) | counterparty and contract administration (CM-1-2-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-5"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-5-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "applicable reporting rules"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved strategies and recommendations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "delegation of authority"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed transaction terms"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "authorized, complete, reported deal records available to downstream processes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Get every executed trade authorized, completely recorded, and reported where required, once and correctly."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20102"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Pre-Deal Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evaluate a prospective trade before execution — its economics, strategy fit, credit and limit headroom, operational feasibility where applicable, and regulatory treatment — so the trader and approver see the deal's value and consequences before committing the company."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Pre-check versus formal clearance distinction added at the decision owner's direction: analysis informs, it never clears an exception. Operational feasibility applies to physical, capacity, transportation, storage, and structured trades — not asserted for every financial derivative. Closes the batch 07 follow-up loop: asset-optimization recommendations enter execution through this analysis and the approval sibling. APQC 20102 is an unrelated claims candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Pre-Trade Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers per-deal analysis ahead of execution: deal economics and sensitivities, fit with the approved strategy, pre-checks against credit exposure and market-risk limit headroom, operational feasibility for physical, capacity, transportation, storage, and structured trades where applicable, and identification of regulatory treatment including reportability. Pre-trade analysis may evaluate available credit exposure and risk-limit headroom, but it does not set limits or independently authorize an override, exception, or breach — those sit with Credit Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-1) and Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3). Distinct from Perform Asset Optimization (CM-1-2-1-1-4), which identifies and values portfolio opportunities — this node analyzes the specific prospective transaction, including ones arising from those recommendations. Excludes the approval decision itself (CM-1-2-1-3-2).\nIn scope: Analyze deal economics and sensitivities | check strategy fit | pre-check credit exposure and limit headroom | assess operational feasibility where applicable | identify regulatory treatment and reportability\nOut of scope: Portfolio opportunity identification (CM-1-2-1-1-4) | credit and risk limit setting, overrides, and exceptions (CM-1-2-2-1, CM-1-2-2-3) | the approval decision (CM-1-2-1-3-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "asset-optimization recommendations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "credit and limit headroom"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prospective deal terms"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "pre-trade analysis supporting the approval decision"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Ensure the economics, authority, credit exposure, risk-limit headroom, operational feasibility, and reporting implications of a specific prospective trade are understood before execution."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-10",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11175"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-p45-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Swap Data Reporting (Creation Data)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trade Regulatory Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Determine whether an executed swap or other transaction is reportable under an applicable trade-reporting regime and, where the organization is the reporting counterparty or has delegated reporting responsibility, submit required creation data to the designated registered swap data repository within applicable deadlines; correct errors and retain required reporting evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Scoped at the decision owner's direction to applicable regimes and assigned reporting responsibility — CFTC Part 45 is US-specific evidence for the creation-data versus continuation-data distinction (17 CFR 45.3 versus 45.4), which is the boundary with CM-1-2-2-2-4, recorded so the Confirmations batch inherits it; it does not make every trade, entity, or jurisdiction reportable. Which entity is the reporting counterparty or delegated reporter per regime is a follow-up noted in the batch 08 PR. APQC 11175 is an unrelated profitability candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.10"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Report Trades to SDR"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers reportability determination, creation-data submission, corrections, resubmissions, acknowledgements, and evidence retention under applicable regimes. Under US CFTC Part 45, this includes creation-data reporting as defined by the applicable rule. Confirmation-event and continuation reporting may be handled by Report Confirmation To SDR (CM-1-2-2-2-4) where the reporting model and regulation require it. Excludes regulatory-policy ownership and monitoring, which belong to Regulatory & Compliance (CM-1-2-4-3); excludes the legal determination of reporting responsibility where Legal/Compliance retains that authority; excludes regimes, jurisdictions, instruments, and reporting events not applicable to the organization.\nIn scope: Determine reportability under applicable regimes | submit required creation data within deadlines where the organization holds reporting responsibility | correct, resubmit, and track acknowledgements | retain required reporting evidence\nOut of scope: Regulatory-policy ownership and compliance monitoring (CM-1-2-4-3) | legal determination of reporting responsibility (Legal/Compliance) | confirmation-event and continuation reporting (CM-1-2-2-2-4) | non-applicable regimes, instruments, and events"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "applicable reporting rules and deadlines"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured deals with reporting attributes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "repository specifications"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "submitted, evidenced creation-data reports under applicable regimes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every reportable trade the organization must report reaches the repository on time, once, correctly."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-11",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Power Transmission Deal Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed power transmission deals — transmission service, capacity, and congestion-related rights, with path, quantity, period, and charges — so transmission positions and obligations are represented from execution onward."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). The dispatch/grid-operations exclusion follows the batch 07 wording on CM-1-2-1-1-6. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.11"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Transmission Deals"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers deal entry for power transmission transactions supporting the power side of the portfolio, consistent with the power nodes elsewhere in the branch (Receive Power Generation Forecast, CM-1-2-1-1-6; Settle Power, CM-1-2-4-1-15; Settle ISO/Power Pools, CM-1-2-4-1-7). Excludes physical transmission scheduling and grid/system operations, owned by the relevant system authorities; excludes power and ISO settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-15, CM-1-2-4-1-7). Where a power transaction involves a separately captured transmission arrangement, Capture Transmission Deals (CM-1-2-1-3-11) records the applicable terms before Settle Power (CM-1-2-4-1-15) calculates or validates the associated transmission-related charges. Other power-settlement activities may proceed independently.\nIn scope: Capture transmission deal terms with path, period, and charges | represent transmission rights and obligations | link deals to books and strategies | correct capture errors\nOut of scope: Transmission scheduling and grid/system operations (system authorities) | power and ISO settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-15, CM-1-2-4-1-7)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "charge structures"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed transmission deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "path and period references"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured transmission deal records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Transmission rights are on the book with their path and period intact."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20074"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trade Authorization"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Secure the approvals a trade requires before execution — verifying the trader's authority under the delegation of authority, escalating deals beyond that authority, and documenting each approval — so every executed trade is traceably authorized."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Escalation wording added at the decision owner's direction: exceptions may be approved under the formal escalation procedure, but this process never owns authority-policy design — applying versus setting the delegation of authority is the front-office/middle-office split. Structured deals route here for escalated approval per CM-1-2-1-3-8. APQC 20074 STRONG with no validator; generic approval candidate, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Obtain Trade Approval"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the pre-execution authorization step: checking the deal against the trader's delegated authority, routing above-authority and non-standard deals (including structured deals) for escalated approval, and recording who approved what. Includes escalation and documented approval, rejection, or conditional approval of trades that exceed delegated authority, approach or breach a limit, are non-standard, or require a documented risk or compliance exception; it does not itself set, waive, or permanently amend risk limits, credit limits, or delegation-of-authority policy. The delegation of authority is set and maintained by Market Risk Management (Establish & Maintain Delegation Of Authority, CM-1-2-2-3-2); this process applies it. Excludes strategy approval, owned by Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4); excludes post-trade compliance monitoring (Regulatory & Compliance, CM-1-2-4-3). Obtain Trade Approval (CM-1-2-1-3-2) checks each trade against the delegation of authority maintained by Establish & Maintain Delegation Of Authority (DOA) (CM-1-2-2-3-2).\nIn scope: Verify trader authority against the delegation of authority | route above-authority, near-limit, and non-standard deals for escalated approval | approve, reject, or conditionally approve under the documented escalation procedure | document approvals traceably and block unapproved execution\nOut of scope: Setting, waiving, or amending limits and delegation-of-authority policy (CM-1-2-2-3-2, CM-1-2-2-3-6) | strategy approval (CM-1-2-1-4) | compliance monitoring (CM-1-2-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "delegation of authority"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "pre-trade analysis"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-11"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-5"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-6"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-7"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-8"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-9"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "documented trade approvals, rejections, and conditions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No trade executes without traceable authority."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20022"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Physical Deal Entry"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed physical purchases and sales of crude, feedstocks, and products completely and promptly — counterparty, product and quality, quantity, price and pricing basis, delivery terms, location, period, and title-transfer terms — linked to book and strategy, so the trade record is available to confirmation, risk, actualization, and settlement."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). First of the eight deal-type capture variants; each shares the capture discipline and differs by instrument terms. Title-transfer, delivery-point, and quality terms retained per the decision owner's review — they drive actualization, invoicing, tax, and settlement downstream. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Physical Trades"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers deal entry and validation for physical commodity transactions: capturing full commercial terms including delivery basis and title-transfer terms, validating against execution evidence, linking to book, strategy, and contract, and correcting capture errors. Excludes negotiating or deciding the trade (strategy processes and the authorized execution role); excludes confirmation with the counterparty (CM-1-2-2-2); excludes movement actualization (CM-1-2-3-1) and settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-1, CM-1-2-4-1-2); excludes product exchange agreements, administered under Manage Product Exchange Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-1). Capture Physical Trades (CM-1-2-1-3-3) records the agreed commercial terms and makes the required trade data available to Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2) for prompt counterparty confirmation. Initial capture precedes submission for confirmation; discrepancies may require controlled correction of the captured record.\nIn scope: Capture full commercial terms of executed physical deals, including delivery and title-transfer terms | validate against execution evidence | link deals to book, strategy, and contract | correct capture errors\nOut of scope: Trade negotiation and execution (strategy processes, authorized execution role) | confirmation (CM-1-2-2-2) | actualization and settlement (CM-1-2-3-1, CM-1-2-4-1) | product exchange agreement administration (CM-1-2-7-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "book and strategy assignments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "execution evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "validated physical deal records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "One accurate record per physical deal, immediately after execution."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19582"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exchange-Traded Deal Capture"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Futures Trade Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record exchange-executed futures and listed-options trades with contract, delivery month, quantity, price, account, clearing-broker, and allocation details; validate captured execution data against available execution and broker messages; and resolve trade-capture exceptions so the trading record reflects the executed cleared position."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction to separate capture validation from independent reconciliation controls: this process resolves its own execution and capture breaks; the independent broker/clearing reconciliation control is owned by a designated control function, whose identity is an open follow-up noted in the batch 08 PR. 'Exchange' disambiguated: exchange-executed cleared instruments, corroborated by the Settle Exchange Trades and Settle Broker siblings; barrel exchanges live in the products branches. APQC 19582 is foreign-exchange trading; false lexical match, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Exchange Trades"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers capture of exchange-executed, cleared instruments: deal entry from execution records, allocation to books and strategies, validation against execution and broker messages, and resolution of capture exceptions. 'Exchange' here means executed on a futures exchange and cleared — not product exchange agreements, which are administered under Manage Product Exchange Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-1) and Manage Refined Product Exchanges (CM-1-2-6-2-2). Excludes independent broker, clearing, and exchange reconciliation controls where those are performed by the middle office, risk, finance operations, or another designated control function; excludes margining and collateral, owned by Credit Risk Management (Perform Margining, CM-1-2-2-1-5); excludes broker settlement (Settle Broker, CM-1-2-4-1-16) and exchange-trade settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-3).\nIn scope: Capture exchange-executed trades with contract and clearing detail | allocate to books and strategies | validate captured data against execution and broker messages | resolve trade-capture exceptions\nOut of scope: Independent broker, clearing, and exchange reconciliation controls (designated control function) | product exchange agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-1, CM-1-2-6-2-2) | margining and collateral (CM-1-2-2-1-5) | broker and exchange settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-16, CM-1-2-4-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "account and book mappings"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "execution records and broker messages"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-5"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-4-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured, exception-resolved exchange trade records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The trading record reflects the executed cleared position, exception by exception."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Storage Capacity Deal Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed storage and throughput deals — facility, capacity, injection and withdrawal rights, fees, and period — so capacity positions, obligations, and costs are represented in the trading system from execution onward."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Negotiate-versus-capture split with CM-1-2-7-1-3 mirrors the established decide-versus-record pattern. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Storage Deals"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers deal entry for storage capacity transactions: leased tankage and cavern capacity, throughput commitments, and capacity resale, with their rights, fee structures, and periods. The negotiation of storage and throughput agreements is owned by Negotiate Storage / Throughput Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-3); this node captures the executed deal into the trading record. Excludes storage inventory administration (Manage Third Party Storage, CM-1-1-3-7-11); excludes storage settlement (Settle Terminal/Storage, CM-1-2-4-1-14). Capture Storage Deals (CM-1-2-1-3-5) records the agreed storage-service terms before those terms are used by Settle Terminal/Storage (CM-1-2-4-1-14) to calculate and validate applicable charges. Settlement follows the agreement’s billing schedule and may occur periodically or in advance while the contract and storage operations remain active.\nIn scope: Capture storage and throughput deal terms | represent capacity rights, obligations, and fees | link deals to books and strategies | correct capture errors\nOut of scope: Agreement negotiation (CM-1-2-7-1-3) | third-party storage inventory administration (CM-1-1-3-7-11) | storage settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-10"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed storage deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "facility and capacity references"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-3-1-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured storage deal records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capacity deals exist in the book the moment they exist in the market."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-emtr-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-rfs-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Environmental Instrument Deal Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed purchases, sales, and transfers of program-specific environmental instruments — such as RINs, RECs, and emissions allowances — with program, vintage, quantity, price, and compliance-period detail, so instrument positions are accurate from execution onward."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Program-specific instrument treatment per the batch 07 Forecast Renewables decision; the in-scope instrument set remains the open follow-up recorded there. Jurisdiction-specific applicability per the EPA source limitations. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Environmental/Renewable Deals"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers deal entry for environmental and renewable instruments, treating each as program-specific per the batch 07 decision: capturing program, instrument type, vintage, and compliance-period attributes alongside commercial terms. Excludes forecasting the position (Forecast Renewables, CM-1-2-1-1-3); excludes instrument actualization (Perform RINs/REC Actualization, CM-1-2-3-1-7); excludes emissions settlement (Settle Environmental Instruments, CM-1-2-4-1-8); excludes regulatory filing (EHS & Government Reporting, locked rule) and the allowance-position economics (Manage and Support Emissions Trading, CM-1-1-7-3-3). Program applicability is jurisdiction-specific.\nIn scope: Capture environmental and renewable deal terms with program, vintage, and period attributes | link deals to compliance positions, books, and strategies | validate against execution evidence | correct capture errors\nOut of scope: Position forecasting (CM-1-2-1-1-3) | instrument actualization (CM-1-2-3-1-7) | settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-8) | regulatory filing (EHS & Government Reporting) | allowance-position economics (CM-1-1-7-3-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "compliance-period calendars"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed instrument deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "program and vintage references"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-3-1-7"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured environmental instrument deal records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every credit bought, sold, or transferred is on the book with its program identity intact."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-7",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-p45-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "OTC Derivatives Capture"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Swap Trade Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed over-the-counter derivative trades — swaps, options, and other bilateral instruments, with underlying index, fixed and floating terms, notional quantity, tenor, and counterparty — flagging reportable transactions, so financial positions and obligations are accurate from execution onward."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Reportability flagging here, submission at CM-1-2-1-3-10 — under US CFTC rules the capture data drives creation-data reporting; other regimes apply their own rules. Swap terminology per the CFTC glossary. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Financial (OTC) Trades"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers deal entry for bilateral financial instruments: full instrument terms, index and pricing references, and the regulatory attributes that determine reportability under applicable trade-reporting regimes. Excludes trade reporting submission itself (Report Trades to SDR, CM-1-2-1-3-10); excludes confirmation (CM-1-2-2-2); excludes valuation and curves (Market Risk Management: Setup And Manage Curves, CM-1-2-2-3-3; Manage Commodity Valuations, CM-1-2-2-3-15); excludes OTC settlement (Settle Financial OTC Trades, CM-1-2-4-1-11). Capture Financial (OTC) Trades (CM-1-2-1-3-7) records the agreed transaction terms and makes the required trade data available to Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2) for prompt counterparty confirmation. Initial capture precedes submission for confirmation; discrepancies and subsequent amendments are handled through controlled correction and confirmation procedures.\nIn scope: Capture OTC instrument terms and references | flag reportable transactions and their attributes | link deals to books, strategies, and master agreements | correct capture errors\nOut of scope: Regulatory reporting submission (CM-1-2-1-3-10) | confirmation (CM-1-2-2-2) | valuation and curve management (CM-1-2-2-3) | OTC settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-11)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed OTC terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "index and reference data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "master agreement links"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-10"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured OTC deal records with reporting attributes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Bilateral derivatives are on the book with the attributes regulation and risk need."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-8",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Structured Transaction Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed structured and non-standard transactions — multi-leg, embedded-optionality, tolling, prepay, and similar bespoke deals — decomposing them into capturable components so their positions, risks, and obligations are fully represented rather than approximated."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Coordination widened at the decision owner's direction to the designated valuation, risk, legal, accounting, and operations stakeholders — independent validation and accounting treatment are not assumed identical to Market Risk ownership; which reviewers are mandatory is a follow-up noted in the batch 08 PR. The representation-fidelity duty is the distinguishing purpose: a structured deal captured as the wrong legs is a silent risk error. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.8"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Structured Deals"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the specialized capture of deals that do not fit standard templates: decomposing the transaction into legs and components the systems can represent, verifying the representation reproduces the deal's economics and risks, and coordinating with the designated valuation, risk, legal, accounting, and operations stakeholders as required to ensure the captured representation is complete, controllable, and suitable for downstream valuation, confirmation, accounting, and settlement. Structured deals route through escalated approval (Obtain Trade Approval, CM-1-2-1-3-2) before execution. Excludes structuring and negotiating the deal (strategy and origination); excludes independent valuation methodology, model validation, and valuation-control approval, owned by the designated valuation and control functions (Market Risk Management for valuation methodology, CM-1-2-2-3-15); excludes each component's downstream confirmation and settlement, which follow their instrument types (Confirmations Management, CM-1-2-2-2; Settlements, CM-1-2-4-1).\nIn scope: Decompose structured deals into capturable components | verify the representation reproduces deal economics and risk | coordinate with designated valuation, risk, legal, accounting, and operations stakeholders | correct representation errors\nOut of scope: Deal structuring and negotiation (strategy, origination) | independent valuation methodology, model validation, and valuation-control approval (designated valuation and control functions; CM-1-2-2-3-15) | component confirmation and settlement per instrument type (Confirmations Management, CM-1-2-2-2; Settlements, CM-1-2-4-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "component and leg templates"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed structured deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "stakeholder representation requirements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "decomposed, verified structured deal records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Bespoke deals are represented whole, not approximated."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-9",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-doe-rppl-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Transport Capacity Deal Capture"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Record executed transportation capacity deals — pipeline capacity, vessel charters, railcar commitments, and trucking capacity, with route or path, capacity, period, and rates — so transport positions, obligations, and costs are represented from execution onward."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 08 (2026-09-19). Deal capture here; contract lifecycle at Contract Management; usage at nominations; settlement at the mode-specific settlement nodes — a durable taxonomy rule per the decision owner's review. APQC: no meaningful candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.3.9"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capture Transportation Deals"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers deal entry for transportation capacity transactions across modes, including capacity acquired, released, or resold. The ongoing administration of carrier relationships and contracts is owned by Manage Carrier Contracts (CM-1-2-1-2-9) and Manage Product Transport Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-2); nominations that use the captured capacity are owned by Plan & Execute Nominations (CM-1-1-3-6-1); transport settlement follows the mode-specific settlement nodes (CM-1-2-4-1-12/-13/-4/-5); physical transport operation is owned by Midstream and carriers.\nIn scope: Capture transportation capacity deal terms by mode | represent capacity rights, obligations, and rates | link deals to books and strategies | correct capture errors\nOut of scope: Carrier contract administration (CM-1-2-1-2-9, CM-1-2-7-1-2) | nominations and capacity use (CM-1-1-3-6-1) | mode-specific settlement (CM-1-2-4-1) | physical transport operation (Midstream, carriers)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-9"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed transport deal terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "rate structures"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "route, path, and mode references"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-4-1-12"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured transportation deal records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Transport capacity is on the book the moment it is committed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20674"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading Strategy Development & Stewardship"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop, approve, and steward the trading strategies the front office runs — defining each strategy's objective, markets, instruments, and horizon, aligning it with approved authorities and risk limits, reviewing performance, and adjusting or retiring strategies as conditions change."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 07 (2026-09-19). A leaf L4 with no children in the map; the front-office/middle-office split is preserved — strategy stewardship here; authority, limits, risk appetite, independent valuation governance, and risk-control challenge at Market Risk Management (exclusion made explicit at the decision owner's direction so strategy approval and risk-appetite approval cannot blur); compliance at Regulatory & Compliance. APQC 20674 is an IT-strategy candidate; false lexical match, comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading Strategy Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the strategy lifecycle: proposing and documenting strategies, securing approval within the delegation of authority, aligning with risk limits, monitoring strategy performance and adherence, and adjusting or retiring strategies. Excludes setting the delegation of authority and the risk limits themselves, owned by Market Risk Management (Establish & Maintain Delegation Of Authority, CM-1-2-2-3-2; Manage Risk Limits, CM-1-2-2-3-6); excludes portfolio-level risk appetite, limit-setting, independent valuation governance, and risk-control challenge, which belong to Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3); excludes trade execution and capture, owned by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3); excludes trading compliance monitoring, owned by Regulatory & Compliance (CM-1-2-4-3). Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4) develops and adjusts trading strategies within the delegated authorities and market-risk limits governed by Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3).\nIn scope: Propose and document trading strategies | secure approval within the delegation of authority | align strategies with risk limits | review strategy performance and adjust or retire\nOut of scope: Delegation of authority and risk limit setting (CM-1-2-2-3-2, CM-1-2-2-3-6) | portfolio risk appetite, independent valuation governance, and risk-control challenge (CM-1-2-2-3) | trade execution and capture (CM-1-2-1-3) | compliance monitoring (CM-1-2-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/constrainedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-1-4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-8"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-13"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "delegation of authority and risk limits"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "forward view and revenue projections"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "strategy performance results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved, monitored trading strategies"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Ensure every strategy the front office runs is defined, authorized, within limits, and worth running."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmations and Risk management consists of processes performed in the middle office to minimize risk of losses in the trading book due to change in market conditions i.e. commodity prices, interest rates, credit spreads, foreign-exchange rates. Middle office is responsible for managing confirmations, scenario modelling and price forecasting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmations & Risk Management"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20711"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty Credit Risk Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The capability to control counterparty credit risk in trading — assessing counterparty creditworthiness, setting and maintaining credit limits, administering credit support and margin, measuring exposure, analyzing portfolio credit risk, monitoring positions against limits, and reporting the credit risk picture — so credit losses are anticipated, bounded, and visible before they happen."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Concept type: capability (the decision owner confirmed) — heterogeneous recurring control processes jointly enabling one outcome; a counterparty can be reviewed, monitored, collateralized, margined, reported, and re-limited concurrently, so there is no single per-counterparty lifecycle. Binding credit-boundary rule (the decision owner, batch 11): Trading Counterparty Credit Risk governs exposure arising from trading, commodity and capacity positions, settlement cycles, collateral, margin, master agreements, and counterparty default risk. Commercial Customer Credit governs exposure arising from customer orders, deliveries, invoices, receivables, payment terms, credit holds, and collections (Manage Credit & Risk, CM-1-3-7-4). The same legal entity may be subject to both processes in different roles; shared legal identity does not merge the exposure, decision rights, limit structures, or control processes. Organizational delivery model not prescribed, per the batch 10 neutrality decision. APQC 20711 is an IT-risk candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit Risk Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the independent credit-risk control over trading counterparties: reviews, limits, credit-support and collateral administration, exposure calculation, margining, advanced analytics, continuous monitoring, and reporting. This is an independent control function; the enterprise may operate it through middle-office, risk, or another designated function — the taxonomy does not prescribe the delivery model. Excludes trading decisions and pre-trade checks, which apply these limits (Manage Pre-Trade Analysis, CM-1-2-1-3-1); excludes commercial customer credit in order-to-cash, owned by Manage Credit & Risk (CM-1-3-7-4) — the boundary is the relationship and exposure type, not the organizational branch; excludes market risk, owned by Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3); excludes inventory risk (Assess & Manage Inventory Risk, CM-1-2-5-4-1); excludes credit-loss accounting — provisions, impairments, write-offs, and disclosures — owned by Finance under its locked rule; excludes legal enforcement, security documentation, and insolvency action, owned by Legal & Corporate Communications. When the transaction is subject to counterparty-credit approval or support requirements, Credit Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-1) maintains approved counterparty credit limits and required credit-support decisions within which Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) operates; the recipient retains its other decisions and authorities.\nIn scope: Assess counterparty creditworthiness | set and maintain credit limits | administer credit support, collateral, and margining | calculate and monitor credit exposure | analyze and report portfolio credit risk\nOut of scope: Trading decisions and pre-trade checks (CM-1-2-1-3-1) | commercial customer credit (CM-1-3-7-4) | market risk (CM-1-2-2-3) | inventory risk (CM-1-2-5-4-1) | credit-loss accounting: provisions, write-offs, disclosures (Finance) | legal enforcement and security documentation (Legal & Corporate Communications)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/capability"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty financials and ratings"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "credit-support and agreement terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "positions and mark-to-market"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "risk appetite"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "bounded, monitored, reported counterparty credit risk"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit losses are anticipated, bounded, and visible before they happen."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19587"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty Credit Assessment"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assess a counterparty's creditworthiness — at onboarding, on a periodic cycle, and on trigger events — analyzing financial statements, ratings, ownership and support structures, payment behavior, and qualitative factors, and assigning or updating the internal credit assessment that limits and monitoring run on."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Review versus surveillance split: this node reassesses on cycle and trigger; CM-1-2-2-1-7 watches continuously and triggers this node. APQC 19587 STRONG with no validator; supporting comparative evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform Counterparty Credit Reviews"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the credit assessment process: initial reviews supporting onboarding (Create New Counterparty, CM-1-2-1-2-1, coordinates them), scheduled periodic reviews, and event-triggered reassessments on deterioration signals or corporate events. The output is the internal credit assessment consumed by Manage Credit Limits (CM-1-2-2-1-2). Excludes setting the limits themselves (CM-1-2-2-1-2); excludes continuous surveillance (Monitor & Analyze Credit, CM-1-2-2-1-7); excludes commercial customer credit assessment (CM-1-3-7-4).\nIn scope: Perform onboarding, periodic, and event-triggered credit reviews | analyze financials, ratings, ownership, and payment behavior | assign and update internal credit assessments | recommend limit and credit-support consequences\nOut of scope: Limit setting (CM-1-2-2-1-2) | continuous surveillance (CM-1-2-2-1-7) | customer credit assessment (CM-1-3-7-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty financials and ratings"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "ownership and support structures"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "payment and dispute history"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current internal credit assessments"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every counterparty's creditworthiness is currently and defensibly assessed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-7"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20929"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit Limit Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish, maintain, publish, and adjust credit limits for trading counterparties and counterparty groups — based on approved credit assessments, risk appetite, exposure methodology, and credit-support arrangements — administer documented temporary-excess and exception decisions under delegated authority, and reduce, suspend, or withdraw limits when deterioration or policy triggers require it."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction: this process establishes, publishes, and administers limits and delegated exception decisions; enforcement happens through connected pre-trade, surveillance, and transaction controls. Temporary excesses are administered and recorded under the approved delegation of authority — which function holds that exception authority is a follow-up noted in the batch 11 PR. APQC 20929 is a corporate-card candidate; false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Credit Limits"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the limit lifecycle: establishing limits from assessments and appetite, structuring them by counterparty, group, tenor, and product where applicable, publishing them to the connected controls, administering and recording temporary-excess approvals made under the approved delegation of authority, and cutting limits on deterioration. Enforcement occurs through the connected controls — pre-trade checks (Manage Pre-Trade Analysis, CM-1-2-1-3-1), surveillance and escalation (CM-1-2-2-1-7), and applicable transaction controls — not through this process itself. Excludes the credit assessment (CM-1-2-2-1-1); excludes portfolio risk appetite, which is governance above this process; excludes customer credit limits in order-to-cash (CM-1-3-7-4).\nIn scope: Establish and structure limits from assessments and appetite | maintain and publish limits by counterparty and group | administer and record temporary-excess approvals under the delegation of authority | reduce, suspend, or withdraw limits on deterioration or policy triggers\nOut of scope: Credit assessment (CM-1-2-2-1-1) | limit enforcement through connected controls (CM-1-2-1-3-1, CM-1-2-2-1-7) | portfolio risk appetite (risk governance) | customer credit limits (CM-1-3-7-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "exposure and utilization data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "internal credit assessments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "risk appetite"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current, approved, and published credit limits and exception decisions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exposure capacity always matches assessed creditworthiness."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-7"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19586"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collateral Administration"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit Support Administration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer contractual credit support both held and posted — cash collateral, securities, letters of credit, guarantees, and other eligible security, with their haircuts, thresholds, independent amounts, and substitutions — calling, receiving, returning, valuing, and reconciling credit support under the applicable arrangements, so credit exposure is secured to the extent the agreements require."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Broadened at the decision owner's direction from 'bilateral versus cleared' to credit support versus CCP/exchange/broker margin: contractual credit support of all forms — cash, securities, letters of credit, guarantees — is administered here, and bilateral margin under a credit-support arrangement stays here unless the operating model separates it. Which collateral forms are genuinely in scope, and whether bilateral IM/VM workflows sit with Credit Risk, Treasury, or a specialized team, are follow-ups noted in the batch 11 PR. Credit-support structure per ISDA documentation for applicable OTC frameworks. APQC 19586 scored 0.8 STRONG with no validator; supporting comparative evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Collateral"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers administration of bilateral and other contractually agreed credit-support arrangements across held and posted positions: issuing and answering calls per credit-support annexes and credit terms, valuing collateral with applicable haircuts, managing eligibility, thresholds, independent amounts, and substitutions, reconciling balances with counterparties, and coordinating release at offboarding (Terminate/Novate Counterparty, CM-1-2-1-2-3). Includes letters of credit, guarantees, and eligible security where in scope. Excludes CCP, exchange, and broker margin workflows, which belong to Perform Margining (CM-1-2-2-1-5) — bilateral margin required under a credit-support arrangement remains within this process unless the detailed operating model intentionally separates it. Credit-support documentation is established through Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2) with Legal & Corporate Communications; the cash and securities movements themselves execute through the settlement and finance processes.\nIn scope: Issue and answer credit-support calls per agreements | value collateral with applicable haircuts | manage eligibility, thresholds, independent amounts, and substitutions | reconcile credit-support positions and coordinate release\nOut of scope: CCP, exchange, and broker margin workflows (CM-1-2-2-1-5) | credit-support documentation (CM-1-2-1-2, Legal & Corporate Communications) | cash and securities movement execution (settlement and finance processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "collateral valuations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty statements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "credit-support terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "exposure calculations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "reconciled, agreement-compliant credit-support positions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exposure is secured exactly as the agreements require, both ways."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12893"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit Exposure Measurement"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Calculate current and, where required by approved methodology, potential future credit exposure for each counterparty and group — aggregating trading positions, mark-to-market values, delivered-but-unpaid and other settlement-cycle exposures, and applicable netting, collateral, and credit-support effects — so limits, monitoring, and credit support run on a defensible exposure number."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Methodology-qualified at the decision owner's direction: potential future exposure, wrong-way-risk adjustments, and stressed assumptions apply where the approved methodology requires them — not silently in every number; the exposure-versus-analytics split with CM-1-2-2-1-6 is preserved. Consumes marks and curves owned by Market Risk; owns the aggregation and offsets. APQC 12893 is a WEAK review-link."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Calculate Credit Exposure"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the exposure measurement process: assembling positions, mark-to-market, and settlement-cycle amounts by counterparty and group; applying enforceable netting and credit-support offsets per the governing agreements; computing potential future exposure where the approved methodology requires it; and publishing exposures to limits, monitoring, and credit support. Exposure measurement may incorporate wrong-way-risk adjustments, concentration considerations, and stressed assumptions where required by approved methodology; portfolio-level analysis remains in Perform Advanced Credit Risk Analytics (CM-1-2-2-1-6). Valuation inputs (curves, marks) are owned by Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3-3, CM-1-2-2-3-15); netting enforceability is a legal determination (Legal & Corporate Communications).\nIn scope: Assemble positions and amounts by counterparty and group | apply enforceable netting and credit-support effects | compute current and methodology-required potential future exposure | publish exposures to limits, monitoring, and credit support\nOut of scope: Valuation and curve ownership (CM-1-2-2-3) | netting enforceability determination (Legal & Corporate Communications) | portfolio-level analytics (CM-1-2-2-1-6) | limit decisions (CM-1-2-2-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "netting and credit-support terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "positions and mark-to-market"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "settlement-cycle amounts"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published current and potential exposures by counterparty and group"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "One defensible exposure number per counterparty, every day."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10954"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Margin Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administer margin obligations for cleared and other applicable margined positions — receiving, validating, forecasting, and issuing or responding to margin calls as applicable, reconciling margin balances against CCP, exchange, broker, and counterparty statements, and escalating failed or disputed calls — so margin obligations are met and margin held matches what positions require."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction: the CCP, clearing broker, or exchange typically computes formal margin requirements — this process validates, forecasts, and operates the calls rather than asserting in-house calculation authority for every cleared product. Margin versus credit support split per the -3 rule. APQC 10954 'Perform abandonment' is an unrelated false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform Margining"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the margining cycle: validating externally calculated margin requirements and calculating internal forecasts or independent checks where required, issuing or responding to calls within deadlines, reconciling margin balances against CCP, exchange, broker, and counterparty statements, escalating failures and disputes, and forecasting margin requirements for liquidity visibility. Cleared positions arrive from Capture Exchange Trades (CM-1-2-1-3-4); contractual credit support is administered at Manage Collateral (CM-1-2-2-1-3); the cash movements execute through settlement and finance processes (Settle Broker, CM-1-2-4-1-16).\nIn scope: Validate externally calculated margin requirements and run internal forecasts or independent checks where required | issue or respond to margin calls within deadlines | reconcile margin balances against CCP, exchange, broker, and counterparty statements | escalate failures and disputes and forecast requirements\nOut of scope: Contractual credit-support administration (CM-1-2-2-1-3) | exchange trade capture (CM-1-2-1-3-4) | margin cash movement execution (CM-1-2-4-1-16, finance processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "CCP, exchange, and broker margin statements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cleared positions and prices"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "margin methodologies and deadlines"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-4-1-16"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "validated, reconciled, escalation-managed margin positions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Margin obligations are always met, and margin held always matches the positions."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19568"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Portfolio Credit Analytics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze credit risk at portfolio level — concentrations, stress and scenario impacts, default-likelihood signals, and correlation effects such as wrong-way exposure — so appetite, limits, and mitigation decisions rest on more than single-counterparty views."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Analyze-and-recommend only: appetite and concentration-limit approval sit with the designated risk-governance body, per the decision owner's edit; independent validation not assumed owned here, per the batch 08 precedent. APQC 19568 is a process-control candidate; false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform Advanced Credit Risk Analytics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers portfolio credit analytics: concentration analysis by counterparty group, sector, geography, and product; credit stress testing and scenario impacts; default-likelihood and early-warning modeling; and wrong-way risk analysis where exposure and default likelihood move together. Findings feed limit structures (CM-1-2-2-1-2) and reporting (CM-1-2-2-1-8). Excludes decision-making on risk appetite and portfolio credit concentration limits where those are set by the designated risk-governance body — this node analyzes and recommends; excludes market risk scenarios, owned by Manage And Run Risk Scenarios (CM-1-2-2-3-11) and Conduct Advanced Risk Analytics (CM-1-2-2-3-12); excludes independent model validation (designated validation function). Perform Advanced Credit Risk Analytics (CM-1-2-2-1-6) provides portfolio concentrations, stress impacts, default signals, and recommended limit structures to inform Manage Credit Limits (CM-1-2-2-1-2); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Analyze portfolio concentrations | run credit stress tests and scenarios | model default likelihood and early-warning signals | analyze wrong-way risk and recommend mitigation\nOut of scope: Risk-appetite and concentration-limit approval (designated risk-governance body) | market risk scenarios and analytics (CM-1-2-2-3-11, CM-1-2-2-3-12) | independent model validation (designated validation function) | limit decisions (CM-1-2-2-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty groupings and sectors"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "default and ratings data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "exposures and limits"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "stress scenarios"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "portfolio credit analyses with mitigation recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The portfolio's credit weak points are found before a default finds them."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-7",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11215"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit Surveillance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Continuously watch counterparty credit — exposures against limits, breach detection and aging, and early-warning signals from ratings, news, payment behavior, and market indicators — escalating breaches and deterioration per policy and triggering reassessment where warranted."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). The detect-versus-decide split: surveillance here, decisions at -1 and -2 — the batch 04 pattern applied to credit. APQC 11215 STRONG with no validator; supporting comparative evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Monitor & Analyze Credit"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers continuous credit surveillance: daily exposure-versus-limit monitoring, breach identification, escalation, and tracking to resolution, and early-warning monitoring of deterioration signals that trigger event-driven reviews (CM-1-2-2-1-1) or limit actions (CM-1-2-2-1-2). Excludes the periodic reassessment itself (CM-1-2-2-1-1); excludes limit decisions (CM-1-2-2-1-2); excludes customer credit monitoring in order-to-cash (Monitor Credit Against Limit, CM-1-3-7-4-3).\nIn scope: Monitor exposures against limits daily | detect, escalate, and track breaches | watch early-warning deterioration signals | trigger reviews and limit actions\nOut of scope: Periodic credit reassessment (CM-1-2-2-1-1) | limit decisions (CM-1-2-2-1-2) | customer credit monitoring (CM-1-3-7-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "breach policy"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "published exposures and limits"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "ratings, news, and payment signals"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "escalated breaches and deterioration alerts with tracking"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No breach and no deterioration signal goes unseen or unescalated."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1-8",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Credit Risk Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce governed internal credit-risk reports — exposures, limit utilization, breaches, credit-support and margin positions, and concentrations, at agreed cadences and levels for management and committees — and provide controlled inputs to applicable external or regulatory reporting through their accountable owners, so the credit risk picture is current, consistent, and decision-ready."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 11 (2026-09-19). Internal report production here; external and statutory reporting is supported through, never owned instead of, its accountable owners — the decision owner's edit prevents reading report production as regulator submission. APQC 10522 is an HR-reporting candidate; false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.1.8"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Credit Risk Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers credit-risk report production and distribution: standard management and committee reporting, breach and exception reporting, credit-support and concentration views, and controlled inputs to external and regulatory reporting owned by their accountable processes. Excludes financial reporting and disclosures, owned by Finance under its locked rule; excludes regulatory filing ownership (Regulatory & Compliance, CM-1-2-4-3); excludes defining enterprise KPIs (KPI workstream). Manage Credit Risk Reporting (CM-1-2-2-1-8) provides credit exposure, utilization, concentration, and credit-support reports to inform Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Produce management and committee credit-risk reporting | report breaches and exceptions | report credit-support, margin, and concentration positions | provide controlled inputs to external reporting through accountable owners\nOut of scope: Financial reporting and disclosures (Finance) | regulatory filing ownership (CM-1-2-4-3) | enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "concentration analyses"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "credit-support and margin positions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "exposures, limits, and breaches"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "distributed, governed credit-risk reports and controlled external-reporting inputs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The credit risk picture reaches its decision-makers current, consistent, and on time."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20682"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trade Confirmation Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Independently confirm and match executed trades with counterparties by generating, receiving, validating, documenting, modifying, reporting, and resolving discrepancies in trade confirmations, so the organization and its counterparty have evidenced agreement on the applicable trade terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). Concept type: process (the decision owner confirmed) — a per-trade lifecycle (generate, document, modify, report, dispute), per the batch 08 variant test. Reworded at the decision owner's direction to describe an organizationally neutral independent control rather than prescribing a middle-office delivery model — the approved L3 definition's 'middle office' names the control function, not a mandated organization. Confirmation structure per ISDA documentation for applicable OTC frameworks; physical and other deal types are confirmed per their governing agreements, standard terms, exchange rules, or platform matching. APQC 20682 is an unrelated IT candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmations Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the per-trade confirmation lifecycle after capture: outgoing confirmation generation, incoming confirmation matching, documentation control, modification processing, continuation reporting where required, and dispute resolution. This process performs an independent control over the trade-capture record. The enterprise may operate that control through a middle-office, operations, shared-services, or other designated function; this taxonomy does not prescribe the organizational delivery model. Excludes deal capture and its corrections, owned by Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3); excludes master agreement establishment and administration, owned by Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2); excludes settlement and settlement disputes (CM-1-2-4-1, CM-1-2-4-1-17); excludes risk measurement (Market Risk Management, CM-1-2-2-3). Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2) establishes the agreed transaction terms used by Settlements (CM-1-2-4-1). Settlement preparation may proceed in parallel; unresolved confirmation discrepancies are subject to the applicable settlement approval and exception controls. For its applicable trading-compliance reporting and documentation controls, Confirmations Management (CM-1-2-2-2) applies the trading-compliance policies and procedures maintained by Regulatory & Compliance (CM-1-2-4-3).\nIn scope: Generate and match trade confirmations | maintain confirmation documentation and evidence | process agreed trade modifications through re-confirmation | report confirmation and continuation events where required | resolve confirmation disputes\nOut of scope: Deal capture and capture corrections (CM-1-2-1-3) | master agreement administration (CM-1-2-1-2) | settlement and settlement disputes (CM-1-2-4-1) | risk measurement and limits (CM-1-2-2-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured deal records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty confirmations and acknowledgements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governing agreement terms"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "matched, evidenced trade confirmations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish timely, retained evidence that the organization and counterparty agree — or have a controlled, visible disagreement — on the applicable trade terms."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10136"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmation Generation & Matching"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce and dispatch outgoing trade confirmations from captured deal records — using the templates and terms of the governing agreement — and match incoming counterparty confirmations or equivalent contractual acknowledgements against the captured deal record, using the applicable product, agreement, and confirmation standards, chasing unconfirmed trades within applicable timeliness requirements."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction: matching runs against 'counterparty confirmations or equivalent contractual acknowledgements' per applicable product, agreement, and confirmation standards — not asserted as universal literal field-by-field automated comparison; timeliness requirements vary by regime, instrument, and counterparty classification. APQC 10136 is an unrelated sales-forecast candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Generate Confirms"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers confirmation generation and matching: assembling confirmations from captured terms per the governing master agreement or standard terms, dispatching through the agreed channel (including electronic confirmation platforms where used), matching incoming confirmations or equivalent acknowledgements against the capture record per the applicable standards, and escalating aging unconfirmed trades. Confirmation methods vary by product and agreement — bilateral confirmations, platform matching, exchange rules, and contractual notices are all accommodated. Mismatches route to Manage Confirm Disputes (CM-1-2-2-2-5); capture errors surfaced by matching route back to Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) for correction. Excludes confirmation template and documentation control, owned by Manage Confirmation Documentation (CM-1-2-2-2-2).\nIn scope: Assemble and dispatch confirmations from captured terms | match incoming confirmations or equivalent acknowledgements per applicable standards | chase and escalate unconfirmed trades within timeliness requirements | route mismatches and capture errors to their owners\nOut of scope: Template and documentation control (CM-1-2-2-2-2) | dispute resolution (CM-1-2-2-2-5) | capture correction (CM-1-2-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured deal records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governing agreement templates"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "incoming counterparty confirmations and acknowledgements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "dispatched and matched confirmations with chase status"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every trade is confirmed or visibly chased, never silently unconfirmed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmation Template & Records Control"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Maintain the confirmation documentation basis — approved templates and standard wording aligned to governing agreements, the archive of dispatched and matched confirmations, and the evidence trail that shows what was agreed and when — so confirmations are consistent, current, and provable."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). Template-versus-agreement split: templates implement what the governing agreements say; changing the agreement is Contract Management's lifecycle, reflected here afterward. APQC 11743 is an unrelated routing candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Confirmation Documentation"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers documentation control for the confirmation process: template and standard-wording maintenance aligned to master agreements and standard terms, version control, the confirmation archive, and retention of matching and dispatch evidence. Legal approval of template wording is owned by Legal & Corporate Communications under its locked rule; the governing agreements themselves are administered by Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2); regulatory record-retention policy is owned by Regulatory & Compliance (CM-1-2-4-3). Manage Confirmation Documentation (CM-1-2-2-2-2) maintains approved confirmation templates, standard wording, and controlled documentation versions that Generate Confirms (CM-1-2-2-2-1) needs to operate its defined process path.\nIn scope: Maintain approved confirmation templates and standard wording | control template versions against governing agreements | archive dispatched and matched confirmations | retain dispatch and matching evidence\nOut of scope: Legal approval of wording (Legal & Corporate Communications) | governing agreement administration (CM-1-2-1-2) | retention policy setting (CM-1-2-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "dispatched and matched confirmations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governing agreement terms"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "legal-approved wording"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "current templates and a complete confirmation archive"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmations are consistent with the governing agreements and provable years later."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11040"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-p45-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trade Amendment Processing"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate the confirmation-side processing of agreed post-execution changes to a trade — including amendments, allocations, partial terminations, and early terminations — by validating counterparty agreement, initiating or validating the required controlled trade-record update, re-confirming revised terms, and triggering applicable lifecycle reporting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). Reworded at the decision owner's direction: this process coordinates and verifies; the authorized trade-record owner performs the controlled update. Modification versus novation: a modification changes agreed terms between the same parties and stays here; a change of party is a novation and belongs to Contract Management per batch 09. Aligned with the batch 08 capture-correction distinction. APQC 11040 is an unrelated trade-association candidate; false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Trade Modifications"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the confirmation-side lifecycle of trade changes: intake and validation of modification requests, verification that both parties agree the change, initiation or validation of the required controlled trade-record update, re-confirmation of modified terms, and triggering of continuation reporting through Report Confirmation To SDR (CM-1-2-2-2-4) where required. The authorized trade-record owner performs the controlled capture update; this process verifies that the record and confirmation reflect the mutually agreed change — it does not independently decide commercial amendments, execute legal novations, or correct internal capture errors that do not alter mutually agreed terms. Excludes the commercial decision to modify (trading and strategy processes); excludes novations and assignments, owned by Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2-3, CM-1-2-1-2-7); excludes unilateral capture corrections (CM-1-2-1-3).\nIn scope: Intake and validate agreed modification requests | verify counterparty agreement to the change | initiate or validate the controlled trade-record update | re-confirm revised terms and trigger applicable reporting\nOut of scope: Commercial modification decisions (trading, strategy) | novations and assignments (CM-1-2-1-2) | unilateral capture corrections (CM-1-2-1-3) | performing the capture update itself (authorized trade-record owner, CM-1-2-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "agreed modification requests"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "capture records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty consents"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "re-confirmed modified trades with triggered reporting"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Modified trades are as provably agreed as new ones."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/requires": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-5"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11175"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-p45-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Swap Data Reporting (Continuation Data)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Report confirmation and lifecycle events for reportable transactions under an applicable trade-reporting regime — submitting required continuation data for amendments, terminations, and other post-execution events to the designated registered swap data repository within applicable deadlines, where the organization holds reporting responsibility — correcting errors and retaining reporting evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). Trigger made explicitly conditional at the decision owner's direction: reporting occurs only where the regime requires it, the event is reportable, and the organization holds or is delegated reporting responsibility — not every confirmation event produces a reportable continuation event. Relations use 'informed-by' rather than 'follows' because the controlled relationship vocabulary has no conditional form; the conditionality is recorded here. CFTC Part 45 (45.3 versus 45.4) is US-specific evidence for the boundary with CM-1-2-1-3-10; it is not a universal model for physical confirmations, exchange-traded futures, or other jurisdictions. APQC 11175 is an unrelated profitability candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.2.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Report Confirmation To SDR"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers continuation-side reporting under applicable regimes: determining which confirmation and lifecycle events require reporting, submitting continuation data within deadlines, corrections, resubmissions, acknowledgements, and evidence retention. A confirmation, modification, or lifecycle event triggers continuation-data reporting only where the applicable regime requires reporting, the event is reportable, and the organization has reporting responsibility or an assigned delegated-reporting obligation. Under US CFTC Part 45 this is continuation-data reporting (45.4); trade creation data is reported at capture by Report Trades to SDR (CM-1-2-1-3-10) — the boundary recorded in batch 08. Excludes regulatory-policy ownership and monitoring (Regulatory & Compliance, CM-1-2-4-3); excludes the legal determination of reporting responsibility (Legal/Compliance); excludes regimes, instruments, and events not applicable to the organization.\nIn scope: Determine reportable confirmation and lifecycle events under applicable regimes | submit required continuation data within deadlines where responsible | correct, resubmit, and track acknowledgements | retain reporting evidence\nOut of scope: Creation-data reporting (CM-1-2-1-3-10) | regulatory-policy ownership and monitoring (CM-1-2-4-3) | legal determination of reporting responsibility (Legal/Compliance) | non-applicable regimes and events"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "applicable reporting rules and deadlines"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "confirmation and lifecycle events"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "repository specifications"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "submitted, evidenced continuation-data reports under applicable regimes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every reportable lifecycle event the organization must report reaches the repository on time, once, correctly."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/triggeredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-3"
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-isda-ma-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmation Dispute Resolution"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Resolve confirmation mismatches and disputes — logging discrepancies between the capture record and the counterparty's confirmation, investigating against execution evidence, agreeing the correct terms with the counterparty, and driving the resolution into the records and any required re-reporting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 10 (2026-09-19). The dispute partition rule (the decision owner, batch 10): confirmation disputes answer 'what did the parties agree the terms were' (here); actualization disputes answer 'what was physically delivered, received, measured, or performed' (CM-1-2-3-1-8); settlement disputes answer 'what is owed, invoiced, received, paid, netted, or applied' (CM-1-2-4-1-17); demurrage claims answer 'was delay or capacity usage compensable' (CM-1-2-4-4); legal proceedings belong to Legal & Corporate Communications. The lifecycle-stage question is the placement test. APQC 11743 is an unrelated routing candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.2.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Confirm Disputes"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the confirmation dispute lifecycle: discrepancy logging and classification, investigation against capture and execution evidence, counterparty negotiation of the correct terms, escalation of aging or material disputes, and closure through corrected records, re-confirmation, and re-reporting where required. Excludes settlement disputes, owned by Manage Settlement Disputes (CM-1-2-4-1-17); excludes actualization disputes (Manage Actualization Disputes, CM-1-2-3-1-8); excludes demurrage claims (CM-1-2-4-4); excludes legal proceedings, owned by Legal & Corporate Communications. When resolution of a confirmation dispute under Manage Confirm Disputes (CM-1-2-2-2-5) produces an authorized, agreed change to the trade’s commercial terms, it hands the change to Manage Trade Modifications (CM-1-2-2-2-3) for the controlled record update and applicable re-confirmation. A correction that merely restores the record to terms already agreed does not constitute this changed-terms trigger and follows the appropriate correction workflow.\nIn scope: Log and classify confirmation discrepancies | investigate against capture and execution evidence | negotiate and agree correct terms with the counterparty | drive resolution into records, re-confirmation, and re-reporting\nOut of scope: Settlement disputes (CM-1-2-4-1-17) | actualization disputes (CM-1-2-3-1-8) | demurrage claims (CM-1-2-4-4) | legal proceedings (Legal & Corporate Communications)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "capture and execution evidence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "confirmation mismatches"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty correspondence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "resolved disputes with corrected, re-confirmed records"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No confirmation mismatch survives unexamined or unresolved."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20711"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002a"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-cftc-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Trading Market Risk Control"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The capability to independently measure, control, monitor, analyze, and report market risk in the trading book by governing risk-book structures, delegated authority, market-data inputs, valuations, limits, control cycles, positions, profit and loss, scenarios, and risk reporting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 12 (2026-09-19). Concept type: capability (the decision owner confirmed), per the batch 11 reasoning — concurrent heterogeneous control processes, no single lifecycle. Bound explicitly to the trading book at the decision owner's direction: refinery-margin, procurement-price, inventory, and corporate hedging exposures are governed here only when expressly booked into the governed trading portfolio; whether a separate corporate hedging program exists is a follow-up noted in the batch 12 PR. Middle-office framing per the approved L3 definition names the control function, not a mandated organization (batch 10 neutrality). APQC 20711 is an IT-risk candidate; comparative evidence only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market Risk Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the independent market-risk control over the trading book: control-framework structures (risk-book structure, delegation of authority, risk limits), market-data and valuation ownership (curves, volatilities and correlations, commodity valuations), the daily and monthly control cycles, risk measurement and monitoring, position and P&L control, risk-policy compliance monitoring, scenarios, advanced analytics, and reporting. An independent control function per the approved L3 definition; the delivery model is not prescribed. Excludes enterprise-wide strategic commodity-price risk, corporate hedging policy, capital allocation, and non-trading operating exposure unless those exposures are expressly booked into the governed trading portfolio. Excludes trading decisions and strategy stewardship, which are governed by these controls (CM-1-2-1-4); excludes credit risk (CM-1-2-2-1); excludes regulatory trading compliance (CM-1-2-4-3); excludes accounting P&L and its reconciliation ownership (Accounting, CM-1-2-4-2, with the economic-to-accounting reconciliation at CM-1-2-4-2-6); excludes independent model validation (designated validation function). Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) performs pre-trade authorization within the delegated authorities and risk limits governed by Market Risk Management (CM-1-2-2-3).\nIn scope: Maintain risk-book structure, delegation of authority, and risk limits | own curves, volatilities, and valuations | run daily and monthly control cycles | measure, monitor, and analyze market risk, positions, and P&L | report the risk picture\nOut of scope: Enterprise-wide commodity-price risk, corporate hedging policy, and non-trading exposure not booked into the trading portfolio | trading decisions and strategy stewardship (CM-1-2-1-4) | credit risk (CM-1-2-2-1) | regulatory trading compliance (CM-1-2-4-3) | accounting P&L (CM-1-2-4-2) | independent model validation (designated validation function)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/capability"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "captured positions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governance decisions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market prices and data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "risk appetite and policy"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "measured, bounded, visible trading-book market risk with governed control structures"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Losses from market moves in the trading book are measured, bounded, and visible before they compound."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16385"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002a"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Risk Book Structure Governance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish and maintain the governed trading-book and portfolio hierarchy used for risk aggregation, valuation, position control, and P&L reporting — defining risk-reporting book attributes, responsible owners, aggregation relationships, and effective-dated changes — and keep trading, risk, and reporting systems aligned to it."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 12 (2026-09-19). Narrowed at the decision owner's direction: strategy is business intent (Trading Strategy Management); the book is a controlled risk and P&L aggregation construct governed here — the two never collide. APQC 16385 is a generic framework candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish And Maintain Book Structure"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers governance of the risk-reporting and control structure: defining risk books with their attributes, owners, and aggregation relationships; controlling openings, closures, and moves with approvals and effective dates; and keeping capture, risk, and reporting systems aligned to one structure. Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4) defines and stewards business strategies; Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3) assigns individual deals into the approved structure; this process governs the risk-reporting and control hierarchy that strategies and deals map into. Excludes legal-entity, ledger, cost-center, profit-center, and chart-of-accounts structures, owned by Accounting (CM-1-2-4-2-8).\nIn scope: Define risk books, attributes, owners, and aggregation relationships | control structure changes with approvals and effective dates | keep capture, risk, and reporting aligned to one structure | maintain structure history\nOut of scope: Business strategy definition and stewardship (CM-1-2-1-4) | deal-to-book assignment at capture (CM-1-2-1-3) | legal-entity, ledger, and chart-of-accounts structures (CM-1-2-4-2-8)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "ownership and aggregation assignments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "structure change requests"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed, versioned risk-book and portfolio hierarchy"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "One governed risk-reporting structure that every position and P&L number rolls up through."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-10",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10935"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002a"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Risk Framework Compliance Monitoring"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Monitor adherence to the organization's own market-risk policies and control framework — mandate and delegation-of-authority adherence, control-cycle completion, exception-procedure use, and policy-required documentation — surfacing violations and control gaps to the accountable owners."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 12 (2026-09-19). Fully drafted and conditionally approved by the decision owner; held pending on the recorded cross-batch dependency because an approved row may carry no material open question. Internal-versus-external rules is the boundary with CM-1-2-4-3. Batch 16 resolution (the decision owner, 2026-09-20): the cross-batch boundary with Monitor Internal Trade Controls is resolved. Monitor Risk Policy Compliance monitors adherence to the internal market-risk framework, including risk appetite, approved limits, risk-book mandates, delegated trading authority, valuation and risk-control procedures, control-cycle evidence, and risk-exception approvals. Monitor Internal Trade Controls (CM-1-2-4-3-4) monitors the operation and evidence of internally implemented controls supporting external trading obligations. Neither process tests or owns the other's framework. Governance note (the decision owner, batch 16): the market-risk framework is governed by the designated Risk Governance body, not Compliance — the former 'governed-by: Regulatory & Compliance' relation is removed; no 'Risk Governance' taxonomy node exists and 'related-to' is not a controlled relationship_type, so the non-hierarchical relationship to Regulatory & Compliance is carried here in prose per the conditional-relation precedent (batches 10/13/14). Row content otherwise unchanged from the batch 12 conditional approval."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.3.10"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Monitor Risk Policy Compliance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers internal risk-policy compliance monitoring: checking that trading activity stays within mandates and the delegation of authority, that control cycles complete with their designated approvals, that exceptions follow their documented procedures, and that policy-required records exist; escalating violations and recurring gaps. The boundary with regulatory compliance is internal-versus-external rules: adherence to the organization's own risk framework is monitored here; compliance with external law, regulation, and market rules is owned by Regulatory & Compliance (CM-1-2-4-3). Excludes policy authorship (risk governance) and disciplinary action (management, HR). Monitor Risk Policy Compliance (CM-1-2-2-3-10) supplies documented risk-policy violations, control gaps, and exception findings that Manage Risk Reporting (CM-1-2-2-3-13) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Monitor mandate and DOA adherence | verify control-cycle completion and designated approvals | check exception-procedure use and documentation | escalate violations and control gaps\nOut of scope: Regulatory compliance monitoring (CM-1-2-4-3) | policy authorship (risk governance) | disciplinary action (management, HR)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "control-cycle records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "exception logs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "policies, mandates, and DOA"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "escalated policy violations and control-gap findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The risk framework is followed in fact, not just on paper."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-11",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11211"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002a"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market Risk Scenario & Stress Testing"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define, maintain, and run the market-risk scenario and stress set — historical and hypothetical market shocks, commodity and basis stresses, and event scenarios — quantifying their P&L and risk impacts so the organization knows what adverse markets would do to the book before they happen."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 12 (2026-09-19). Closes the batch 02 pointer: trading and market-risk scenarios here; production scenarios at CM-1-1-4-7-8. APQC 11211 is a WEAK review-link."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.3.11"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage And Run Risk Scenarios"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers trading-book scenario and stress analysis: maintaining the approved scenario library, running scenarios on the control calendar and on demand, quantifying P&L and measure impacts, and feeding results to limits, appetite discussions, and reporting. This is the trading and market-risk scenario home that batch 02's approved Perform Scenario Analysis (CM-1-1-4-7-8) explicitly points to — production-case scenario analysis stays there. Excludes credit stress testing (CM-1-2-2-1-6); excludes scenario methodology approval (risk governance). Manage And Run Risk Scenarios (CM-1-2-2-3-11) provides scenario and stress impacts on positions, profit and loss, and risk measures to inform Manage Risk Limits (CM-1-2-2-3-6); the recipient retains its own decisions. Manage And Run Risk Scenarios (CM-1-2-2-3-11) supplies scenario and stress results, assumptions, and measure impacts that Manage Risk Reporting (CM-1-2-2-3-13) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Maintain the approved scenario and stress library | run scenarios on calendar and on demand | quantify P&L and measure impacts | feed results to limits, appetite, and reporting\nOut of scope: Production-case scenario analysis (CM-1-1-4-7-8) | credit stress testing (CM-1-2-2-1-6) | scenario methodology approval (risk governance)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market histories"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "positions and valuations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "scenario library"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "quantified scenario and stress impacts"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Adverse markets are rehearsed before they are real."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-12",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20728"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002a"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002b"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Advanced Market Risk Analytics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze market risk beyond the standard measures — backtesting the measures against outcomes, analyzing model behavior and measure limitations, investigating risk concentrations and emerging exposures, and developing analytical improvements — recommending changes to methodologies, limits, and controls."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 12 (2026-09-19). Analyze-and-recommend per the batch 11 rule; model-risk boundaries per CCRO Model Risk practice as evidence. APQC 20728 is an IT-threat candidate; false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.3.12"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct Advanced Risk Analytics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers advanced market-risk analysis: backtesting and performance analysis of the risk measures, deep-dives into concentrations, correlations, and emerging exposure patterns, analysis of measure and model limitations, and recommendations to the governance and control owners. Analyze-and-recommend only: methodology approval and independent model validation sit with the designated governance and validation functions (model-risk practice per the CCRO Model Risk publication as reference evidence). Excludes credit analytics (CM-1-2-2-1-6); excludes running the standard measures (CM-1-2-2-3-7). Conduct Advanced Risk Analytics (CM-1-2-2-3-12) provides analysis and recommended limit changes that inform Manage Risk Limits (CM-1-2-2-3-6), which decides and administers any change under delegated authority. Where a governed risk report includes advanced analytical results, Manage Risk Reporting (CM-1-2-2-3-13) consumes the results produced by Conduct Advanced Risk Analytics (CM-1-2-2-3-12).\nIn scope: Backtest risk measures against outcomes | analyze concentrations, correlations, and emerging exposures | analyze measure and model limitations | recommend methodology, limit, and control changes\nOut of scope: Methodology approval and independent model validation (designated functions) | credit analytics (CM-1-2-2-1-6) | standard measure production (CM-1-2-2-3-7)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "measure histories and outcomes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "model documentation"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "positions and market data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "analytical findings with methodology and control recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The risk framework's blind spots are found by analysis, not by losses."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3-13",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10522"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ccro-002a"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market Risk Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce governed internal market-risk reports — measures, limit utilization, breaches, scenario results, positions, and P&L, at agreed cadences for management and committees — and provide controlled inputs to applicable external or regulatory reporting through their accountable owners."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 12 (2026-09-19). Mirrors the batch 11 reporting rule: internal production here; external reporting supported through, never owned instead of, accountable owners. APQC 10522 is an HR-reporting false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.2.3.13"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Risk Reporting"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers market-risk report production and distribution: daily and periodic management and committee reporting, breach and exception reporting, scenario and stress reporting, and controlled inputs to external reporting owned by its accountable processes. Excludes financial reporting and disclosures (Finance, locked rule); excludes regulatory filing ownership (CM-1-2-4-3); excludes credit-risk reporting (CM-1-2-2-1-8); excludes enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream). Manage Risk Reporting (CM-1-2-2-3-13) provides governed market-risk, utilization, breach, position, and profit-and-loss reports to inform Trading Strategy Management (CM-1-2-1-4); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Produce management and committee risk reporting | report breaches, exceptions, and scenario results | distribute on the agreed calendar | provide controlled inputs to external reporting through accountable owners\nOut of scope: Financial reporting and disclosures (Finance) | regulatory filing ownership (CM-1-2-4-3) | credit-risk reporting (CM-1-2-2-1-8) | enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
