   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 19 (2026-09-20). Batch 03 constraint implemented: operational SCM-context forecasting consuming the published forecast as calibration input; legitimate local differences reconcile through governed exception/variance processes, not forced equality (the decision owner, batch 19). Normalized label 'Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand' queued to make the boundary visible. The variance threshold that triggers escalation is an operating-model follow-up carried in the batch 19 PR. APQC 'Forecast IT service demand' is a false lexical match. Step 3d naming pass — scope-ambiguity Batch 1 (A+B+C, 2026-09-21): renamed from 'Forecast Refined Product Demand' to 'Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand'. Prior label(s) retained as altLabel(s): 'Forecast Refined Product Demand'."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20634"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Refined Product Demand"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast refined-product demand operationally for the supply-chain context — projecting short-horizon demand by product, location, and period from lifting history, orders, seasonality, and local market signals, calibrated against the published enterprise forecast — so supply operations and replenishment run on location-level demand projections at operational granularity."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.6.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Forecast Operational Refined Product Demand"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers operational demand forecasting under the batch 03 constraint: short-horizon, location-level projections by product and period for supply operations, replenishment support, and exchange utilization; built from rack lifting history, current orders, seasonality, weather and local market signals; calibrated against the published enterprise forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) and reconciled through governed exception and variance processes where material differences arise — operational forecasts can legitimately differ on local timing, geography, product granularity, and immediate operational signals, and this process consumes the enterprise forecast without producing, revising, republishing, or overriding it. The batch 03 three-way partition: enterprise published forecast at CM-1-1-1-1; trading intake at CM-1-2-1-1-2; operational SCM-context forecasting here. Excludes the enterprise published forecast (CM-1-1-1-1, batch 03); trading forecast intake and forward views (CM-1-2-1-1-2); the refinery-planning demand basis (CM-1-1-4-7-1); feedstock demand (CM-1-2-5-2-2, batch 18).\nIn scope: Project short-horizon demand by product, location, and period | build from lifting history, orders, and local signals | calibrate against the published enterprise forecast and reconcile material differences through governed variance processes | publish operational projections to supply operations and replenishment\nOut of scope: Enterprise published forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) | trading forecast intake (CM-1-2-1-1-2) | refinery demand basis (CM-1-1-4-7-1) | feedstock demand (CM-1-2-5-2-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/weekly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Published enterprise forecast (CM-1-1-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "rack lifting history and orders"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "seasonality and local market signals"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operational location-level demand projections reconciled to the published forecast"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Location-level demand projections at the granularity supply operations actually runs on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19948"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-lnl-t2s-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "S&T Product Supply Fulfillment"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Fulfill approved refined-product replenishment and supply requirements from Supply & Trading sources by coordinating product availability at purchased-supply, exchange, transfer, and third-party source points; confirming feasible supply and transport arrangements; and handing approved movements to the processes that schedule, actualize, and settle them."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 19 (2026-09-20). Q2 decision (the decision owner, Option A with fulfillment language): commercial-source fulfillment and supply coordination — never a parallel scheduling or dispatch organization; 'operate' wording removed because it can imply terminal-operations or dispatch ownership. The product-side mirror of the batch 18 feedstock logistics cluster, complementing the batch 04 replenishment decision and batch 05 distribution scheduling ownerships. Concept-type: process — one fulfillment cycle. APQC candidate is an unrelated internal-operations match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.6.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Supply Operations"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the S&T-sourced supply-fulfillment cycle under the Q2 (Option A) reading: coordinating commercial supply status and availability at source points where Supply And Trading supplies the network — purchased volumes, exchange locations, transfers, third-party terminals (CM-1-2-6-3-1); fulfilling network replenishment requirements from traded sources, consuming the replenishment decisions owned by Manage Inventory Replenishment (CM-1-1-3-7-9, batch 04) (CM-1-2-6-3-2); and coordinating transportation arrangements for S&T-sourced primary movements (CM-1-2-6-3-3). Supply Operations may identify feasible commercial sources and communicate fulfillment constraints, but it does not decide network replenishment quantity or timing, allocate constrained product, execute trades, administer primary movements, or direct physical operations. The complementarity rule: Physical Distribution Scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6, batch 05) owns primary-movement nominations and shipper-side administration; Secondary Distribution Management (CM-1-1-3-8) owns terminal-to-customer delivery; this cluster supplies the network from commercial sources and provides its movements to the owning scheduling, actualization, and settlement processes. Excludes replenishment decisions (CM-1-1-3-7-9, batch 04); allocation decisions (CM-1-1-2); primary movement scheduling and administration (CM-1-1-3-6, batch 05); secondary distribution (CM-1-1-3-8); trade execution (CM-1-2-1-3); exchange agreement administration (CM-1-2-7-1-1); physical terminal and transport operations (operators, carriers, Midstream).\nIn scope: Coordinate commercial supply status at S&T-supplied source points | fulfill approved replenishment requirements from traded, exchanged, and transferred product | confirm feasible supply and transport arrangements | hand approved movements to the owning scheduling, actualization, and settlement processes\nOut of scope: Replenishment decisions (CM-1-1-3-7-9) | allocation decisions (CM-1-1-2) | primary movement scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6) | secondary distribution (CM-1-1-3-8) | trade execution (CM-1-2-1-3) | exchange administration (CM-1-2-7-1-1) | physical operations (operators, carriers, Midstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/weekly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-3-7-9"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Replenishment requirements (CM-1-1-3-7-9)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "agreed purchases and transfers (CM-1-2-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operational demand and exchange plans (CM-1-2-6-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Fulfilled supply requirements handed to the owning scheduling and actualization processes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The network reliably supplied from commercial sources, with every decision right left where earlier batches put it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 19 (2026-09-20). Coordinates-commercial-status, never operates (owner-versus-executor pattern, batch 05): operators run the terminals; this process coordinates the S&T supply interest at them. Normalized label 'Coordinate S&T Source-Point Supply Operations' queued to prevent mistaken inference of physical operations (the decision owner, batch 19). APQC 'Manage treasury operations' is a false lexical match on 'operations'. Step 3d naming pass, authority-risk category (2026-09-21, the decision owner's approval): renamed 'Manage Primary Distribution Operations' -> 'Coordinate S&T Source-Point Supply Operations' — the concept coordinates S&T source-point supply operations; the old label invited mistaken inference of physical operations."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10734"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm32-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Primary Distribution Operations"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate commercial supply status at the source points where Supply And Trading supplies primary distribution — monitoring availability, loading capability, and product quality at purchased-supply, exchange, transfer, and third-party terminal locations, resolving supply issues with operators and counterparties, and keeping source-point status current for replenishment fulfillment and scheduling."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.6.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate S&T Source-Point Supply Operations"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers S&T-side source-point coordination: monitoring product availability, allocation, loading capability, and quality status at locations where the network is supplied from purchases, exchanges, transfers, and third-party terminals; resolving availability, quality, and loading issues with terminal operators, exchange partners, and suppliers; and maintaining current source-point status for replenishment fulfillment (CM-1-2-6-3-2), demand management (CM-1-2-6-2-1), and the scheduling processes. Physical terminal operations belong to the operators; own-refinery rack and terminal operations to Refining and Midstream; movement scheduling to CM-1-1-3-6. Excludes physical terminal operations (operators, Midstream); own-production scheduling and administration (CM-1-1-3-5/-6); terminal contracting (commercial processes); terminal/storage settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14).\nIn scope: Monitor availability, loading capability, and quality at S&T-supplied source points | resolve supply issues with operators and counterparties | keep source-point status current for replenishment fulfillment and scheduling\nOut of scope: Physical terminal operations (operators, Midstream) | own-production scheduling (CM-1-1-3-5/-6) | terminal contracting (commercial processes) | terminal settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source-point status from operators and partners"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "agreed purchases, transfers, and exchange entitlements (CM-1-2-1-3, CM-1-2-7-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "replenishment and demand needs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Current, coordinated source-point supply status"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every S&T-supplied source point ready to load the right product when the network needs it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 19 (2026-09-20). Q2 decision at its sharpest point: the batch 04 decision right ('Manage Inventory Replenishment owns the replenishment decision') is preserved verbatim — this row is the S&T fulfillment counterpart, decide-versus-fulfill mirroring decide-versus-advise. Normalized label 'Fulfill Replenishment From Trading Sources' queued with priority (the decision owner, batch 19: highest naming collision in the batch; names mirror the locked taxonomy, so carried as alt label until the naming pass). APQC 'Manage collaborative replenishment planning' scored STRONG at 3b but NO SOURCE — honored. Step 3d naming pass — scope-ambiguity Batch 1 (A+B+C, 2026-09-21): renamed from 'Manage Replenishment' to 'Fulfill Replenishment From Trading Sources'. Prior label(s) retained as altLabel(s): 'Manage Replenishment'."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10256"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Replenishment"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Fulfill network replenishment requirements from Supply And Trading sources — receiving the replenishment quantities and timing decided by the network replenishment owner, sourcing them from purchased, exchanged, and transferred product where own production does not cover them, and confirming fulfillment plans, constraints, and exceptions back — so replenishment decisions are met without S&T re-deciding them."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.6.3.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Fulfill Replenishment From Trading Sources"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers replenishment fulfillment from commercial sources: receiving replenishment requirements decided by Manage Inventory Replenishment (CM-1-1-3-7-9, batch 04 — that process owns when and how much to resupply each stock point); determining the feasible S&T source — purchased product, exchange liftings (CM-1-2-6-2-2), or transfers — where own production and the regional plan do not cover the requirement; initiating the sourcing through the coordination and trading processes; and confirming fulfillment plans, timing, constraints, and exceptions back to the requirement owner — under supply constraint, fulfillment may differ from the request, and the confirmation returns what is feasible for the owner's decision. This process fulfills, and never makes, the replenishment decision. Excludes the replenishment decision (CM-1-1-3-7-9, batch 04); allocation decisions (CM-1-1-2); trade execution (CM-1-2-1-3); movement scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6); feedstock replenishment (CM-1-2-5, batch 18).\nIn scope: Receive replenishment requirements from the deciding owner | determine the feasible S&T source where own production does not cover | initiate sourcing through coordination and trading processes | confirm fulfillment plans, constraints, and exceptions back to the requirement owner\nOut of scope: Replenishment decisions (CM-1-1-3-7-9, batch 04) | allocation decisions (CM-1-1-2) | trade execution (CM-1-2-1-3) | movement scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6) | feedstock replenishment (CM-1-2-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/daily"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-3-7-9"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Replenishment requirements (CM-1-1-3-7-9)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "available purchases and transfers"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "exchange entitlements (CM-1-2-6-2-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "source-point status (CM-1-2-6-3-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Confirmed fulfillment plans with constraints and exceptions returned to the decision owner"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Fulfill approved replenishment requirements from feasible commercial sources while returning confirmed timing, constraints, and exceptions to the replenishment decision owner."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 19 (2026-09-20). Deterministic handoff (the decision owner, batch 19): confirmed movement requirements go to Physical Distribution Scheduling, which owns primary movement nomination and shipper-side administration (batch 05), and to Actualizations for commercial movement actuals — the handoff is unconditional, making the batch 05 boundary enforceable. Coordinate-not-execute per batch 18. Normalized label 'Coordinate S&T-Sourced Primary Transportation' queued. APQC 'Manage bulk transportation' is a WEAK generic match. Step 3d naming pass — scope-ambiguity Batch 1 (A+B+C, 2026-09-21): renamed from 'Manage Primary Distribution Transportation' to 'Coordinate S&T-Sourced Primary Transportation'. Prior label(s) retained as altLabel(s): 'Manage Primary Distribution Transportation'."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12923"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-doe-rppl-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-orp-dpsc-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Primary Distribution Transportation"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate transportation arrangements for Supply And Trading-sourced primary product movements — pipeline, marine, rail, and truck arrangements under available carrier contracts, capacity, and transport agreements for volumes S&T supplies into the network — providing confirmed movement requirements to the processes that own scheduling and actualization."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.6.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate S&T-Sourced Primary Transportation"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers transportation coordination for S&T-sourced product movements, the product-side counterpart of the batch 18 feedstock transportation cluster: coordinating and monitoring the commercial and logistical arrangements to move S&T-sourced volumes — purchases, exchange liftings, transfers — under carrier contracts (CM-1-2-1-2-9), capacity rights, and transportation deals (CM-1-2-1-3-9); requesting or coordinating nominations, bookings, and carrier actions under the batch 18 coordinate-not-execute rule; tracking status and resolving in-transit issues; and providing the confirmed source, transport, capacity, timing, and commercial-movement requirements to Physical Distribution Scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6), which owns primary movement nomination and shipper-side administration, and to Actualizations (CM-1-2-3-1), which owns commercial movement actuals. Excludes primary movement nomination, scheduling, and shipper-side administration (CM-1-1-3-6, batch 05); carrier contracting (CM-1-2-1-2-9); transportation deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-9); charter-party negotiation and physical transport (marine logistics, carriers); actualization and freight settlement (CM-1-2-3-1, CM-1-2-4-1); secondary distribution (CM-1-1-3-8).\nIn scope: Coordinate transport arrangements for S&T-sourced product movements under existing contracts and capacity | request or coordinate nominations, bookings, and carrier actions | track status and resolve in-transit issues | provide confirmed movement requirements to Physical Distribution Scheduling and Actualizations\nOut of scope: Primary movement nomination and administration (CM-1-1-3-6) | carrier contracting (CM-1-2-1-2-9) | transportation deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-9) | charter negotiation and physical transport (marine logistics, carriers) | actualization and settlement (CM-1-2-3-1, CM-1-2-4-1) | secondary distribution (CM-1-1-3-8)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/cadence/weekly"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-9"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Fulfillment plans (CM-1-2-6-3-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "carrier contracts and capacity (CM-1-2-1-2-9)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "movement status from carriers"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinated transport arrangements with confirmed requirements provided to scheduling and actualization"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "S&T-sourced product moved on managed arrangements, handed unconditionally to the processes that schedule and account for it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Product distribution management involves managing product and transportation agreements, terminal operations."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Products Distribution Management"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12895"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Product Commercial Agreements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiate, maintain commercial requirements for, and coordinate lifecycle changes to product-side agreements that enable product exchanges, customer delivery commitments, and storage/throughput access, so dependent supply, distribution, and settlement processes operate against current commercially agreed terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one agreement-lifecycle discipline across three agreement families (batch 09 pattern). Handoff model (the decision owner, batch 20): negotiation and commercial requirements here; record administration with Contract Management where in trading scope — the two never both 'administer' the same lifecycle. Receiving end of the batch 09 exclusions and the batch 08/14/19 exchange bindings. APQC 'Establish lifting agreements' scored NONE; comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Contractual Agreements Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the commercial-agreement lifecycle for three product-side agreement families: product exchange agreements including their terms, entitlement rules, and contractual imbalance treatment (CM-1-2-7-1-1); customer-facing product transport and delivery agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-2, under the batch 09 boundary rule); and negotiation of storage and throughput agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-3, under the batch 09 storage split). The handoff model: commercial negotiation and commercial-requirement ownership sit in this cluster; legal drafting, legal review, and execution authority with Legal & Corporate Communications under its locked rule; the controlled contract record, document lifecycle, and renewal/termination/novation administration with Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2) where the agreement is within its trading-contract scope; deal capture with Trade Capture (CM-1-2-1-3); operational use with Supply Operations, Distribution, and the relevant operating domains; settlement with Settlements (CM-1-2-4-1). Excludes trading contract administration and the controlled contract record (CM-1-2-1-2); legal services and execution authority (Legal & Corporate Communications, locked rule); deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3); settlement (CM-1-2-4-1); operational exchange utilization (CM-1-2-6-2-2, batch 19). When the approved supply arrangement uses a product-side agreement administered within the source scope, Contractual Agreements Management (CM-1-2-7-1) supplies current exchange, storage/throughput, and customer delivery agreement terms and entitlements that Supply Operations (CM-1-2-6-3) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Negotiate product exchange agreements with entitlement and imbalance terms | negotiate and maintain commercial requirements for customer-facing delivery agreements | negotiate storage and throughput agreements | coordinate lifecycle changes and keep dependent processes supplied with current terms\nOut of scope: Contract record and lifecycle administration (CM-1-2-1-2) | legal services and execution authority (Legal & Corporate Communications, locked rule) | deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3) | settlement (CM-1-2-4-1) | operational exchange utilization (CM-1-2-6-2-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial requirements from demand, supply, and network processes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty proposals"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "legal review (Legal & Corporate Communications)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiated product-side commercial agreements with maintained commercial requirements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every exchange, delivery, and storage arrangement running on current, correct, commercially negotiated terms."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16630"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiate and administer product exchange agreements — the terms under which product is exchanged with other suppliers across locations and time — owning the entitlement rules, differentials, and contractual imbalance calculation and treatment, and recommending or making delegated commercial decisions on imbalance resolution, so exchange supply operates against governed agreements with controlled balances."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Receiving row of six bindings (batches 08/09/14/18/19): 'not product exchange agreements' (futures split, b08); imbalance treatment administered here (b14); contractual imbalance calculation, commercial decision, agreement administration, and settlement conditions here versus operational visibility at CM-1-2-6-2-2 (b19). Delegated-authority rule (the decision owner, batch 20): imbalance remedies are recommended or decided within the documented delegation and the governing agreement, respecting authority thresholds, Finance impact, and Legal review. The entitlement, not a parcel, is the governed object (b13 entitlement concept). APQC 'Manage product images' is a false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Product Exchange Agreements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the exchange-agreement lifecycle: negotiating exchange agreements with counterparty suppliers — locations, products, volumes, differentials and location/quality adjustments, entitlement rules, imbalance provisions, and termination terms; administering agreements through amendments and renewals; performing the contractual imbalance calculation and treatment the agreements provide (batch 14 binding); recommending or making delegated commercial decisions on imbalance resolution, make-up, cash-out, or other contractual remedies under the governing agreement — authority thresholds, Finance impact, and Legal review apply per the documented delegation; and supplying entitlement and position data to the operational utilization process. The batch 19 split: operational visibility and proposed utilization at Manage Refined Product Exchanges (CM-1-2-6-2-2); contractual calculation and commercial decisions here. 'Exchange' means product exchange arrangements, not futures exchanges (CM-1-2-1-3-4, batch 08). Exchange settlement executes per the agreements at Settlements (CM-1-2-4-1-2, batch 14). Excludes operational utilization planning (CM-1-2-6-2-2); futures-exchange trading (CM-1-2-1-3-4); settlement execution (CM-1-2-4-1); legal drafting and execution authority (Legal & Corporate Communications); movement scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6). Manage Product Exchange Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-1) maintains exchange-agreement entitlement rules, differentials, and imbalance terms within which Manage Refined Product Exchanges (CM-1-2-6-2-2) operates; the recipient retains its other decisions and authorities.\nIn scope: Negotiate exchange agreements with entitlement, differential, and imbalance terms | administer amendments and renewals | perform contractual imbalance calculation and treatment and recommend or make delegated decisions on remedies | supply entitlement and position data to operational utilization\nOut of scope: Operational utilization (CM-1-2-6-2-2) | futures-exchange trading (CM-1-2-1-3-4) | settlement execution (CM-1-2-4-1) | legal drafting and execution (Legal & Corporate Communications) | movement scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exchange requirements from demand and supply processes (CM-1-2-6-2-2, CM-1-2-6-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty proposals"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "lifted and delivered volumes (CM-1-2-3-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-4-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed exchange agreements with calculated balances, delegated decisions, and current entitlement data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exchange supply governed by sound agreements, with every balance calculated, decided under the right authority, and controlled under contract."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16630"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-gloss-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiate and administer customer-facing product transport and delivery agreements — the delivery terms linked to product sale and marketing arrangements, including delivered pricing bases, delivery service commitments, and receiving requirements — so product deliveries to customers operate against current, correct commercial delivery terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Receiving row of the batch 09 boundary rule with the decision owner's classification test recorded verbatim: the agreement's commercial purpose decides — capacity/rates for supply movements versus part of a product-sale commitment — never the transport mode alone. APQC 'Manage product images' is a false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Product Transport Agreements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the customer-facing side of the batch 09 boundary rule: negotiating and administering the transport and delivery agreements connected to product sale and marketing arrangements — delivered-price and freight bases, delivery windows and service commitments, receiving-facility requirements, and delivery-related liability terms — through amendments and renewals, keeping order management, secondary distribution, and settlement supplied with current terms. The classification test is the agreement's commercial purpose, not the physical transport mode: a truck contract can be a carrier agreement when it procures capacity or rates for supply movements (Manage Carrier Contracts, CM-1-2-1-2-9), or a customer-facing delivery agreement when it forms part of a product-sale commitment (here) — the batch 09 rule applied to every mode. Excludes carrier contracts for supply and trading movements (CM-1-2-1-2-9, batch 09 rule); customer order capture and fulfillment (CM-1-3-7); secondary delivery scheduling (CM-1-1-3-8); legal drafting and execution (Legal & Corporate Communications); transportation deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-9). When the scheduled delivery is covered by a customer-facing transport agreement administered by the source, Manage Product Transport Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-2) supplies current customer-facing delivery windows, receiving requirements, and service commitments that Secondary Distribution Management (CM-1-1-3-8) consumes in its defined work. When the settlement includes customer-facing delivery terms administered by the source, Manage Product Transport Agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-2) supplies current customer delivery, delivered-price, freight, and receiving terms that Settlements (CM-1-2-4-1) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Negotiate customer-facing delivery and transport terms linked to product sales | administer amendments and renewals | maintain delivered-price, service, and receiving terms | keep order, distribution, and settlement processes supplied with current terms\nOut of scope: Carrier contracts for supply/trading movements (CM-1-2-1-2-9) | order capture and fulfillment (CM-1-3-7) | secondary delivery scheduling (CM-1-1-3-8) | legal drafting and execution (Legal & Corporate Communications) | transportation deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-9)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Product sale and marketing arrangements (CM-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty and customer proposals"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "delivery capability and cost data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Administered customer-facing transport and delivery agreements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every customer delivery running on negotiated, current delivery terms."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10815"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm32-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiate storage and throughput agreements — leased tankage, cavern capacity, terminal throughput, and handling arrangements — establishing capacity, fee structures, service levels, and quality-protection terms, obtaining required commercial approvals, coordinating execution through Legal and authorized signatories, and handing executed agreements to the contract record and deal capture, so storage and throughput capacity is secured on sound commercial terms."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Receiving row of the batch 09 three-way storage split, applied verbatim, with the decision owner's execution correction: this process obtains commercial approvals and coordinates execution; Legal and authorized signatories execute. The batch 09 capture caveat retained: a captured storage deal exists only where capacity is commercially distinct. APQC 'Negotiate service-level agreements' is a WEAK IT candidate."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiate Storage / Throughput Agreements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the negotiation position in the batch 09 storage split: identifying storage and throughput needs with the supply and trading processes; negotiating capacity, term, fee structures (throughput, storage, blending, handling, minimums), service levels, and quality-protection provisions; obtaining required commercial approvals and coordinating execution of the agreement through Legal and authorized signatories — execution authority remains with Legal & Corporate Communications and the authorized signatories, not this process. On execution the agreement hands off per the split: the contract record is maintained by Manage Storage Contract (CM-1-2-1-2-10); commercially distinct capacity transactions are captured by Capture Storage Deals (CM-1-2-1-3-5) — per the batch 09 caveat, not every storage agreement results in a separately captured deal, only where capacity is commercially distinct, traded, allocated, acquired, released, or modeled as a transaction; company stock in third-party facilities is administered by Manage Third Party Storage (CM-1-1-3-7-11); charges settle at Settle Terminal/Storage (CM-1-2-4-1-14). Excludes contract record administration (CM-1-2-1-2-10); capacity deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-5); third-party storage inventory administration (CM-1-1-3-7-11); storage settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14); legal drafting and execution authority (Legal & Corporate Communications).\nIn scope: Identify storage and throughput needs with supply and trading processes | negotiate capacity, fees, service levels, and quality-protection terms | obtain commercial approvals and coordinate execution through Legal and authorized signatories | hand executed agreements to the contract record and deal capture\nOut of scope: Contract record administration (CM-1-2-1-2-10) | capacity deal capture (CM-1-2-1-3-5) | third-party storage administration (CM-1-1-3-7-11) | storage settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14) | legal drafting and execution authority (Legal & Corporate Communications)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Capacity needs from supply, trading, and network processes"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market capacity availability and rates"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "quality-protection requirements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-2-10"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-1-3-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Executed storage and throughput agreements handed to record and capture"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Storage and throughput capacity secured when needed, on terms that protect product and economics."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19948"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm32-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-osha-psm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Company-Managed Terminal & Fleet Operations"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The capability to operate and maintain company-managed marketing and distribution terminals, loading facilities, and associated distribution fleet assets where the business unit is the designated operating entity, including site safety execution, fleet capability management, and site-asset integrity and availability."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Q2 decision (the decision owner, narrowed): this capability applies where the company is the designated operator — never categorically 'the terminal operator', since the same legal entity may own a facility operated by a third party, Midstream, Refining, a joint venture, or a terminal services company. Every prior operator exclusion is preserved: for facilities operated elsewhere, the operator remains external to this cluster. Concept-type: capability per the batch 11 test. Which terminals, tanks, racks, and fleet assets are actually company-managed by Marketing/Distribution is an asset-inventory follow-up carried in the batch 20 PR. APQC 'Analyze internal operations' scored NONE; comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Terminal Operations Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the management of company-managed marketing and distribution terminal and fleet operations under the Q2 reading: site safety management (CM-1-2-7-2-1), fleet management (CM-1-2-7-2-2), and site asset management (CM-1-2-7-2-3), applied where the Marketing/Distribution business is the designated operating entity. Asset ownership alone does not determine scope: this capability applies only where the Marketing/Distribution business is operationally accountable for the site or fleet — Refining-operated, Midstream-operated, third-party-operated, and centrally operated assets remain with their designated operating domains or providers, and where the company owns but does not operate a facility, its interest is held through agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-3), source-point coordination (CM-1-2-6-3-1), storage administration (CM-1-1-3-7-11), and settlement (CM-1-2-4-1-14). The capability is located in the Supply & Trading taxonomy because it supports marketing/distribution supply operations; its operational delivery may sit in a dedicated terminal operations, distribution operations, fleet, Midstream, engineering, or shared-services organization, depending on asset ownership and operating accountability. Scheduling remains with its owners (CM-1-1-3-6, CM-1-1-3-8, batch 05); EHS policy, regulatory reporting, and filings with EHS & Government Reporting under its locked rule. Excludes Refining-, Midstream-, centrally-, and third-party-operated assets (their designated operators, locked rules); movement and delivery scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6, CM-1-1-3-8); EHS policy and regulatory reporting (EHS & Government Reporting, locked rule); storage/terminal commercial agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-3).\nIn scope: Operate site safety programs within the enterprise EHS framework at company-managed sites | manage own and contracted fleet capability and compliance | manage site-asset integrity coordination and availability | keep company-managed operations safe, compliant, and available\nOut of scope: Refining-, Midstream-, centrally-, and third-party-operated assets (designated operators, locked rules) | movement and delivery scheduling (CM-1-1-3-6, CM-1-1-3-8) | EHS policy and regulatory reporting (EHS & Government Reporting, locked rule) | storage/terminal agreements (CM-1-2-7-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/capability"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Enterprise EHS framework and policies"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "fleet and asset condition data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "supply and distribution requirements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Safely and compliantly operated company-managed terminals and fleet"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Company-managed terminals and fleet that are safe, compliant, and reliably available."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11741"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm32-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-osha-psm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operate the safety programs at company-managed terminal and fleet operations — hazardous-materials handling safety, staff safety training and procedures, and contractor safety qualification and control — executing the enterprise EHS framework at site level, so people and operations at company-managed facilities are protected and compliant."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Q3 decision with the decision owner's incident split: the site executes response, gathers facts, notifies, and executes corrective actions; EHS governs investigation method, assesses reportability, and reports — execution versus accountability. Process-safety phrasing conditioned: applicable regimes (such as OSHA PSM where regulated substances meet threshold conditions) are executed within the enterprise EHS/process-safety framework; jurisdiction-specific. Executes-within-policy (batch 07/11/15 pattern). APQC 'Manage materials master lists' is a false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Safety (Materials, Staff, Contractor)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers line-management safety execution at company-managed sites: hazardous-materials handling and storage safety procedures for the products handled; staff safety training, competence, and procedure compliance; contractor safety qualification, induction, and work control; site safety inspections and observations; participating in site incident response, fact gathering, initial notification, and corrective-action execution, and providing required incident information to EHS for governed investigation, reportability assessment, and regulatory reporting. Where an operation is subject to applicable process-safety regulations or standards — such as OSHA PSM in the United States where regulated substances meet threshold conditions — the site executes applicable operating controls within the enterprise EHS/process-safety framework. Executes-within-framework: EHS & Government Reporting owns safety policy, the EHS management framework, investigation governance, reportability assessment, regulatory reporting, and filings under its locked rule; this process operates the programs at site level and feeds it. Excludes EHS policy, framework, investigation governance, reportability assessment, and regulatory reporting (EHS & Government Reporting, locked rule); separately established emergency-response ownership; third-party site safety (their operators); fleet transport-safety compliance administration (CM-1-2-7-2-2).\nIn scope: Operate hazardous-materials handling safety procedures | run staff safety training and procedure compliance | qualify, induct, and control contractors | participate in incident response and provide required incident information to EHS\nOut of scope: EHS policy, investigation governance, reportability assessment, and regulatory reporting (EHS & Government Reporting, locked rule) | separately established emergency-response ownership | third-party site safety (their operators) | fleet transport-safety administration (CM-1-2-7-2-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Enterprise EHS framework and policies"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "contractor and staff records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "site hazard and product data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operated site safety programs with incident information and evidence into the EHS framework"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Nobody hurt, nothing released, everything evidenced — at every company-managed site."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12944"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-ei-hm32-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-fmcsa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage the capacity, readiness, safety, compliance, maintenance, and performance of company-operated and contracted road-delivery fleet resources so Secondary Distribution Management can assign safe, qualified, and available vehicles and carriers to approved delivery schedules."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). The decision owner's consistency correction applied: where the company operates its own fleet, this function's vehicles and drivers execute the scheduled deliveries — execution is not categorically excluded; what stays excluded is the scheduling and dispatch decision (CM-1-1-3-8, batch 05 split). US transport-safety context spans two regimes: FMCSA motor-carrier safety regulations and PHMSA hazardous-materials/cargo-tank rules — different agencies; state, hours-of-service, CDL, drug/alcohol, inspection, and insurance requirements apply additionally; jurisdiction-specific elsewhere. Dispatch execution ownership after scheduling is an operating-model follow-up carried in the batch 20 PR. APQC 'Manage third party bulk storage' scored STRONG at 3b but NO SOURCE — honored; storage candidate, not fleet."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Fleet (Own/Third Party)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers fleet management for product distribution: fleet-capacity planning; vehicle standards, inspections, and maintenance-program governance; driver qualification and safety compliance; carrier qualification and carrier-performance management; transport-safety and hazardous-materials compliance programs (in the United States, the FMCSA motor-carrier safety regime under 49 CFR Parts 300-399 and the applicable PHMSA Hazardous Materials Regulations for cargo tanks; state and jurisdictional requirements additional); and fleet readiness. Where the company operates its own fleet, it provides the vehicles and drivers that execute scheduled deliveries; where third parties operate the fleet, it manages contractual qualification and performance. Route, load, and delivery-window scheduling and dispatch decisioning remain with Secondary Distribution Management (CM-1-1-3-8, batch 05). Excludes route, load, and delivery-window scheduling and dispatch decisioning (CM-1-1-3-8); customer order capture (CM-1-3-7); carrier contract negotiation where that belongs to Contract Management (CM-1-2-1-2-9); customer delivery terms (CM-1-2-7-1-2); marine, rail, and pipeline capacity (their owning processes); fleet financing and capital decisions (Finance, accountable owners); settlement (CM-1-2-4-1).\nIn scope: Plan fleet capacity across own and contracted resources | govern vehicle standards, inspections, and maintenance programs | administer driver qualification and transport-safety compliance | qualify and manage carriers and provide execution-ready fleet resources to scheduling\nOut of scope: Route, load, and dispatch scheduling (CM-1-1-3-8) | order capture (CM-1-3-7) | carrier contract negotiation (CM-1-2-1-2-9) | customer delivery terms (CM-1-2-7-1-2) | marine, rail, and pipeline capacity (owning processes) | fleet financing and capital decisions (Finance, accountable owners)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Delivery demand and schedules (CM-1-1-3-8)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "applicable transport regulations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "driver and carrier records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "vehicle condition and compliance data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Execution-ready, compliant fleet capacity assigned through scheduling"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A safe, compliant, available fleet behind every scheduled delivery — driving it where the company operates it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/13930"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-api-653-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-api-mpms-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-7-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage the operational availability, condition, integrity coordination, and business-use allocation of company-managed marketing and distribution terminal assets — including tanks, racks, meters, additive systems, vapor-recovery equipment, and supporting infrastructure — within enterprise engineering, maintenance, and EHS standards."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 20 (2026-09-20). Coordinates-integrity-and-availability (the decision owner, batch 20): the process coordinates with accountable engineering and maintenance providers and maintains business-use configuration; standards, certification, methodology, and capital stay with their owners. API 653 anchors in-service aboveground storage tank inspection practice for API 650/12C-constructed tanks; applicability is tank- and jurisdiction-specific and the enterprise's engineering standards govern. Whether this row owns business-use allocation or only maintains availability data for a scheduling owner is an operating-model follow-up carried in the batch 20 PR. APQC 'Manage rack allocations' is a WEAK partial match, comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.2.7.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Site Assets (Tank, Rack, Etc.)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers site asset management at company-managed terminals: asset registers and condition monitoring; coordinating inspection, maintenance, and integrity requirements with the accountable engineering and maintenance providers (in-service aboveground storage tank inspection follows API 653 practice where applicable; measurement equipment per the applicable API MPMS chapters); maintenance planning with operations; maintaining business-use configuration and availability information for racks, bays, tanks, and associated assets and coordinating operational allocation with the designated terminal and scheduling owners; and asset performance and availability management. The process coordinates inspection, maintenance, and integrity requirements with accountable engineering and maintenance providers; it does not itself establish engineering standards, approve technical integrity methodology, perform regulated inspection certification, own capital-project decisions, or define measurement methodology. Excludes engineering standards and integrity methodology (enterprise engineering function); regulated inspection certification (certified inspectors/providers); capital investment decisions and projects (enterprise capital process, accountable owners); Refining- and Midstream-operated assets (locked rules); measurement methodology (CM-1-1-3-7-4); site safety programs (CM-1-2-7-2-1).\nIn scope: Maintain asset registers and condition monitoring | coordinate inspection, maintenance, and integrity requirements with accountable engineering and maintenance providers | plan maintenance with operations | maintain business-use configuration and availability information and coordinate allocation with designated owners\nOut of scope: Engineering standards and integrity methodology (enterprise engineering) | regulated inspection certification (certified providers) | capital decisions and projects (enterprise capital process) | Refining/Midstream assets (locked rules) | measurement methodology (CM-1-1-3-7-4) | site safety programs (CM-1-2-7-2-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Asset condition and inspection data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "engineering and maintenance provider programs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operations requirements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "product allocation needs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Available, integrity-coordinated site assets with maintained business-use configuration"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every tank, rack, and meter at company-managed sites fit for service when operations needs it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Marketing Includes Processes Such As Performing Market Analysis, Developing Marketing Strategy, New Product Development, Managing Retail Marketing Operations. It Includes Processes Required To Take The Products & Services From Strategic Conception, Through Planning To Operational Execution."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 2
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market analysis & insight process determines market attractiveness & identifies evolving opportunities & threats as to the industry in general & company specifically."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market Analysis & Insight"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10106"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-steo-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze the downstream product markets the company serves or could serve — market size, demand and supply balances, channel structure, margin pools, and regulatory and structural change — through a recurring, governed analysis cycle, so marketing strategy and planning decisions rest on a current, evidenced view of the market."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one four-step analysis lifecycle (the batch 08 variant pattern; this cluster is the template's first instance), confirmed in review. Lifecycle order normalized per review: Define Objectives & Scope precedes Source & Collect Information precedes Analyze Data precedes Document Findings. Market data for US fuels marketing is anchored by EIA's Petroleum Marketing Monthly and STEO within their US-only, survey-category limitations; vendor data under its licensing terms (batch 12 follow-up). Batch 21 durable rule (review): \"Marketing Analysis produces governed evidence, insight, hypotheses, and recommendations. It does not itself set strategy, approve investments, establish prices, allocate product, publish the enterprise forecast, define enterprise KPIs, make commercial offers, or execute campaigns.\" APQC candidate is a WEAK generic intelligence match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring market-analysis lifecycle for downstream fuels and products markets: sourcing market data (CM-1-3-1-1-1), defining each cycle's objectives and scope (CM-1-3-1-1-2), analyzing market size, demand and supply, channel structure, pricing environments, and margin pools (CM-1-3-1-1-3), and documenting governed findings (CM-1-3-1-1-4). Analyze-and-inform: strategy decisions belong to the strategy and planning branches (CM-1-3-2/3/5); the enterprise demand forecast to Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1, batch 03); supply-network economics to CM-1-2-6-1 (batch 19 four-lens rule); enterprise KPI definition to the KPI workstream. Excludes strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3); demand forecast production (CM-1-1-1-1); supply-economics analysis (CM-1-2-6-1); KPI definition (KPI workstream); competitor-specific analysis (CM-1-3-1-5). Market Analysis (CM-1-3-1-1) provides governed downstream market balances, channel structure, margins, and structural-change findings to inform Brand Strategy (CM-1-3-2-1); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Run the recurring market-analysis cycle | analyze market size, demand-supply, channels, and margin pools | maintain a current evidenced market view | feed strategy, planning, and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship\nOut of scope: Strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3) | demand forecast production (CM-1-1-1-1) | supply-economics analysis (CM-1-2-6-1) | KPI definition (KPI workstream) | competitor analysis (CM-1-3-1-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Government and industry market data (EIA PMM/STEO)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "internal sales and channel data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "licensed vendor data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed market-analysis findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A current, evidenced market view under every marketing decision."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10195"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source and collect the market data the market-analysis cycle needs — government statistics, licensed market data, industry publications, and internal sales and channel data — qualifying sources, respecting licensing terms, and organizing collected data for analysis."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Sourcing step of the shared analysis lifecycle, market instance. Licensed data used within its terms — the licensing owner question stands (batch 12). APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source & Collect Information"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers market-data sourcing: identifying and qualifying sources for market size, demand, supply, price, and channel data; collecting under the applicable licensing and use terms; recording provenance and currency; and organizing data for the analysis step (CM-1-3-1-1-3). Data-vendor selection and licensing ownership follow the batch 12 follow-up owner; enterprise data governance frameworks apply where established. Excludes the analysis itself (CM-1-3-1-1-3); vendor licensing ownership (accountable owner per batch 12 follow-up); enterprise data governance (its owner).\nIn scope: Identify and qualify market data sources | collect under licensing and use terms | record provenance and currency | organize data for analysis\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-1-3) | vendor licensing ownership (batch 12 follow-up owner) | enterprise data governance (its owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Government statistics (EIA)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "internal sales and channel records"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "licensed vendor data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified, organized market data with provenance"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The right market data, legitimately sourced, ready to analyze."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19521"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define each market-analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which markets, products, channels, and periods, answering which decisions — so analysis effort lands on the questions strategy and planning actually need answered."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Framing step of the shared lifecycle, market instance — the lifecycle's first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' scored STRONG at 3b but NO SOURCE — honored; generic-step match, comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers analysis framing: agreeing the cycle's decision-supporting questions with the strategy, planning, and commercial consumers; setting market, product, channel, geography, and period scope; selecting methods and required data; and setting the cycle's deliverable and timing. The consumers own their decisions; this step owns the framing. Excludes the decisions the analysis supports (consumers); the analysis itself (CM-1-3-1-1-3); data collection (CM-1-3-1-1-1).\nIn scope: Agree decision-supporting questions with consumers | set market, product, channel, and period scope | select methods and required data | set deliverables and timing\nOut of scope: The supported decisions (consumers) | analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-1-3) | data collection (CM-1-3-1-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer decision needs (CM-1-3-2/3/5)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "available data inventory"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreed analysis objectives, scope, and method per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analysis aimed at real decisions, not analysis for its own sake."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20962"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze the collected market data against the defined objectives — market sizing, demand and supply balance, channel and margin structure, trend and scenario analysis — producing evidenced analytical results with their assumptions and confidence stated."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Analysis step of the shared lifecycle, market instance. APQC 'Analyze data' scored STRONG at 3b but NO SOURCE — honored; generic-step match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Data"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers market-analysis execution: applying the defined methods to the qualified data; sizing markets and segments; analyzing demand-supply balances, channel structures, pricing environments, and margin pools; testing trends and scenarios; and stating assumptions, limitations, and confidence with the results. Results are analytical inputs to decisions, not decisions; forecast production stays with CM-1-1-1-1. Excludes decision-making (consumers); demand forecast production (CM-1-1-1-1); documentation and distribution (CM-1-3-1-1-4).\nIn scope: Apply defined methods to qualified data | size markets and analyze demand-supply, channels, and margins | test trends and scenarios | state assumptions, limitations, and confidence\nOut of scope: Decisions (consumers) | forecast production (CM-1-1-1-1) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified data (CM-1-3-1-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "objectives and methods (CM-1-3-1-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced market-analysis results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced answers to the framed questions, with honesty about confidence."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/14095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document and distribute the market-analysis findings — governed findings records with their evidence, assumptions, and confidence — to the consuming strategy, planning, and insight processes, maintaining the findings library so analysis is reusable and auditable."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Documentation step of the shared lifecycle, market instance; the shared evidence-lineage statement (review) applies. APQC 'Document trade' is a false lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document Findings"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers findings documentation: producing the governed findings record with evidence, assumptions, limitations, and confidence; distributing to the agreed consumers and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6); and maintaining the findings library with versioning and currency. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis itself (CM-1-3-1-1-3); the consumers' decisions; enterprise records-retention policy (governance owner). Document Findings (CM-1-3-1-1-4) supplies governed market-analysis findings with evidence, assumptions, limitations, and confidence that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Produce governed findings records with evidence and confidence | distribute to agreed consumers and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship | maintain the versioned findings library\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-1-3) | consumer decisions | records-retention policy (governance owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "distribution agreements with consumers"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed, distributed market findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Findings that outlive the meeting — governed, evidenced, findable."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/13169"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze the company's own position and performance in its downstream markets — market share, portfolio and asset position, capability strengths and gaps, and performance against the market, using approved internal data, external benchmarks, and stated comparability assumptions — through a recurring, governed analysis cycle, so strategy is built on an honest view of where the company stands."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Q2 partition: the company's own position and performance — the self-analysis lens; competitor conduct sits at CM-1-3-1-5 and market structure at CM-1-3-1-1. Data-quality qualifier added in review: approved internal data, external benchmarks, and stated comparability assumptions. Shared lifecycle, second instance; normalized order applies. Batch 21 durable rule (review): \"Marketing Analysis produces governed evidence, insight, hypotheses, and recommendations. It does not itself set strategy, approve investments, establish prices, allocate product, publish the enterprise forecast, define enterprise KPIs, make commercial offers, or execute campaigns.\" APQC candidate is a WEAK pricing match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Company Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring company-analysis lifecycle: sourcing internal performance, share, portfolio, and capability data alongside market benchmarks (CM-1-3-1-2-1); framing each cycle's questions (CM-1-3-1-2-2); analyzing share, position, capability, and relative performance (CM-1-3-1-2-3); and documenting governed findings (CM-1-3-1-2-4). Uses governed financial and operational data from its accountable owners (Accounting, batch 15; operations processes); it analyzes position, it does not produce financial results or decide strategy. Share and comparative-performance conclusions state their category definitions, data coverage, channel coverage, geographic scope, and comparability assumptions. Excludes strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3); financial reporting production (CM-1-2-4-2, Finance); cost-to-serve analysis (CM-1-2-6-1-3, batch 19); competitor analysis (CM-1-3-1-5); KPI definition (KPI workstream). Company Analysis (CM-1-3-1-2) supplies governed company-analysis findings and evidence lineage that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work. Company Analysis (CM-1-3-1-2) provides company market-share, capability-gap, portfolio-position, and relative-performance findings to inform Brand Strategy (CM-1-3-2-1); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Run the recurring company-analysis cycle | analyze share, portfolio, capability, and relative performance | maintain an honest evidenced self-view | feed strategy and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship\nOut of scope: Strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3) | financial reporting (CM-1-2-4-2, Finance) | cost-to-serve (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | competitor analysis (CM-1-3-1-5) | KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed financial and operational data (CM-1-2-4-2, operations)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "capability assessments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "share and benchmark data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed company-position findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Strategy built on where the company actually stands, not where it hopes it stands."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10195"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source and collect the data the company-analysis cycle needs — governed internal financial, volume, share, and capability data, and the external benchmarks to compare against — respecting the data owners' controls and organizing the data for analysis."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, company instance — consumes governed data, never produces it. APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source & Collect Information"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers company-analysis sourcing: internal performance, volume, margin, portfolio, and capability data from their accountable owners; external share and benchmark data under licensing terms; provenance and currency recording; organization for analysis (CM-1-3-1-2-3). Excludes producing the internal data (its owners); the analysis (CM-1-3-1-2-3); vendor licensing ownership (batch 12 follow-up owner).\nIn scope: Collect governed internal performance and capability data | collect external benchmarks under licensing terms | record provenance and organize for analysis\nOut of scope: Internal data production (accountable owners) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-2-3) | licensing ownership (batch 12 follow-up owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed internal data (CM-1-2-4-2, operations)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "licensed benchmarks"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified, organized company and benchmark data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The company's own numbers and fair benchmarks, ready to analyze."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19521"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define each company-analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which businesses, markets, capabilities, and periods, answering which strategic questions — so self-analysis lands where strategy needs it."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, company instance — first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers framing for company analysis: agreeing decision-supporting questions with strategy and planning consumers; setting business, market, capability, and period scope; selecting methods and benchmarks; setting deliverables and timing. Excludes the supported decisions (consumers); analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-2-3); data collection (CM-1-3-1-2-1).\nIn scope: Agree strategic questions with consumers | set business, market, capability, and period scope | select methods and benchmarks | set deliverables and timing\nOut of scope: Supported decisions (consumers) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-2-3) | collection (CM-1-3-1-2-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer decision needs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "data inventory"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreed objectives, scope, and method per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Self-analysis aimed at strategy's real questions."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20962"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze the company's position against the defined objectives — share and share-trend analysis, portfolio and asset-position assessment, capability strengths and gaps, and performance versus market and benchmarks — producing evidenced results with assumptions and confidence stated."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, company instance; comparability assumptions stated with results (review qualifier). APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Data"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers company-analysis execution: share and trend computation; portfolio and asset-position assessment; capability strength/gap analysis against market requirements; relative-performance analysis against benchmarks; assumptions, limitations, and confidence stated, including category definitions, data coverage, and comparability assumptions behind share and performance conclusions. Excludes decisions (consumers); financial result production (CM-1-2-4-2, Finance); documentation (CM-1-3-1-2-4).\nIn scope: Compute share and trends | assess portfolio and asset position | analyze capability strengths and gaps | benchmark relative performance with stated confidence\nOut of scope: Decisions (consumers) | financial production (CM-1-2-4-2) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-2-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified data (CM-1-3-1-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "objectives (CM-1-3-1-2-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced company-position results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "An honest, evidenced answer to how the company is really positioned."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/14095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document and distribute the company-analysis findings — governed records with evidence, assumptions, and confidence — to strategy, planning, and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship, maintaining the findings library."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, company instance; internal-assessment classification respected; shared evidence-lineage statement applies. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.2.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document Findings"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers findings documentation for company analysis: governed records with evidence and confidence; distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Sensitive internal assessments distribute per their classification. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-2-3); consumer decisions; records-retention policy (governance owner). Document Findings (CM-1-3-1-2-4) supplies governed company-analysis findings with evidence, assumptions, limitations, and confidence that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Produce governed findings records | distribute per classification to agreed consumers | maintain the versioned library\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-2-3) | decisions (consumers) | retention policy (governance owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-2-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "classification rules"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed, distributed company findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Self-knowledge that is governed, findable, and appropriately protected."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/13169"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze end-consumer behavior in the company's downstream markets — needs, preferences, buying patterns, journey and experience drivers, and segment dynamics — through a recurring, governed analysis cycle operating within the applicable privacy frameworks, so consumer-facing strategy rests on evidenced consumer understanding."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Q2 partition: end consumers here; direct customers and branded marketers at CM-1-3-1-4 — the B2C/B2B lens split. Q3 review enhancement: the shared personal-data governance statement (verbatim in scope note) replaces the general privacy wording — analysis within approved controls is distinguished from ownership of privacy policy, consent, rights, security, and retention. Shared lifecycle, third instance; normalized order applies. Batch 21 durable rule (review): \"Marketing Analysis produces governed evidence, insight, hypotheses, and recommendations. It does not itself set strategy, approve investments, establish prices, allocate product, publish the enterprise forecast, define enterprise KPIs, make commercial offers, or execute campaigns.\" APQC candidate is a WEAK pricing match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring consumer-analysis lifecycle: sourcing consumer research, transaction, loyalty, and market data within privacy and consent constraints (CM-1-3-1-3-1); framing cycles (CM-1-3-1-3-2); analyzing needs, behavior, journeys, and segment dynamics (CM-1-3-1-3-3); documenting governed findings (CM-1-3-1-3-4). 'Consumer' means the end consumer (retail/B2C); direct customers and branded marketers are analyzed at CM-1-3-1-4. Personal, customer, loyalty, transaction, and behavioral data may be sourced and analyzed only for approved purposes, under the applicable lawful basis, notice/consent status where required, retention rules, access controls, data-minimization requirements, and privacy/security classifications established by the accountable Data Governance, Privacy, Legal, and Security owners. Analysis operates within these controls; it does not own privacy policy, consent and notice management, data-subject rights, data security, retention/deletion execution, or marketing-execution use of personal data. Excludes customer and marketer analysis (CM-1-3-1-4); consumer strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2-3, CM-1-3-2-5); privacy framework ownership (accountable governance owners); loyalty program operation (CM-1-3-6-6). Consumer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-3) provides consumer insight that informs Consumer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-3). Consumer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-3) supplies governed consumer-analysis findings and evidence lineage that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Run the recurring consumer-analysis cycle within privacy frameworks | analyze needs, behavior, journeys, and segments | maintain evidenced consumer understanding | feed consumer strategy and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship\nOut of scope: Customer/marketer analysis (CM-1-3-1-4) | strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2-3/-5) | privacy framework ownership and consent, rights, security, and retention operations (governance owners) | loyalty operation (CM-1-3-6-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer research and panels"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market and demographic data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "transaction and loyalty data within consent"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed consumer-analysis findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer-facing decisions built on evidenced, lawfully obtained consumer understanding."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10195"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source and collect the consumer data the analysis cycle needs — research studies, panels, transaction and loyalty data, and demographic and market data — within consent, privacy, and licensing constraints, and organize it for analysis."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, consumer instance — consent basis recorded with the data; the cluster's shared personal-data governance statement governs sourcing. APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source & Collect Information"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers consumer-data sourcing: research commissioning inputs, panel and study data, transaction and loyalty data used within its consent basis, demographic and market data; provenance, consent-basis, and currency recording; organization for analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3). Sourcing operates under the shared personal-data governance statement recorded at CM-1-3-1-3: approved purposes, lawful basis, notice/consent status, retention, access, and minimization controls set by the accountable Data Governance, Privacy, Legal, and Security owners. Excludes privacy framework ownership (governance owners); the analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3); loyalty program data operations (CM-1-3-6-6).\nIn scope: Collect research, panel, transaction, and demographic data within consent and licensing | record provenance and consent basis | organize for analysis\nOut of scope: Privacy framework ownership (governance owners) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3) | loyalty data operations (CM-1-3-6-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Research and panel data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "consented transaction/loyalty data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "demographic data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified consumer data with provenance and consent basis"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer data that is useful and lawful, ready to analyze."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19521"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define each consumer-analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which segments, behaviors, journeys, and markets, answering which proposition and experience questions — so consumer research answers real decisions."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, consumer instance — first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.3.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers framing for consumer analysis: agreeing decision-supporting questions with proposition, experience, and planning consumers; setting segment, behavior, journey, geography, and period scope; selecting methods including research design needs; setting deliverables and timing. Excludes the supported decisions (consumers); analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-3-3); research fieldwork procurement (per the operating model).\nIn scope: Agree proposition and experience questions with consumers | set segment, behavior, and journey scope | select methods and research designs | set deliverables and timing\nOut of scope: Supported decisions (consumers) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3) | fieldwork procurement (operating model)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer strategy questions (CM-1-3-2-3/-5)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreed objectives, scope, and research design per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Research designed for decisions, not curiosity."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20962"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze consumer data against the defined objectives — segmentation and segment dynamics, needs and preference analysis, behavior and journey analysis, and experience drivers — producing evidenced results with assumptions and confidence stated, within the privacy constraints the data carries."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, consumer instance; the marketing-segmentation lens of the batch 19 four-lens rule. APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Data"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers consumer-analysis execution: segment identification and dynamics; needs, preference, and price-response analysis; behavior, journey, and experience-driver analysis; assumptions, limitations, and confidence stated; analysis respecting the consent basis and privacy constraints recorded with the data. Consumer segmentation here is the marketing lens of the four-lens rule (batch 19). Excludes decisions (consumers); segmentation for supply economics (CM-1-2-6-1-1), credit, or party hierarchy (their lenses); documentation (CM-1-3-1-3-4).\nIn scope: Identify segments and dynamics | analyze needs, preferences, and price response | analyze behavior, journeys, and experience drivers | state assumptions and confidence within privacy constraints\nOut of scope: Decisions (consumers) | other segmentation lenses (CM-1-2-6-1-1, credit, party hierarchy) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-3-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified consumer data (CM-1-3-1-3-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "objectives (CM-1-3-1-3-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced consumer-analysis results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced consumer understanding at decision depth."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/14095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document and distribute consumer-analysis findings — governed records with evidence, assumptions, and confidence, respecting the privacy classification of underlying data — to proposition, experience, and planning consumers and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship, maintaining the findings library."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, consumer instance; review default: aggregate/de-identified publication unless a specific approved use case authorizes controlled individual-level access; shared evidence-lineage statement applies. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.3.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document Findings"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers findings documentation for consumer analysis: governed records with evidence and confidence, published at aggregation levels consistent with privacy constraints; distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Consumer findings should normally be published at an aggregate, de-identified, or otherwise privacy-consistent level unless a specific approved use case authorizes controlled individual-level access. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3); consumer decisions; privacy framework ownership (governance owners). Document Findings (CM-1-3-1-3-4) supplies governed consumer-analysis findings with evidence, assumptions, limitations, and confidence that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Produce governed findings at privacy-consistent aggregation | distribute to agreed consumers | maintain the versioned library\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-3-3) | decisions (consumers) | privacy frameworks (governance owners)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-3-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "privacy classifications"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed, privacy-consistent consumer findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer insight that travels — without the personal data traveling with it."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10106"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze the company's direct customers and branded marketers — commercial and industrial customers, resellers, and the branded wholesalers, jobbers, and distributors who market under or alongside the brand — their needs, economics, performance, and relationship health, through a recurring, governed analysis cycle, so B2B and channel strategy rests on evidenced counterparty understanding."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Q2 decision: 'marketer' in the downstream fuels sense — branded wholesalers, jobbers, distributors — alongside direct commercial customers; the B2B lens paired with the consumer (B2C) lens at CM-1-3-1-3. Glossary candidate (review): \"Branded Marketer: a wholesaler, jobber, distributor, dealer, or other channel intermediary that markets or resells petroleum products under, alongside, or in association with a branded product, supply, or commercial arrangement\" — defined so it is not confused with the corporate marketing function. Four-lens rule (batch 19) applied: analysis lens here, credit and supply-economics and hierarchy lenses elsewhere. Shared personal-data governance statement and account-management boundary added per review. Shared lifecycle, fourth instance. Batch 21 durable rule (review): \"Marketing Analysis produces governed evidence, insight, hypotheses, and recommendations. It does not itself set strategy, approve investments, establish prices, allocate product, publish the enterprise forecast, define enterprise KPIs, make commercial offers, or execute campaigns.\" APQC candidate is a WEAK generic intelligence match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer And Marketer Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring customer-and-marketer analysis lifecycle: sourcing customer and marketer performance, volume, and relationship data (CM-1-3-1-4-1); framing cycles (CM-1-3-1-4-2); analyzing needs, channel economics, performance, and relationship health (CM-1-3-1-4-3); documenting governed findings (CM-1-3-1-4-4). 'Marketer' is read in the downstream fuels sense: branded wholesalers, jobbers, and distributors reselling under or alongside the brand. This is the marketing analysis lens of the batch 19 four-lens rule: the same entities appear in supply-economics segmentation (CM-1-2-6-1-1), credit assessment, and the party hierarchy through their own lenses. Personal, customer, loyalty, transaction, and behavioral data may be sourced and analyzed only for approved purposes, under the applicable lawful basis, notice/consent status where required, retention rules, access controls, data-minimization requirements, and privacy/security classifications established by the accountable Data Governance, Privacy, Legal, and Security owners. Assess relationship health and retention risk as an analytical signal; do not own account interventions, retention offers, sales actions, or account-management execution. Excludes end-consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3); credit assessment (batch 11 boundary); supply-economics segmentation (CM-1-2-6-1-1); channel strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2-4, CM-1-3-3-3); account management execution (CM-1-3-6). Customer And Marketer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-4) provides customer and marketer insight that informs Customer And Marketer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-2). Customer And Marketer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-4) supplies governed customer/marketer-analysis findings and evidence lineage that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Run the recurring customer-and-marketer analysis cycle | analyze needs, channel economics, performance, and relationship health as analytical signals | maintain evidenced counterparty understanding | feed channel strategy and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship\nOut of scope: Consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3) | credit assessment (batch 11 boundary) | supply-economics segmentation (CM-1-2-6-1-1) | channel strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2-4, CM-1-3-3-3) | account management execution (CM-1-3-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer and marketer volume, margin, and relationship data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel economics"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market context (CM-1-3-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed customer-and-marketer findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "B2B and channel decisions built on evidenced understanding of the customers and marketers who move the volume."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10195"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source and collect customer and marketer data for the analysis cycle — volumes, margins, service and relationship records, marketer network data, and external context — under the applicable data controls, organized for analysis."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance. APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.4.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source & Collect Information"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers customer-and-marketer data sourcing: internal volume, margin, service, and relationship data from their accountable owners; marketer network and performance data; external market context; provenance and currency recording; organization for analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3). Commercially sensitive counterparty data handled per its classification; personal and behavioral data under the shared governance statement recorded at CM-1-3-1-4. Excludes internal data production (accountable owners); the analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3); credit data ownership (batch 11 boundary).\nIn scope: Collect volume, margin, service, and relationship data | collect marketer network data and external context | record provenance and organize for analysis\nOut of scope: Internal data production (owners) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | credit data (batch 11 boundary)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Internal volume/margin/service data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market context"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "marketer network data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified customer-and-marketer data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The counterparty facts, complete and controlled, ready to analyze."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19521"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define each customer-and-marketer analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which segments, channels, marketers, and periods, answering which proposition and channel questions."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance — first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.4.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers framing: agreeing decision-supporting questions with proposition, channel-strategy, and sales-planning consumers; setting customer-segment, channel, marketer, geography, and period scope; selecting methods; setting deliverables and timing. Excludes the supported decisions (consumers); analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-4-3); data collection (CM-1-3-1-4-1).\nIn scope: Agree proposition and channel questions with consumers | set segment, channel, and marketer scope | select methods | set deliverables and timing\nOut of scope: Supported decisions (consumers) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | collection (CM-1-3-1-4-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer decision needs (CM-1-3-2-2/-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreed objectives, scope, and method per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty analysis aimed at channel and proposition decisions."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20962"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze customer and marketer data against the defined objectives — needs and segment analysis, channel and counterparty economics, performance and share-of-wallet, and relationship health — producing evidenced results with assumptions and confidence stated."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance; consumes batch 19 cost-to-serve as governed input; relationship health is an analytical signal, never account-management execution (review boundary protecting the future CM-1-3-6 branch). APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.4.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Data"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers analysis execution: customer and marketer segment analysis on the marketing lens; channel and counterparty economics; volume, margin, and share-of-wallet performance; relationship health and retention risk; assumptions and confidence stated. Assess relationship health and retention risk as an analytical signal; do not own account interventions, retention offers, sales actions, or account-management execution. Cost-to-serve economics come from CM-1-2-6-1-3 (batch 19) as governed input; credit risk stays with the credit process (batch 11 boundary). Excludes decisions (consumers); cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3); credit assessment (batch 11 boundary); account interventions and sales actions (CM-1-3-6); documentation (CM-1-3-1-4-4).\nIn scope: Analyze segments, needs, and counterparty economics | analyze performance and share-of-wallet | assess relationship health and retention risk as an analytical signal | state assumptions and confidence\nOut of scope: Decisions (consumers) | cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | credit assessment (batch 11 boundary) | account interventions and sales actions (CM-1-3-6) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-4-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Qualified data (CM-1-3-1-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cost-to-serve assessments (CM-1-2-6-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "objectives (CM-1-3-1-4-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced customer-and-marketer results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Know each customer and marketer relationship as well as the numbers allow."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/14095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document and distribute customer-and-marketer findings — governed records with evidence, assumptions, and confidence, handled per commercial-sensitivity classification — to proposition, channel, and sales consumers and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship, maintaining the findings library."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, customer/marketer instance; counterparty confidentiality respected; shared evidence-lineage statement applies. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.4.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document Findings"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers findings documentation: governed records with evidence and confidence; commercially sensitive counterparty findings distributed per classification; distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3); consumer decisions; records-retention policy (governance owner). Document Findings (CM-1-3-1-4-4) supplies governed customer/marketer-analysis findings with evidence, assumptions, limitations, and confidence that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Produce governed findings records | distribute per commercial-sensitivity classification | maintain the versioned library\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-4-3) | decisions (consumers) | retention policy (governance owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-4-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "classification rules"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed, classification-controlled findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty insight shared with the right people and no one else."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/13169"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze competitors in the company's downstream markets — their positions, conduct, capabilities, network moves, and likely responses — through a recurring, governed analysis cycle using legitimately obtained information, so strategy anticipates the competition it will actually face."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Q2 partition: competitor conduct and position here; market structure at CM-1-3-1-1. Review rule added verbatim: no solicitation, receipt, retention, or use of competitively sensitive information from improper channels; competition-law legality is never determined independently — concerns go to Legal/Compliance. Follow-up (review): if this branch is operationalized, register a legal/competition-policy source or the approved enterprise competition-law policy — the current CFTC/EIA source set carries no antitrust authority. Shared lifecycle, fifth instance. Batch 21 durable rule (review): \"Marketing Analysis produces governed evidence, insight, hypotheses, and recommendations. It does not itself set strategy, approve investments, establish prices, allocate product, publish the enterprise forecast, define enterprise KPIs, make commercial offers, or execute campaigns.\" APQC candidate is a WEAK pricing match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Competitor Analysis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the recurring competitor-analysis lifecycle: sourcing legitimately obtainable competitor information (CM-1-3-1-5-1); framing cycles (CM-1-3-1-5-2); analyzing competitor positions, conduct, economics, and likely responses (CM-1-3-1-5-3); documenting governed findings (CM-1-3-1-5-4). Competitive intelligence is gathered only from legitimate sources and methods, within competition-law boundaries owned by Legal & Corporate Communications and the compliance framework (batch 16). The process must not solicit, receive, retain, or use competitively sensitive information obtained through improper channels, including non-public competitor pricing, future commercial plans, capacity intentions, customer terms, or strategic information where acquisition or use would breach law, confidentiality obligations, or competition-policy controls. It may not determine competition-law legality independently; concerns are referred to Legal & Corporate Communications and the compliance framework. Excludes market-structure analysis (CM-1-3-1-1); competition-law compliance ownership (Legal, compliance per batch 16); strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3); pricing decisions (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3). Competitor Analysis (CM-1-3-1-5) provides legitimately sourced competitor positions, capabilities, and response assessments to inform Brand Strategy (CM-1-3-2-1); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Run the recurring competitor-analysis cycle on legitimate sources | analyze competitor positions, conduct, and likely responses | maintain evidenced competitive understanding | feed strategy and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship\nOut of scope: Market-structure analysis (CM-1-3-1-1) | competition-law compliance ownership (Legal, CM-1-2-4-3 framework) | strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3) | pricing decisions (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | improper-channel information (prohibited; referred to Legal/Compliance)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Public and licensed competitor information"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market observations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "network and pricing observations from legitimate sources"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed competitor-analysis findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Never surprised by a competitor move the evidence already signaled."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10195"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source and collect competitor information from legitimate sources — public filings and disclosures, licensed market data, observable market conduct, and published network and pricing information — recording provenance, and never through anti-competitive exchange or illegitimate means."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance, with the legitimacy screen: provenance recorded, improper offers refused and reported, legality questions referred to Legal/Compliance (batch 16 compliance architecture; review prohibition applied verbatim). APQC candidate is a WEAK account-data match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.5.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Source & Collect Information"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers competitor-information sourcing: public and licensed sources, observable conduct, and published data; provenance recording for every item; source-legitimacy screening under the compliance framework. The process must not solicit, receive, retain, or use competitively sensitive information obtained through improper channels, including non-public competitor pricing, future commercial plans, capacity intentions, customer terms, or strategic information where acquisition or use would breach law, confidentiality obligations, or competition-policy controls. It may not determine competition-law legality independently; concerns are referred to Legal & Corporate Communications and the compliance framework. Information offered through improper channels is refused and reported per procedure. Competition-law boundaries are owned by Legal and the compliance framework (batch 16). Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3); competition-law ownership (Legal, compliance); any illegitimate or anti-competitive acquisition (prohibited, reported per procedure).\nIn scope: Collect from public, licensed, and observable legitimate sources | record provenance for every item | screen source legitimacy and refuse and report improper offers\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | competition-law ownership (Legal, compliance) | illegitimate acquisition (prohibited)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Public filings and disclosures"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "legitimate market observations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "licensed data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Provenance-recorded, legitimacy-screened competitor information"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Competitive information the company can defend having."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19521"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define each competitor-analysis cycle's objectives, questions, scope, and method with the consuming stakeholders — which competitors, markets, and dimensions, answering which strategic and response questions."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance — first step per the normalized order. APQC 'Define objectives' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.5.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Analysis Objectives & Scope"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers framing: agreeing decision-supporting questions with strategy, planning, and pricing consumers; setting competitor, market, and dimension scope; selecting methods within the legitimate-sources rule; setting deliverables and timing. Excludes the supported decisions (consumers); analysis execution (CM-1-3-1-5-3); collection (CM-1-3-1-5-1).\nIn scope: Agree strategic and response questions with consumers | set competitor, market, and dimension scope | select methods within the legitimate-sources rule | set deliverables and timing\nOut of scope: Supported decisions (consumers) | analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | collection (CM-1-3-1-5-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Strategy and pricing questions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreed objectives, scope, and method per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Competitive questions worth answering, scoped to what can legitimately be known."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20962"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze competitor information against the defined objectives — position and share assessment, conduct and strategy inference, capability and economics estimation, and likely-response analysis — producing evidenced results that state what is known, inferred, and assumed."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance; fact/inference/assumption separation is the quality rule. APQC 'Analyze data' STRONG/NO SOURCE — honored."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.5.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Data"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers competitor-analysis execution: position and share assessment from legitimate data; conduct pattern and strategy inference; capability and economics estimation with stated uncertainty; likely-response and scenario analysis; explicit separation of known facts, inferences, and assumptions. Excludes decisions (consumers); market-structure analysis (CM-1-3-1-1); documentation (CM-1-3-1-5-4).\nIn scope: Assess positions and shares from legitimate data | infer conduct and strategy patterns | estimate capabilities and economics with stated uncertainty | analyze likely responses, separating fact from inference\nOut of scope: Decisions (consumers) | market-structure analysis (CM-1-3-1-1) | documentation (CM-1-3-1-5-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Screened competitor information (CM-1-3-1-5-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market context (CM-1-3-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "objectives (CM-1-3-1-5-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced competitor results with stated confidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Competitive judgment that knows what it knows and admits what it guesses."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/14095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document and distribute competitor-analysis findings — governed records separating fact, inference, and assumption, handled per sensitivity classification — to strategy, planning, and pricing consumers and Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship, maintaining the findings library."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Shared lifecycle step, competitor instance; shared evidence-lineage statement applies, including competition-sensitivity classification. APQC 'Document trade' is a false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.5.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Document Findings"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers findings documentation: governed records with the fact/inference/assumption separation preserved; sensitivity-classified distribution to agreed consumers and CM-1-3-1-6; versioned library maintenance. Findings records preserve the evidence lineage, source-use restrictions, assumptions, analytical method, confidence/uncertainty, and applicable commercial, privacy, and competition-sensitivity classification. Excludes the analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3); consumer decisions; records-retention policy (governance owner). Document Findings (CM-1-3-1-5-4) supplies governed competitor-analysis findings with evidence, assumptions, limitations, and confidence that Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Produce governed findings preserving fact/inference separation | distribute per sensitivity classification | maintain the versioned library\nOut of scope: Analysis (CM-1-3-1-5-3) | decisions (consumers) | retention policy (governance owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analysis results (CM-1-3-1-5-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "classification rules"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed, classified competitor findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Competitive intelligence that stays honest as it travels."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 21 (2026-09-20). Q1/Q4 review decision (the decision owner): capability, not process — it combines three concurrent, differently cadenced functions (cross-subject synthesis and insight packaging; metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence-lineage stewardship; insight-adoption and analytical-effectiveness monitoring) that form no single repeating lifecycle — the batch 04/07/11/12/15 capability test. Horizon: continuous. Preferred label 'Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship' recorded as alt label and queued for the naming pass (row name mirrors the locked taxonomy). KPI routing (review, verbatim in scope note): marketing-analysis metrics are evidence-layer measures that may inform candidate KPIs but become enterprise KPIs only through separate KPI Store classification, governance, approval, and publication (b11/12 exclusions carried forward). APQC 'Establish baseline metrics' is a WEAK partial match. Step 3d naming pass — scope-ambiguity Batch 3 (E+F, 2026-09-21): renamed from 'Insight and Metrics' to 'Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19954"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Insight and Metrics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The capability to synthesize governed market, company, consumer, customer/marketer, and competitor findings into decision-ready marketing insight; maintain shared marketing-analysis metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence lineage; and monitor insight adoption and analytical effectiveness."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.1.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers cross-analysis synthesis and metrics stewardship as a standing capability: integrating governed findings from the five analysis processes (CM-1-3-1-1 through -5) into decision-ready insight and implications for strategy, planning, and execution consumers; packaging insight; maintaining the shared marketing-analysis metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence lineage to analysis findings; and monitoring insight adoption, evidence reuse, and analytical effectiveness. Marketing-analysis metrics describe market conditions, customer/consumer insight, competitive position, segmentation, reach, channel economics, and analytical evidence quality. They may inform candidate KPIs but do not become enterprise KPIs unless separately classified, governed, approved, and published through the KPI Store. Excludes enterprise KPI definition and KPI Store governance (KPI workstream); marketing execution performance analysis (CM-1-3-5-5); financial performance reporting (CM-1-2-4-2, Finance); operational performance metrics owned by supply, distribution, or product domains; the subject analyses themselves (CM-1-3-1-1 through -5); strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3). Marketing Insight and Metrics Stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6) provides decision-ready marketing insight that informs Brand Strategy (CM-1-3-2-1).\nIn scope: Synthesize the five analyses into decision-ready insight | maintain shared marketing-analysis metrics, definitions, baselines, and evidence lineage | monitor insight adoption, evidence reuse, and analytical effectiveness | serve one evidence base to strategy, planning, and execution\nOut of scope: Enterprise KPI definition and KPI Store governance (KPI workstream) | marketing execution performance analysis (CM-1-3-5-5) | financial performance reporting (CM-1-2-4-2) | operational metrics of supply, distribution, and product domains | the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1-1/-2/-3/-4/-5) | strategy decisions (CM-1-3-2/3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/capability"
   }
  ],
