   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-5"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand performance evidence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market, company, consumer, and competitor findings"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved brand strategy with objectives and tested hypotheses"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A deliberate, evidenced, approved answer to where and how the brand competes."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Second step of the brand-strategy lifecycle. Name is singular in the locked taxonomy; plural normalized label queued for the naming pass. APQC 'Evaluate strategic initiatives' is a WEAK generic match. Step 3d naming pass — normalization-only mechanical Batch 6 (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternative' to 'Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10058"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-pmpa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternative"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (Brand)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate the alternative strategic operating models through which the brand could go to market — branded dealer and marketer networks, company-operated retail, unbranded participation, and mixed models — and evaluate them against the brand objectives and the governed evidence base."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for brand strategy: defining candidate operating alternatives; evaluating them against brand objectives, market and company findings, channel economics, and — where an arrangement meets the statutory and contractual franchise criteria — the PMPA and state-franchise constraints on changing branded arrangements (cluster PMPA statement at CM-1-3-2-1); and recommending the preferred alternative with its evidence to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-1-4). Evaluation, not commitment: strategy development and approval land at CM-1-3-2-1-4. Excludes strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4); channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6); franchise legal assessment (Legal, locked rule).\nIn scope: Define candidate brand operating alternatives | evaluate against objectives, evidence, and applicable franchise constraints | recommend the preferred alternative with evidence\nOut of scope: Strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4) | channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6) | franchise legal assessment (Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Brand objectives and hypotheses (CM-1-3-2-1-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "analysis findings (CM-1-3-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel economics"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evaluated brand operating alternatives with a recommendation"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Real alternatives, honestly evaluated, before the brand commits."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20002"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Brand Objectives and Hypotheses"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish the brand objectives and the testable strategic hypotheses for each brand-strategy cycle — what the brand must achieve, in which markets and channels, and which beliefs about consumers, customers, and competitors the strategy depends on."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the brand-strategy lifecycle. Capitalization and plural normalized in the queued label; name locked. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Brand Objectives and hypothesis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers objective and hypothesis setting for brand strategy: translating corporate and commercial direction into brand objectives; stating the strategic hypotheses (market, consumer, customer/marketer, competitor beliefs) the strategy rests on in testable form; and setting the cycle's decision calendar. The first step of the brand-strategy lifecycle: objectives and hypotheses frame the alternatives (CM-1-3-2-1-1) and the testing (CM-1-3-2-1-3). Excludes corporate strategy (its owner); the testing itself (CM-1-3-2-1-3); strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4).\nIn scope: Set brand objectives from corporate and commercial direction | state testable strategic hypotheses | set the cycle's decision calendar\nOut of scope: Corporate strategy (its owner) | hypothesis testing (CM-1-3-2-1-3) | strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Corporate and commercial direction"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior cycle results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Brand objectives and testable hypotheses per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Brand strategy that knows what it is trying to achieve and what it is betting on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10102"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and Test Brand Hypotheses"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop the brand hypotheses into testable propositions and test them against evidence — analysis findings, consumer and customer research, pilots and market tests where authorized — so the brand strategy commits only to beliefs that survived contact with evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Third step of the brand-strategy lifecycle; evidence controls inherited from batch 21 (privacy statement, competitor-information prohibition). APQC 'Develop marketing strategy' is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop & Test Brand Hypothesis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers hypothesis development and testing: converting strategic hypotheses into testable propositions; testing against the governed findings of Marketing Analysis (CM-1-3-1) and purpose-run research or pilots; recording results, confidence, and disconfirmed beliefs; and feeding validated hypotheses to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-1-4). Testing uses the batch 21 evidence base and inherits its controls (privacy, competitive-information legitimacy). Excludes the underlying analyses (CM-1-3-1); pilot execution in channels (CM-1-3-6); strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4).\nIn scope: Develop hypotheses into testable propositions | test against governed findings, research, and authorized pilots | record results, confidence, and disconfirmed beliefs\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1) | in-channel pilot execution (CM-1-3-6) | strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Hypotheses (CM-1-3-2-1-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed findings (CM-1-3-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Tested brand hypotheses with evidence and confidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Brand bets tested before they are placed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10102"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-pmpa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and Update Brand Strategy"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop or update the brand strategy — positioning, brand architecture, branded-channel participation, and investment direction — from the tested hypotheses and evaluated alternatives, secure the applicable approvals, and issue the approved strategy to the design, planning, and execution branches."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Final step of the brand-strategy lifecycle — the develop-and-maintain-approved-direction step of the three-layer rule (analysis informs, strategy develops and maintains approved direction, design/planning/execution operationalize). Governance-safe wording per review. Name's spacing/capitalization normalized in the queued label. APQC 'Develop marketing strategy' is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop / update Brand"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers strategy development, approval, and maintenance: consolidating tested hypotheses and the recommended alternative into the brand strategy; developing approved brand positioning and architecture direction; developing approved branded-channel participation direction, subject to applicable franchise, contractual, legal, and investment constraints; recommending brand investment direction; securing and recording approval under the applicable enterprise delegation of authority; and updating the strategy as cycles complete. The approved output feeds Marketing Communications Strategy (CM-1-3-3-5), Channel Design (CM-1-3-3-3), and brand standard management (CM-1-3-6-7); this row develops and maintains approved direction, it does not design, execute, or unilaterally alter franchise or trademark arrangements. Excludes design and planning (CM-1-3-3, CM-1-3-5); brand standard enforcement (CM-1-3-6-7); franchise legal work (Legal, locked rule).\nIn scope: Develop, recommend, and maintain approved brand positioning and architecture | develop approved branded-channel participation direction subject to franchise, contractual, legal, and investment constraints | recommend brand investment direction under the applicable approvals | issue the approved strategy to design, planning, and execution\nOut of scope: Design and planning (CM-1-3-3/5) | brand standard enforcement (CM-1-3-6-7) | franchise legal work (Legal locked rule) | unilateral franchise or trademark changes (approval and Legal processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Tested hypotheses (CM-1-3-2-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "franchise-constraint advice (Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved, current brand strategy"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "One approved brand strategy the rest of Marketing can build on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11168"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-pmpa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and maintain the approved value proposition offered to the company's direct customers and branded marketers — the strategic promise concerning supply, brand, program, service, and support value made to commercial customers, resellers, jobbers, distributors, and dealers — through a recurring, hypothesis-driven strategy cycle, so B2B and channel relationships are built on a deliberate, evidenced, approved promise."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one hypothesis-driven VP lifecycle (template shared with CM-1-3-2-3; batch 08/21 variant pattern). Lifecycle order: Establish CVP principles and objectives → Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP) → Test Customer value proposition → Develop/Update Strategy (CVP). 'Marketer' per the batch 21 Branded Marketer glossary candidate. Review wording: the strategic promise concerning supply, brand, program, service, and support value — operational promises live with the design and management branches. PMPA applicability fact-dependent (verbatim in scope note). Batch 22 durable rule and price-role boundary recorded verbatim in scope note. APQC 'Define offering and customer value proposition' scored STRONG at 3b with no validator agreement — treated as genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer And Marketer Value Proposition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the B2B/channel value-proposition lifecycle: establishing CVP principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-2-3), formulating and evaluating strategic alternatives for how the proposition is delivered (CM-1-3-2-2-2), testing the proposition with customer and marketer evidence (CM-1-3-2-2-1), and developing and updating the approved proposition strategy (CM-1-3-2-2-4). 'Marketer' carries the batch 21 downstream-fuels reading (Branded Marketer glossary candidate). The proposition is the strategic promise; the Offer Definition, Pricing, Channel Design, and Channel & Partner Management branches turn that promise into actual products, terms, service models, and partner activity. Marketing Strategy develops and maintains approved brand, value-proposition, channel, and customer-experience direction using governed evidence from Marketing Analysis. It does not perform the analyses; design detailed offers, prices, channels, networks, communications, or operating models; plan campaigns and sales; or execute channel, sales, brand, loyalty, or service programs. Material strategic changes follow the applicable enterprise delegation, investment, legal, and governance approvals. Where an arrangement meets the applicable statutory and contractual criteria for a branded motor-fuel franchise, changes to trademark, supply, lease, renewal, termination, or non-renewal arrangements may be constrained by the PMPA and applicable state law. Legal classification, interpretation, notice requirements, termination/non-renewal analysis, and franchise documentation remain the responsibility of Legal & Corporate Communications. Strategy may set the strategic role of price in the proposition or channel — such as value, premium, parity, transparency, index linkage, or loyalty emphasis — but does not establish pricing strategy, price architecture, price rules, price levels, discounts, formula terms, or transaction prices. Those activities belong to Pricing Strategy Management and Sales Pricing. Excludes the consumer proposition (CM-1-3-2-3); offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3); account and partner management (CM-1-3-6-1/-2); customer and marketer analysis (CM-1-3-1-4). Customer And Marketer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-2) is informed by the insight of Customer And Marketer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-4). Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1) defines offers that deliver the approved value proposition set by Customer And Marketer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-2).\nIn scope: Run the recurring B2B/channel value-proposition cycle | develop and maintain the approved strategic promise to direct customers and branded marketers | test the proposition against counterparty evidence | keep the approved proposition current for offer design and channel management\nOut of scope: Consumer proposition (CM-1-3-2-3) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | account/partner management (CM-1-3-6-1/-2) | the analysis (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer and marketer findings (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel economics"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved customer-and-marketer value proposition"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A deliberate, evidenced, approved promise to the customers and marketers who move the volume."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11168"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Test Customer and Marketer Value Proposition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Test the customer-and-marketer value proposition against evidence — counterparty findings, direct customer and marketer feedback, win/loss and retention signals, and competitive benchmarks — so the proposition strategy commits only to a promise the evidence supports."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Test step of the B2B VP lifecycle; capitalization and marketer coverage normalized in the queued label. Competitive comparisons under the batch 21 competitor-information prohibition. APQC 'Define offering and customer value proposition' STRONG, no validator — comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Test Customer value proposition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers proposition testing on the B2B/channel lens: structuring the proposition into testable elements; testing against Customer And Marketer Analysis findings (CM-1-3-1-4), authorized customer and marketer feedback, and competitive context (CM-1-3-1-5, legitimate sources only); recording results and confidence; and feeding the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-2-4). Excludes the underlying analyses (CM-1-3-1-4/-5); account interventions from test findings (CM-1-3-6); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4).\nIn scope: Structure the proposition into testable elements | test against counterparty findings, feedback, and competitive context | record results and confidence\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1-4/-5) | account interventions (CM-1-3-6) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Proposition elements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty findings (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "feedback and win/loss evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Tested proposition elements with evidence and confidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A promise tested with the people it is made to."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10058"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Customer and Marketer Value Proposition Alternatives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate alternative strategic models for delivering the customer-and-marketer value proposition — supply-led, brand-and-program-led, service-led, and mixed models across the channel structure — and evaluate them against the CVP objectives and the governed evidence base."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Alternatives step of the B2B VP lifecycle; expanded normalized label queued per review. APQC 'Evaluate strategic initiatives' is a WEAK generic match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for the B2B/channel proposition: defining candidate delivery models; evaluating against CVP principles and objectives, counterparty economics, channel strategy direction, and — where arrangements meet the franchise criteria — the applicable franchise constraints (cluster PMPA statement at CM-1-3-2-2); recommending the preferred alternative to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-2-4). Excludes proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4); channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6).\nIn scope: Define candidate proposition delivery models | evaluate against objectives, economics, and applicable constraints | recommend with evidence\nOut of scope: Proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4) | channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | operating model design (CM-1-3-3-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "CVP principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-2-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel direction (CM-1-3-2-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty economics"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evaluated proposition delivery alternatives with a recommendation"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The proposition delivered the best way, chosen from real alternatives."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20002"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Customer and Marketer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish the principles and objectives of the customer-and-marketer value proposition — what the promise must achieve for the company and for its customers and marketers, and the principles any proposition must satisfy."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the B2B VP lifecycle; expanded normalized label queued. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish CVP principles and objectives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers principle and objective setting for the B2B/channel proposition: translating commercial strategy and brand strategy into proposition objectives; setting the principles (economic, brand, service, franchise-relationship) any candidate proposition must satisfy; and setting the cycle's decision calendar. First step of the CVP lifecycle. Excludes commercial strategy (its owner); the alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-2-2/-1); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4).\nIn scope: Set proposition objectives from commercial and brand direction | set the principles candidate propositions must satisfy | set the decision calendar\nOut of scope: Commercial strategy (its owner) | alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-2-2/-1) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-2-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial and brand direction"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior cycle results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "CVP principles, objectives, and decision calendar per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A proposition that knows what it must achieve before it is designed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-pmpa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and Update Customer and Marketer Value Proposition Strategy"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop or update the customer-and-marketer value-proposition strategy from the tested elements and evaluated alternatives, secure the applicable approvals, and issue the approved proposition to offer definition, channel strategy, and channel management."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Develop-and-maintain step of the B2B VP lifecycle; governance-safe wording per review. Workbook 3b review note confirmed: APQC 'Develop KM strategy' is a FALSE lexical match (knowledge-management 'strategy', different sense) — carried forward; comparative only. Expanded normalized label queued."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.2.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers proposition strategy development, approval, and maintenance: consolidating tested elements and the recommended delivery model into the proposition; developing, recommending, and maintaining the approved promise by customer and marketer segment under the applicable delegation of authority, with franchise constraints applying where arrangements meet the franchise criteria; and updating it as cycles complete. Output feeds Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1), Channel Strategy (CM-1-3-2-4), and Channel & Partner Management (CM-1-3-6-1). Develops and maintains the approved promise, not the offers, prices, or accounts. Excludes offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3); account/partner execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2).\nIn scope: Develop, recommend, and maintain the approved proposition by customer and marketer segment | issue the approved proposition to offer definition and channel processes | update as cycles complete\nOut of scope: Offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | account/partner execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/rejected"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Tested elements (CM-1-3-2-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-2-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "franchise-constraint advice (Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved customer-and-marketer value proposition strategy"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "One approved B2B promise the offer and channel processes can build on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11168"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and maintain the approved value proposition offered to end consumers in the company's downstream markets — the strategic promise concerning fuel, convenience, loyalty, and experience value — through a recurring, hypothesis-driven strategy cycle grounded in governed consumer evidence, so consumer-facing offers and experiences deliver a deliberate, approved promise."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — the consumer instance of the VP lifecycle template (shared with CM-1-3-2-2). Lifecycle order: Establish Consumer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives → Formulate and Evaluate Consumer Value Proposition Alternatives → Test Consumer Value Proposition → Develop and Update Consumer Value Proposition Strategy. Review naming decision: the child names reuse the template's 'Customer'/'CVP' wording under the Consumer cluster — consumer-directional normalized labels (Test Consumer Value Proposition; Formulate and Evaluate Consumer Value Proposition Alternatives; Establish Consumer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives; Develop and Update Consumer Value Proposition Strategy) queued for the naming pass to prevent B2C/B2B ontology confusion. Consumer evidence under the batch 21 privacy controls. Batch 22 durable rule and price-role boundary recorded verbatim in scope note. APQC 'Define offering and customer value proposition' is the comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer Value Proposition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the consumer (B2C) value-proposition lifecycle: establishing principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-3-3), formulating and evaluating delivery alternatives (CM-1-3-2-3-2), testing with consumer evidence (CM-1-3-2-3-1), and developing and updating the approved proposition strategy (CM-1-3-2-3-4). Consumer evidence comes from Consumer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-3) under its privacy and publication controls (batch 21 shared statement; aggregate/de-identified default). The proposition is the strategic promise; concrete offers, network, and experience designs live at CM-1-3-3-1/-4 and CM-1-3-2-5; loyalty operation at CM-1-3-6-6. Marketing Strategy develops and maintains approved brand, value-proposition, channel, and customer-experience direction using governed evidence from Marketing Analysis. It does not perform the analyses; design detailed offers, prices, channels, networks, communications, or operating models; plan campaigns and sales; or execute channel, sales, brand, loyalty, or service programs. Material strategic changes follow the applicable enterprise delegation, investment, legal, and governance approvals. Strategy may set the strategic role of price in the proposition or channel — such as value, premium, parity, transparency, index linkage, or loyalty emphasis — but does not establish pricing strategy, price architecture, price rules, price levels, discounts, formula terms, or transaction prices. Those activities belong to Pricing Strategy Management and Sales Pricing. Excludes the B2B/marketer proposition (CM-1-3-2-2); offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4); loyalty operation (CM-1-3-6-6); consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3). Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1) defines offers that deliver the approved value proposition set by Consumer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-3).\nIn scope: Run the recurring consumer value-proposition cycle | develop and maintain the approved fuel, convenience, loyalty, and experience promise | test the proposition against governed consumer evidence | keep the approved proposition current for offer and experience design\nOut of scope: B2B/marketer proposition (CM-1-3-2-2) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | loyalty operation (CM-1-3-6-6) | the analysis (CM-1-3-1-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market findings (CM-1-3-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved consumer value proposition"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A deliberate, evidenced, approved promise to the consumer at the pump and in the store."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Test step of the consumer VP lifecycle; the locked name reuses the template's 'Customer' wording — consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. Privacy controls inherited from batch 21. APQC 'Define offering and customer value proposition' STRONG, no validator — comparative anchor. Step 3d naming pass — directionality-missing Batch 4 (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Test Customer value proposition' to 'Test Consumer Value Proposition'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11168"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Test Customer value proposition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Test the consumer value proposition against evidence — governed consumer findings, research, and authorized concept and market tests — so the consumer promise commits only to what the evidence supports."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Test Consumer Value Proposition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers proposition testing on the consumer lens: structuring the proposition into testable elements; testing against Consumer Analysis findings (CM-1-3-1-3), purpose-run research, and authorized concept or market tests; recording results and confidence; feeding the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-3-4). Testing uses personal data only through the governed findings and controls of CM-1-3-1-3 (batch 21 shared statement); test publication follows the aggregate/de-identified default. Excludes the consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3); in-market test execution (CM-1-3-6); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4).\nIn scope: Structure the consumer proposition into testable elements | test against governed findings, research, and authorized tests | record results and confidence within privacy controls\nOut of scope: Consumer analysis (CM-1-3-1-3) | in-market execution (CM-1-3-6) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Proposition elements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "research and test results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Tested consumer-proposition elements with evidence and confidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A consumer promise tested before it is made."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Alternatives step of the consumer VP lifecycle; consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. APQC 'Evaluate strategic initiatives' is a WEAK generic match. Step 3d naming pass — directionality-missing Batch 4 (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP)' to 'Formulate and Evaluate Consumer Value Proposition Alternatives'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10058"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Strategic Operating Alternatives (CVP)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate alternative strategic models for delivering the consumer value proposition — fuel-led, convenience-led, loyalty-led, digital-led, and mixed models — and evaluate them against the proposition objectives and the governed evidence base."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.3.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Formulate and Evaluate Consumer Value Proposition Alternatives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers alternative formulation and evaluation for the consumer proposition: defining candidate delivery models; evaluating against principles and objectives, consumer findings, retail economics, and brand direction; recommending the preferred alternative to the develop/update step (CM-1-3-2-3-4). Excludes proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4); retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4); offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1).\nIn scope: Define candidate consumer-proposition delivery models | evaluate against objectives, evidence, and economics | recommend with evidence\nOut of scope: Proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4) | retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Principles and objectives (CM-1-3-2-3-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "retail economics"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evaluated consumer-proposition delivery alternatives with a recommendation"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The consumer promise delivered the best way, chosen from real alternatives."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the consumer VP lifecycle; consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' is a WEAK adjacent match. Step 3d naming pass — directionality-missing Batch 4 (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Establish CVP principles and objectives' to 'Establish Consumer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20002"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish CVP principles and objectives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish the principles and objectives of the consumer value proposition — what the consumer promise must achieve and the principles any candidate proposition must satisfy."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Consumer Value Proposition Principles and Objectives"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers principle and objective setting for the consumer proposition: translating commercial and brand strategy into consumer-proposition objectives; setting the principles (economic, brand, experience, privacy-by-design) candidates must satisfy; setting the cycle's decision calendar. First step of the consumer VP lifecycle. Excludes commercial strategy (its owner); alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-3-2/-1); proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4).\nIn scope: Set consumer-proposition objectives | set the principles candidates must satisfy, including privacy-by-design | set the decision calendar\nOut of scope: Commercial strategy (its owner) | alternatives and testing (CM-1-3-2-3-2/-1) | proposition strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-3-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial and brand direction"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior cycle results"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer-proposition principles, objectives, and decision calendar per cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A consumer promise that knows what it must achieve before it is designed."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Develop-and-maintain step of the consumer VP lifecycle; governance-safe wording per review; consumer-directional normalized label required by review, queued. Same FALSE-match caution as CM-1-3-2-2-4: APQC 'Develop KM strategy' is a different 'strategy' sense; comparative only. Step 3d naming pass — directionality-missing Batch 4 (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)' to 'Develop and Update Consumer Value Proposition Strategy'. Prior label retained as altLabel."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11095"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop/Update Strategy (CVP)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop or update the consumer value-proposition strategy from the tested elements and evaluated alternatives, secure the applicable approvals, and issue the approved proposition to offer definition, experience strategy, and consumer-facing planning."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.3.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and Update Consumer Value Proposition Strategy"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers consumer-proposition strategy development, approval, and maintenance: consolidating tested elements and the recommended delivery model into the proposition; developing, recommending, and maintaining the approved promise by consumer segment (marketing lens, batch 19/21) under the applicable delegation of authority; updating as cycles complete. Output feeds Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1), Customer Experience Strategy (CM-1-3-2-5), and consumer-facing planning (CM-1-3-5). Develops and maintains the approved promise, not the offers, networks, or campaigns. Excludes offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); network design (CM-1-3-3-4); campaign planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6).\nIn scope: Develop, recommend, and maintain the approved consumer proposition by segment | issue the approved proposition to offer, experience, and planning processes | update as cycles complete\nOut of scope: Offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | campaign planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Tested elements (CM-1-3-2-3-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand direction (CM-1-3-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "evaluated alternatives (CM-1-3-2-3-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved consumer value-proposition strategy"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "One approved consumer promise the offer and experience processes can build on."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10103"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-pmpa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and maintain the approved strategic channel-of-trade direction for downstream sales and distribution — which routes to market the company participates in, their strategic roles, and the target channel mix — through a recurring cycle of channel diagnostics and hypothesis-driven strategy development under the applicable enterprise approvals, so channel design and channel management execute a deliberate, evidenced, approved direction."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one diagnostics-to-strategy lifecycle. Lifecycle order: Conduct Channel of trade diagnostics → Establish operating Objectives and develop Channel Strategy Hypothesis → approved strategy developed and maintained at this L4. Channel-of-trade vocabulary is illustrative (review caveat verbatim in scope note); enterprise taxonomy governs. Investment-authority wording per review: recommend and maintain approved direction, subject to delegated approvals — material for retail-network acquisitions, divestitures, dealer conversions, and branded/unbranded transitions. PMPA applicability fact-dependent (verbatim in scope note). Batch 22 durable rule and price-role boundary recorded verbatim in scope note. APQC 'Develop sales strategy' is a WEAK adjacent match (sales planning is CM-1-3-5-1)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Sales & Distribution Channel Strategy"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the channel-strategy lifecycle: conducting channel-of-trade diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1) and establishing channel operating objectives and the channel-strategy hypothesis (CM-1-3-2-4-2), with the approved strategy developed and maintained at this L4. Channels of trade span company-operated retail, branded dealer, branded marketer/jobber and distributor, unbranded rack and wholesale, and direct commercial channels. These are illustrative external channel-of-trade labels. The enterprise's approved commercial/channel taxonomy governs internal classification. EIA's DTW/rack/retail categories are external statistical context only, per the SRC-EIA-PMM-001 limitations. Marketing Strategy develops and maintains approved brand, value-proposition, channel, and customer-experience direction using governed evidence from Marketing Analysis. It does not perform the analyses; design detailed offers, prices, channels, networks, communications, or operating models; plan campaigns and sales; or execute channel, sales, brand, loyalty, or service programs. Material strategic changes follow the applicable enterprise delegation, investment, legal, and governance approvals. Where an arrangement meets the applicable statutory and contractual criteria for a branded motor-fuel franchise, changes to trademark, supply, lease, renewal, termination, or non-renewal arrangements may be constrained by the PMPA and applicable state law. Legal classification, interpretation, notice requirements, termination/non-renewal analysis, and franchise documentation remain the responsibility of Legal & Corporate Communications. Strategy may set the strategic role of price in the proposition or channel — such as value, premium, parity, transparency, index linkage, or loyalty emphasis — but does not establish pricing strategy, price architecture, price rules, price levels, discounts, formula terms, or transaction prices. Those activities belong to Pricing Strategy Management and Sales Pricing. Strategy only: detailed channel design at CM-1-3-3-3, retail network design at CM-1-3-3-4, partner management at CM-1-3-6-1, sales strategy and planning at CM-1-3-5-1. Excludes channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4); channel/partner management (CM-1-3-6-1); sales planning (CM-1-3-5-1); secondary distribution operations (CM-1-1-3-8, SCM-vs-Commercial locked rule). Sales & Distribution Channel Design (CM-1-3-3-3) designs the channel system from the approved channel strategy set by Sales & Distribution Channel Strategy (CM-1-3-2-4).\nIn scope: Run the recurring channel-strategy cycle | develop and maintain approved channel-of-trade participation, roles, and target mix | recommend and maintain approved direction for channel investment, expansion, de-emphasis, or exit, subject to delegated investment, legal, franchise, and corporate approvals | issue channel direction to design, planning, and management\nOut of scope: Channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | retail network design (CM-1-3-3-4) | channel/partner management (CM-1-3-6-1) | sales planning (CM-1-3-5-1) | secondary distribution operations (CM-1-1-3-8, locked rule) | pricing strategy, rules, and levels (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-6"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Channel diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cost-to-serve assessments (CM-1-2-6-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "customer/marketer findings (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved channel-of-trade strategy and target mix"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every route to market chosen on purpose, with evidence and the right approvals."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11466"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-eia-pmm-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct Channel-of-Trade Diagnostics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Diagnose the performance and economics of each channel of trade the company participates in — volumes, margins, cost-to-serve, share, counterparty health, and structural trends — producing the evidenced channel picture the channel strategy is built on."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Diagnostic step of the channel-strategy lifecycle; hyphenation/capitalization normalized in the queued label. EIA channel categories are external statistical context only (b21 limitation). APQC 'Conduct planning activities for major trade customers' is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.4.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct Channel of trade diagnostics"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers channel diagnostics: assembling channel-level volume, margin, and share evidence; consuming cost-to-serve assessments from CM-1-2-6-1-3 (batch 19) and counterparty findings from CM-1-3-1-4 as governed inputs; assessing channel structural trends with external statistical context (EIA PMM categories, within their limitations); and stating findings with assumptions and confidence. Diagnostics inform; the strategy hypothesis and the approved strategy sit at CM-1-3-2-4-2 and the L4. Excludes cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3); the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); the strategy hypothesis and approved strategy (CM-1-3-2-4-2, CM-1-3-2-4).\nIn scope: Assemble channel-level performance and economics evidence | consume governed cost-to-serve and counterparty findings | assess structural channel trends | state findings with confidence\nOut of scope: Cost-to-serve production (CM-1-2-6-1-3) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1) | strategy hypothesis and approved strategy (CM-1-3-2-4-2, CM-1-3-2-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-2-6-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Channel volume/margin/share data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "EIA channel statistics (context)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cost-to-serve (CM-1-2-6-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "counterparty findings (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced channel-of-trade diagnostics"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "An honest channel-by-channel picture before the channel bets are made."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20002"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-pmpa-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Channel Operating Objectives and Channel Strategy Hypothesis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish the channel operating objectives and develop the channel-strategy hypothesis — the proposed channel participation, roles, and target mix with the beliefs it depends on stated testably — for evaluation and approval at the channel-strategy level."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Hypothesis step of the channel-strategy lifecycle; review's normalized label queued. APQC 'Establish channel objectives' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.4.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish operating Objectives and develop Channel Strategy Hypothesis"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers objective-setting and hypothesis development for channel strategy: translating commercial, brand, and value-proposition direction into channel operating objectives; developing the channel-strategy hypothesis from the diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1); stating dependencies and risks, including — where arrangements meet the franchise criteria — the applicable PMPA and state-franchise constraints on changes to existing branded arrangements (cluster PMPA statement at CM-1-3-2-4); and submitting the hypothesis for development and approval of the strategy at CM-1-3-2-4. Excludes the diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1); strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-4); channel design (CM-1-3-3-3); franchise legal assessment (Legal, locked rule).\nIn scope: Set channel operating objectives from strategy direction | develop the channel-strategy hypothesis from diagnostics | state dependencies, risks, and applicable franchise constraints | submit for strategy development and approval\nOut of scope: Diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1) | strategy development and approval (CM-1-3-2-4) | channel design (CM-1-3-3-3) | franchise legal assessment (Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Channel diagnostics (CM-1-3-2-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand direction (CM-1-3-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Channel operating objectives and the channel-strategy hypothesis"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A channel strategy proposed as a testable bet, not an assumption."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19959"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and maintain the approved customer-experience strategy for the company's downstream customer and consumer interactions — the experience aspiration, guiding principles, and strategic pillars that every channel, offer, and service interaction is designed against — through a recurring strategy cycle grounded in governed consumer and customer evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one aspiration-to-strategy lifecycle. Lifecycle order per review: Identify Customer Experience Aspiration → Define Customer Experience Guiding Principles → Establish Customer Experience Strategic Pillars → develop and maintain the approved customer-experience strategy at this L4 (explicit strategy-maintenance output added per review, so the L4 is a strategy node, not a container). Cross-audience per review: 'Customer' definition verbatim in scope note — consumers, commercial customers, channel partners, and marketers at their interaction points. Experience evidence under batch 21 privacy controls. Batch 22 durable rule and price-role boundary recorded verbatim in scope note. APQC 'Develop customer experience strategy' scored 0.857 STRONG — the branch's strongest genuine APQC anchor; no validator agreement recorded, treated as comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer Experience Strategy"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the experience-strategy lifecycle: identifying the customer-experience aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1), defining experience guiding principles (CM-1-3-2-5-2), and establishing the strategic pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-3). Develop and maintain the approved customer-experience strategy by consolidating the aspiration, principles, and pillars into a governed strategic direction issued to design, service, channel, and execution processes. 'Customer' includes consumers, commercial customers, channel partners, and marketers where they interact with the company's products, services, channels, support, digital touchpoints, and operational processes. The experience promise must be consistent with the value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3) and brand strategy (CM-1-3-2-1). Marketing Strategy develops and maintains approved brand, value-proposition, channel, and customer-experience direction using governed evidence from Marketing Analysis. It does not perform the analyses; design detailed offers, prices, channels, networks, communications, or operating models; plan campaigns and sales; or execute channel, sales, brand, loyalty, or service programs. Material strategic changes follow the applicable enterprise delegation, investment, legal, and governance approvals. Strategy may set the strategic role of price in the proposition or channel — such as value, premium, parity, transparency, index linkage, or loyalty emphasis — but does not establish pricing strategy, price architecture, price rules, price levels, discounts, formula terms, or transaction prices. Those activities belong to Pricing Strategy Management and Sales Pricing. Strategy only: experience delivery sits with the channel, service, and execution processes (CM-1-3-6, CM-1-3-9); experience measurement with Service & Support Measurement (CM-1-3-9-3) and Marketing Performance Analysis (CM-1-3-5-5); experience evidence from Consumer and Customer/Marketer Analysis under their privacy controls. Excludes experience delivery (CM-1-3-6, CM-1-3-9); experience measurement (CM-1-3-9-3, CM-1-3-5-5); the analyses (CM-1-3-1-3/-4); loyalty operation (CM-1-3-6-6). Customer Experience Strategy (CM-1-3-2-5) provides approved customer-experience aspirations, guiding principles, and strategic pillars to inform Service & Support Enablement (CM-1-3-9-1); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Run the recurring experience-strategy cycle | set the experience aspiration, principles, and pillars | consolidate them into the approved, governed experience strategy and maintain it | keep the experience promise consistent with brand and value propositions | issue experience direction to design, service, and execution\nOut of scope: Experience delivery (CM-1-3-6, CM-1-3-9) | experience measurement (CM-1-3-9-3, CM-1-3-5-5) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1-3/-4) | loyalty operation (CM-1-3-6-6) | pricing strategy, rules, and levels (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Consumer and customer/marketer findings (CM-1-3-1-3/-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand direction (CM-1-3-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved, maintained customer-experience strategy (aspiration, principles, pillars)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every customer interaction designed against one deliberate, approved experience promise."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19960"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify the customer-experience aspiration — the target experience the company commits to across its consumer and customer interactions — from the brand strategy, value propositions, and governed experience evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). First step of the experience-strategy lifecycle. APQC 'Assess customer experience' is a WEAK measurement-side match (measurement is CM-1-3-9-3/CM-1-3-5-5)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.5.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify Customer Experience Aspiration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers aspiration setting: synthesizing what consumers and customers value in their interactions (from CM-1-3-1-3/-4 findings) with brand and proposition direction; articulating the target experience and its ambition level relative to competitive and category benchmarks; and framing the aspiration for the principles step (CM-1-3-2-5-2). First step of the experience-strategy lifecycle; the consolidated strategy is developed and maintained at CM-1-3-2-5. Excludes the analyses (CM-1-3-1-3/-4); the principles and pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-2/-3); experience delivery (CM-1-3-6, CM-1-3-9).\nIn scope: Synthesize experience evidence with brand and proposition direction | articulate the target experience and ambition level | frame the aspiration for principles and pillars\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1-3/-4) | principles and pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-2/-3) | experience delivery (CM-1-3-6/9)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Experience evidence (CM-1-3-1-3/-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand and proposition direction"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "competitive benchmarks (legitimate sources)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The customer-experience aspiration"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A stated ambition for how interactions should feel, grounded in evidence."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19967"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define the guiding principles that translate the experience aspiration into decision rules — the consistent behaviors, standards of treatment, and design tenets every channel, offer, and service decision must satisfy."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Second step of the experience-strategy lifecycle. APQC 'Define a vision for the customer experience' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.5.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Customer Experience Guiding Principles"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers principle definition: converting the aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1) into explicit, decision-usable principles; reconciling them with brand strategy, value propositions, and operational and regulatory constraints; and issuing them for the pillars step (CM-1-3-2-5-3) and for use by design, planning, and execution processes. Principles guide decisions; they are not service procedures (CM-1-3-9) or brand standards (CM-1-3-6-7). Excludes the aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1); the pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-3); service procedures (CM-1-3-9); brand standard management (CM-1-3-6-7).\nIn scope: Convert the aspiration into decision-usable principles | reconcile with brand, proposition, and constraint context | issue principles to strategy, design, and execution consumers\nOut of scope: The aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1) | pillars (CM-1-3-2-5-3) | service procedures (CM-1-3-9) | brand standards (CM-1-3-6-7)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The aspiration (CM-1-3-2-5-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand and proposition direction"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operational and regulatory constraints"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer-experience guiding principles"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The experience promise written as rules people can decide with."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10020"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish the strategic pillars of the customer-experience strategy — the small set of experience priorities the company will invest in and be known for — with their intended outcomes and the evidence basis for each."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 22 (2026-09-20). Third step of the experience-strategy lifecycle; the consolidated strategy is developed and maintained at the L4 per review. Experience-pillar measures follow the batch 21 KPI Store routing: evidence-layer measures unless separately governed as enterprise KPIs. APQC 'Establish strategic vision' is a WEAK generic match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.2.5.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish Customer Experience Strategic Pillars"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers pillar establishment: selecting the experience priorities from the aspiration and principles; stating each pillar's intended customer outcome and evidence basis; aligning pillars with channel strategy, value propositions, and service direction; and issuing the completed pillar set for consolidation into the approved strategy at CM-1-3-2-5 and use by planning and execution. Pillars direct investment and design focus; delivery programs and their measurement belong to CM-1-3-5/6/9. Excludes strategy consolidation and maintenance (CM-1-3-2-5); delivery programs (CM-1-3-5/6/9); enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream).\nIn scope: Select experience priorities with intended outcomes | state each pillar's evidence basis | align pillars with channel, proposition, and service direction | issue the pillar set for strategy consolidation\nOut of scope: Strategy consolidation and maintenance (CM-1-3-2-5) | delivery programs (CM-1-3-5/6/9) | KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Aspiration and principles (CM-1-3-2-5-1/-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel and proposition direction"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "experience evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The customer-experience strategic pillars"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A few experience priorities the company actually invests behind."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Offer design & development process consist of the elements of the go-to-market approach determined in the marketing operations strategy. It links the long-term strategy with the operational planning by detailing all strategic aspects (customer offer, sales channel & operations, distribution network)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Offer Design & Development"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10464"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define the concrete customer offers that deliver the approved value propositions — which customer groups are targeted, what each offer contains, how it is validated, and how its performance will be measured — through a recurring offer-design cycle, so execution sells defined, validated offers rather than improvised ones."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 23 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one offer-design lifecycle; horizon tactical (design layer). Lifecycle order: Define Target Customer Groups → Define Customer Offer → Validate Customer Offer → Define Offer Measurement Framework. Middle layer of the batch 22 three-layer rule: designs within approved strategic direction, never re-decides it. Launch control per review: defined does not mean sellable — the applicable approval controls gate executability. APQC 'Negotiate offer' is a FALSE match (HR job-offer negotiation)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer Offer Definition"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the offer-definition lifecycle: defining target customer groups (CM-1-3-3-1-1), defining the customer offer (CM-1-3-3-1-2), validating it with evidence (CM-1-3-3-1-3), and defining its measurement framework (CM-1-3-3-1-4). Designs within approved strategic direction: the value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3) and brand strategy (CM-1-3-2-1) set the promise; this cluster turns the promise into defined offers. Defined offers become executable only after required commercial, pricing, legal, operational, product/service, and approval controls are satisfied. Offer price terms are designed with, and governed by, Pricing Strategy Management (CM-1-3-3-2) and executed by the pricing processes; product and service development beyond offer assembly sits at CM-1-3-4-3; campaign and sales execution at CM-1-3-5/6. Excludes value-proposition strategy (CM-1-3-2-2/-3); pricing strategy, rules, and levels (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3); product/service development (CM-1-3-4-3); campaign planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6); enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream). Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1) defines offers that deliver the approved value proposition set by Customer And Marketer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-2). Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1) defines offers that deliver the approved value proposition set by Consumer Value Proposition (CM-1-3-2-3). When the offer has completed its applicable commercial, pricing, legal, operational, and product/service approvals, Customer Offer Definition (CM-1-3-3-1) supplies approved, validated customer-offer content and eligibility definitions that Sales Execution (CM-1-3-6-2) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Run the recurring offer-definition cycle | define target customer groups on the marketing lens | define and validate concrete offers from the approved propositions | define offer measurement frameworks with KPI Store routing\nOut of scope: VP strategy (CM-1-3-2-2/-3) | pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | product development (CM-1-3-4-3) | campaign/sales execution (CM-1-3-5/6) | enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream) | offer launch approval (applicable approval controls)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-2-4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-3-4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved value propositions (CM-1-3-2-2/-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "offer performance evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Defined, validated customer offers with measurement frameworks"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The approved promise turned into offers a salesperson can actually sell."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10160"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define the customer groups each offer targets — selecting and prioritizing segments from the governed segmentation evidence — so offers are designed for identified groups rather than everyone."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 23 (2026-09-20). Targeting step; four-lens rule applied (batch 19/21); review privacy/eligibility caveat verbatim in scope note — material for retail/loyalty offers and credit-sensitive segments. APQC 'Define target audience' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Target Customer Groups"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers targeting: selecting target groups for offers from the marketing-lens segmentation evidence of Consumer and Customer/Marketer Analysis (CM-1-3-1-3/-4); prioritizing groups against the approved propositions and channel strategy; and recording targeting rationale. Targeting may use personal, loyalty, account, and behavioral data only for approved purposes and within applicable privacy, consent, suppression, fairness, and non-discrimination controls. The design instance of the batch 19 four-lens rule: targeting uses the marketing lens; supply-economics, credit, and party-hierarchy segmentation stay with their lenses. Excludes the segmentation analyses (CM-1-3-1-3-3, CM-1-3-1-4-3); other segmentation lenses (their owners); offer content definition (CM-1-3-3-1-2); privacy and fairness framework ownership (accountable governance owners).\nIn scope: Select and prioritize target groups from governed segmentation evidence | apply privacy, consent, suppression, fairness, and non-discrimination controls | align targeting with propositions and channel strategy | record targeting rationale\nOut of scope: Segmentation analysis production (CM-1-3-1-3/-4) | other segmentation lenses (four-lens rule) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1-2) | privacy/fairness framework ownership (governance owners)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Segmentation findings (CM-1-3-1-3/-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved propositions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel direction (CM-1-3-2-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Prioritized target customer groups per offer with rationale"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Offers aimed at chosen groups, chosen on evidence, within the rules."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19967"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define the content of each customer offer — the product, service, program, and experience elements assembled for the target group, with the commercial logic connecting them — implementing the approved value proposition as a concrete, specifiable offer."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 23 (2026-09-20). Definition step of the offer lifecycle; implements, never redefines, the approved propositions (batch 22 boundary); dependency-identification rule per review. APQC 'Define a vision for the customer experience' is a WEAK false-direction match (experience strategy is CM-1-3-2-5)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Customer Offer"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers offer definition: assembling product, service, program, and experience elements into the offer for each target group; specifying the offer precisely enough to validate, price, plan, and execute; and stating the commercial logic. Offer definition identifies the required pricing, product, channel, service, legal, tax, operational, and technology dependencies; it does not itself approve those dependent designs. Price-term design is coordinated with Pricing Strategy Management (CM-1-3-3-2), which governs price architecture and rules. The offer implements the approved proposition; it does not redefine it. Excludes price architecture, rules, and levels (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3); new product/service development (CM-1-3-4-3); the validation (CM-1-3-3-1-3); proposition strategy (CM-1-3-2-2/-3); approval of dependent designs (their owners).\nIn scope: Assemble offer elements for each target group | specify offers precisely for validation, pricing, planning, and execution | state the commercial logic | identify dependent designs without approving them\nOut of scope: Price architecture/rules/levels (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | product development (CM-1-3-4-3) | validation (CM-1-3-3-1-3) | proposition strategy (CM-1-3-2-2/-3) | dependent-design approval (their owners)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Target groups (CM-1-3-3-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved propositions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "available products, services, and programs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Specified customer offers with commercial logic and dependencies"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "An offer specified well enough to validate, price, and sell."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19968"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Validate defined offers against evidence before release — customer and consumer response, commercial viability, operational deliverability, and consistency with the approved proposition — so offers reach planning and execution already tested."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 23 (2026-09-20). Validation step; go/no-go distinction per review — this process recommends, the applicable approval and launch-planning process decides. Privacy controls and publication default inherited (batch 21); consumes batch 19 cost-to-serve as governed input. APQC 'Validate with customers' is a WEAK generic match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Validate Customer Offer"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers offer validation: testing offer response with governed evidence and authorized research or concept tests (under the batch 21 privacy controls and aggregate/de-identified default); validating commercial viability with the pricing processes and cost-to-serve evidence (CM-1-2-6-1-3); confirming operational deliverability with the affected operating processes; and checking proposition consistency. Produces validation evidence and a recommendation—proceed, revise, defer, or stop—for the applicable approval and launch-planning process. Excludes in-market pilot execution (CM-1-3-6); the analyses (CM-1-3-1); launch approval and release decisions (the applicable approval and launch-planning process, CM-1-3-5).\nIn scope: Test offer response with governed evidence and authorized tests | validate commercial viability and operational deliverability | check proposition consistency | produce validation evidence with a proceed/revise/defer/stop recommendation\nOut of scope: In-market execution (CM-1-3-6) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1) | launch approval and release decisions (approval process, CM-1-3-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Specified offers (CM-1-3-3-1-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cost-to-serve (CM-1-2-6-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed findings and research"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Validation evidence with a proceed/revise/defer/stop recommendation"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No offer reaches the market untested."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
