    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define KPI Framework"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20966"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Design the blueprint for how Marketing operates approved strategies and designs, including business-process architecture, role/capability requirements, organizational interfaces, procedural frameworks, control points, and measurement requirements, without setting headcount, appointing individuals, owning enterprise policy, or implementing technology architecture."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 24 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one operating-model design lifecycle; tactical. Review definition adopted verbatim: an architecture/blueprint process, never an organizational-decision, technology-architecture, HR, or policy owner. Lifecycle: Determine Channel Of Trade Mix (translation) → Develop Business Process Blueprint → Develop Organizational Blueprint → Define Procedural Framework & Guidelines → Define Operating Model Measurement Framework, with the process and organizational blueprints co-developed iteratively per review. Technology-implication statement verbatim in scope note — connects to the future System Integration and Domain Modeling workstreams without expanding scope. APQC 'Design resource model for KM approaches' is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operating Model Design"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the operating-model design lifecycle: translating the approved channel-of-trade mix into operating-model requirements (CM-1-3-3-6-3), developing the business process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1), developing the organizational blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-2), defining the procedural framework and guidelines (CM-1-3-3-6-4), and defining the operating-model measurement framework (CM-1-3-3-6-5). The process and organizational blueprints are co-developed iteratively; the listed order is a logical dependency, not a rigid one-way sequence. The blueprint may identify technology, data, integration, and automation requirements for subsequent architecture and delivery work, but it does not own enterprise architecture, solution design, product selection, implementation, or technical operation. The receiving end of the batch 23 structure-model boundary: blueprint-level design only — HR headcount, appointments, and management authority follow HR and management processes; enterprise policy stays with its accountable functions (batch 15 procedures-not-policy discipline); organizational/delivery-model neutrality applies (b10/15/16/20). Excludes HR headcount and appointments (HR, management); enterprise policy ownership (accountable functions); channel mix decisions (CM-1-3-2-4); channel system design (CM-1-3-3-3); enterprise architecture, solution design, and implementation (technology owners); enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream).\nIn scope: Run the operating-model design lifecycle | translate approved strategies and designs into process and organizational blueprints | define procedural frameworks within enterprise policies | identify technology, data, integration, and automation requirements for downstream architecture work | define operating-model measurement with KPI Store routing\nOut of scope: HR headcount and appointments (HR, management) | enterprise policy ownership (accountable functions) | channel mix (CM-1-3-2-4) | channel system design (CM-1-3-3-3) | enterprise/solution architecture and implementation (technology owners) | enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved strategies (CM-1-3-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "design outputs (CM-1-3-3-1/-2/-3/-4/-5)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operating performance evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The marketing operating-model blueprint: process, organizational, procedural, technology-requirement, and measurement designs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "An operating model designed for the strategy it serves."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10015"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop the business process blueprint for the marketing operating model — the end-to-end processes, handoffs, and control points through which the marketing strategies and designs operate — at blueprint level, for the operating processes to implement."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 24 (2026-09-20). Process-blueprint step; co-developed iteratively with the organizational blueprint (review note — the listed order is a logical dependency, not a rigid sequence). APQC 'Develop business strategy' is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.6.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop Business Process Blueprint"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers process blueprinting: mapping the marketing operating processes end-to-end against the approved strategies and designs; defining handoffs, control points, and decision rights at blueprint level (consistent with this taxonomy's decision-rights architecture); identifying process gaps and redundancies; and maintaining the blueprint as designs evolve. Co-developed iteratively with the organizational blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-2) per review. Blueprint, not implementation: process implementation, technology enablement, and continuous improvement belong to the operating processes and their owners. Excludes process implementation (operating processes); technology design (its owners); organizational blueprint content (CM-1-3-3-6-2); enterprise process governance (its owner).\nIn scope: Map end-to-end marketing operating processes against approved designs | define handoffs, control points, and decision rights at blueprint level | identify gaps and redundancies | maintain the blueprint\nOut of scope: Process implementation (operating processes) | technology design (its owners) | organizational blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-2) | enterprise process governance (its owner)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operating-model requirements (CM-1-3-3-6-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved designs (CM-1-3-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operating performance evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The marketing business process blueprint"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The marketing machine drawn before it is built."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10042"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop the organizational blueprint for the marketing operating model — the capabilities, roles, and organizational constructs the process blueprint requires — at blueprint level, without setting headcount or making appointments."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 24 (2026-09-20). Organizational-blueprint step; batch 23 headcount boundary is this row's governing rule; organizational neutrality per b10/15/16/20; co-developed iteratively with the process blueprint (review). APQC 'Develop and set organizational goals' is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.6.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop Organizational Blueprint"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers organizational blueprinting: deriving required capabilities and role types from the process blueprint; defining organizational constructs (teams, capability groupings, interfaces to Commercial, Finance, Legal, and operations) at blueprint level; stating capacity assumptions; and maintaining the blueprint, co-developed iteratively with the process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1). The batch 23 boundary governs: the blueprint defines desired roles, coverage, and capacity assumptions — it does not set HR headcount, job grading, compensation, operating-organization decisions, or individual appointments, which follow HR, management, and the applicable approval processes; organizational/delivery-model neutrality (b10/15/16/20) — the blueprint describes what the model requires, not the org chart. Excludes headcount approval, grading, compensation, and appointments (HR, management, approvals); the process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1).\nIn scope: Derive required capabilities and role types from the process blueprint | define organizational constructs and interfaces at blueprint level | state capacity assumptions | maintain the blueprint iteratively with the process blueprint\nOut of scope: Headcount, grading, compensation, and appointments (HR, management) | process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "capability assessments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "capacity assumptions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The marketing organizational blueprint"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The organization the process needs, described without naming names."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10127"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Translate Channel-of-Trade Mix into Operating Model Requirements"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Translate the approved channel-of-trade mix and channel-design outputs into the capabilities, processes, service models, role types, control requirements, technology needs, and organizational interfaces required to operate each channel — without deciding, revising, approving, or reopening the channel mix."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 24 (2026-09-20). Q3 decision (review: 'the most important boundary in the package'): translation, never re-decision — the locked name reads as a mix decision but the mix is owned at CM-1-3-2-4 (batch 22); the canonical interpretation is recorded verbatim in the scope note and the preferred label 'Translate Channel-of-Trade Mix into Operating Model Requirements' is PROMOTED in the naming-normalization backlog per review (high-value correction). Relations per review: uses-input from Channel Strategy and Channel Design (information dependency, not lifecycle sequence — translation iterates as approved strategy evolves), enables toward both blueprints. APQC 'Determine channel role and fit with target segments' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.6.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Determine Channel Of Trade Mix"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers mix translation: taking the approved channel-of-trade mix (CM-1-3-2-4) and channel-design outputs (CM-1-3-3-3) and determining what each channel requires of the operating model — capabilities, processes, service and support models, role types, control requirements, technology needs, and organizational interfaces; identifying operating-model implications of mix changes; and feeding requirements to the process and organizational blueprints (CM-1-3-3-6-1/-2). Determine Channel Of Trade Mix within Operating Model Design translates the approved channel-of-trade mix and channel-design outputs into the capabilities, processes, service models, role types, control requirements, technology needs, and organizational interfaces required to operate each channel. It does not decide, revise, approve, or reopen the channel mix. Mix decisions belong to Sales & Distribution Channel Strategy (CM-1-3-2-4) under its approvals. Excludes channel mix decisions (CM-1-3-2-4); channel system design (CM-1-3-3-3); partner management (CM-1-3-6-1). Determine Channel Of Trade Mix (CM-1-3-3-6-3) supplies channel-derived role, capability, capacity, and organizational-interface requirements that Develop Organizational Blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-2) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Determine operating-model requirements per channel of trade from the approved mix and channel design | identify operating-model implications of mix changes | feed requirements to the blueprints\nOut of scope: Channel mix decisions (CM-1-3-2-4) | channel system design (CM-1-3-3-3) | partner management (CM-1-3-6-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-2-4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved channel mix (CM-1-3-2-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel design outputs (CM-1-3-3-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operating capability evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operating-model requirements per channel of trade"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every channel in the approved mix operationally provided for."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/18627"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define the procedural frameworks and guidelines under which the marketing operating model runs — the standard procedures, working guidelines, and escalation paths that implement enterprise policies in marketing's operations — within, never in place of, the policies owned by their accountable functions."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 24 (2026-09-20). Procedural step; b15 procedures-not-policy discipline is the governing rule; review controlled-document requirement verbatim in scope note (owner, version, effective date, approval, review trigger, evidence requirements, escalation path) — supports the project's artifact-control principles. APQC 'Define communication guidelines and mechanisms' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.6.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Procedural Framework & Guidelines"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers procedural-framework definition: converting enterprise policies (commercial, pricing governance, privacy, compliance, brand) into marketing operating procedures, guidelines, and escalation paths; keeping procedures consistent with the process blueprint and decision-rights architecture; and maintaining them as policies and designs change. Procedures are controlled documents with owner, version, effective date, approval, review trigger, evidence requirements, and escalation path. The batch 15 procedures-not-policy discipline governs: this process writes procedures within policies — policy ownership stays with the accountable functions (Finance, Legal, Compliance, Data Governance, HR, and the batch 16 compliance architecture); formal Legal/Compliance interpretation is never this process's. Excludes policy ownership (accountable functions); compliance framework ownership (batch 16 architecture); procedure execution and adherence monitoring (operating processes, CM-1-3-6-8); the process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1).\nIn scope: Convert enterprise policies into controlled marketing procedures, guidelines, and escalation paths | keep procedures consistent with the blueprint and decision rights | maintain procedures as controlled documents as policies and designs change\nOut of scope: Policy ownership (accountable functions) | compliance framework ownership (batch 16 architecture) | formal Legal/Compliance interpretation (Legal, Compliance) | procedure execution/adherence monitoring (operating processes, CM-1-3-6-8) | process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Enterprise policies (accountable functions)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operating feedback"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "process blueprint (CM-1-3-3-6-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Controlled marketing procedural frameworks and guidelines"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Policies made usable at the working level, without being rewritten."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 24 (2026-09-20). Template row (batch 23 treatment); preferred label 'Define Operating Model Measurement Framework' queued prominently per review; full measurement-framework routing statement in scope note. APQC 'Define objectives' is a WEAK generic match. Step 3d naming pass (2026-09-21): renamed from 'Define KPI Framework' to 'Define Operating Model Measurement Framework' — critical semantic-collision resolution. Prior label retired from ontology aliases (a shared generic altLabel would recreate the collision); scoped historical alias 'Define KPI Framework (Operating Model)' recorded in the identity/migration map."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19521"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define the measurement framework for the marketing operating model — process performance, capability health, and operating-efficiency measures with their definitions, baselines, targets, and measurement responsibilities — as evidence-layer measures with governed routing toward enterprise KPIs."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.3.6.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define Operating Model Measurement Framework"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers operating-model measurement design. Defines domain-level measures, baselines, targets, measurement responsibilities, data sources, and review cadence needed to evaluate operating-model design outcomes. The framework may nominate measures as candidate KPIs but does not approve, publish, version, calculate, certify, or govern enterprise KPIs. Those activities follow the Enterprise Measurement Catalog, Candidate KPI Register, Enterprise KPI Catalog, and KPI Store governance process. Operating-model measures span process cycle and quality performance against the blueprint, capability health, and operating efficiency, aligned with the metrics stewarded at CM-1-3-1-6. Excludes enterprise KPI definition and KPI Store governance (KPI workstream); measurement execution (operating processes, CM-1-3-5-5); metrics stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6).\nIn scope: Define operating-model measures, baselines, targets, responsibilities, data sources, and review cadence | align with stewarded metrics | nominate candidate KPIs into KPI Store governance\nOut of scope: Enterprise KPI approval, publication, and governance (KPI Store workstream) | measurement execution (operating processes, CM-1-3-5-5) | metrics stewardship (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Blueprints and frameworks (CM-1-3-3-6-1/-2/-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "KPI Store classification rules"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "stewarded metric definitions (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The operating-model measurement framework (evidence-layer, KPI Store-routed)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The operating model measured against its blueprint."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/priorPreferredLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define KPI Framework (Operating Model)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Define KPI Framework"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "New product & service development process details step-by-step procedure to do feasibility study for a new product and conceptualize it, defines vision based on market need and developed implementation plan, and manages R&D collaboration, licensing & IP, and lifecycle management."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "New Product & Service Development"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16824"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Set the innovation vision and implementation plans for downstream products and services — where the company will innovate, which market needs and signals justify it, and how R&D effort will be mobilized — through a recurring visioning cycle grounded in the governed evidence base, so concept and development work runs against deliberate innovation direction."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one visioning-and-planning lifecycle; horizon strategic. Lifecycle: Market Sensing (continuous) and Identify Market Needs continuously inform each other → Develop R&D Implementation Plans → approved direction feeds concept/feasibility work. Vision-versus-strategy boundary and Q2 innovation-consumes-analysis rule (canonical wording) verbatim in scope note. APQC 'Develop plan for new product/service development and introduction/launch' is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Visioning And Implementation Planning"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the innovation-visioning lifecycle: continuous market sensing (CM-1-3-4-1-2), periodic identification of market needs on the innovation lens (CM-1-3-4-1-1), and development of R&D implementation plans (CM-1-3-4-1-3), with sensing and needs identification continuously informing each other. The innovation vision translates approved corporate, brand, proposition, portfolio, and market direction into innovation themes and implementation priorities. It does not establish corporate strategy, approve investment, or select the final R&D portfolio. Innovation processes consume governed findings from Marketing Analysis and may commission purpose-run research through approved research controls. They do not recreate Market, Consumer, Customer/Marketer, Competitor, or Company Analysis; maintain a competing evidence base; publish the enterprise demand forecast; or alter the governed forecast without the appropriate owner's process. Excludes the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); strategy ownership (CM-1-3-2, corporate strategy); concept and feasibility work (CM-1-3-4-2); development (CM-1-3-4-3); R&D portfolio selection and management (CM-1-3-4-5); R&D investment approval (delegated authorities). Visioning And Implementation Planning (CM-1-3-4-1) sets the innovation vision and the needs that justify it, which inform Concept & Feasibility Study (CM-1-3-4-2).\nIn scope: Run the recurring innovation-visioning cycle | maintain continuous market and technology sensing | identify market needs on the innovation lens from governed evidence | develop approval-ready R&D implementation plans\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1) | corporate strategy and strategy ownership (CM-1-3-2, corporate) | concept/feasibility (CM-1-3-4-2) | development (CM-1-3-4-3) | R&D portfolio selection (CM-1-3-4-5) | R&D investment approval (delegated authorities)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed insight (CM-1-3-1-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approved strategy direction (CM-1-3-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market and consumer findings (CM-1-3-1-1/-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "technology and external signals"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The innovation vision and approval-ready R&D implementation plans"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Innovation pointed at evidenced needs, not at whatever seems interesting."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10109"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify the market needs the innovation program should serve — unmet and emerging customer, consumer, and channel needs read from the governed evidence base on the innovation-opportunity lens — prioritized as innovation opportunities with their evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Needs step of the visioning lifecycle; opportunity-selection wording per review — prioritizes for exploration, never selects for funding; continuously informed by Market Sensing. APQC 'Identify market segments' STRONG, no validator — false-direction match (segmentation ≠ needs identification); comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify Market Needs"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers needs identification: reading governed findings (CM-1-3-1-1/-3/-4) and sensing signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2) for unmet and emerging needs; framing and prioritizing needs as innovation opportunities with evidence and confidence; and feeding prioritized needs to R&D planning (CM-1-3-4-1-3) and ideation (CM-1-3-4-2-1). Prioritizes needs for exploration and concept generation; delegated stage-gate and investment authorities select concepts for funded development. The innovation-opportunity lens of the Q2 rule: consumes the analyses, never re-performs them; personal data only through the governed findings and batch 21 controls. Excludes the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); demand forecasting (CM-1-1-1-1); concept selection for funded development (delegated stage-gate and investment authorities).\nIn scope: Read governed findings and signals for unmet and emerging needs | frame and prioritize needs as innovation opportunities with evidence | feed prioritized needs to planning and ideation\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1) | demand forecasting (CM-1-1-1-1) | concept selection for funded development (delegated authorities)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed findings (CM-1-3-1-1/-3/-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prior opportunity results"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sensing signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Prioritized market needs as innovation opportunities for exploration"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The needs worth innovating for, found in the evidence."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11424"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Continuously sense the market, technology, regulatory, and competitive signals relevant to downstream product and service innovation — a standing scan that feeds needs identification and planning with early, sourced, reliability-rated signals."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Sensing step; horizon continuous — a standing scan, not a cycle. Review classification verbatim in scope note: outputs are signals/hypotheses/watch items, never established market facts — they become governed findings only after validation through Concept Research, Marketing Analysis, or another accountable analysis process. Source classes per review recorded for traceability. Q2 rule and batch 21 competitor-information prohibition apply. APQC 'Review market performance' is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Market Sensing"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers innovation sensing: maintaining a standing scan of technology developments (fuels, energy transition, convenience, digital), regulatory trajectories, competitive moves (legitimate sources only, batch 21 prohibition), and market signals. Market Sensing records sourced, reliability-rated signals, emerging hypotheses, and watch items. Signals become governed findings only after appropriate validation through Concept Research, Marketing Analysis, or another accountable analysis process. Signals are recorded by source class — primary/public authority, licensed market/technology intelligence, partner/customer signal, internal operating signal, hypothesis/watch item — with reliability rating and provenance. Sensing complements, never duplicates, the recurring subject analyses (Q2 rule): a forward scan for innovation, not a governed market analysis. Excludes the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); improper competitive intelligence (prohibited, batch 21); regulatory interpretation (Legal, Regulatory). Market Sensing (CM-1-3-4-1-2) maintains the standing scan of market, technology, regulatory and competitive signals that informs Identify Market Needs (CM-1-3-4-1-1).\nIn scope: Maintain the standing innovation scan across technology, regulatory, competitive, and market signals | record signals by source class with reliability rating and provenance | feed signals to needs identification and planning as hypotheses, not established facts\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1) | improper competitive intelligence (prohibited) | regulatory interpretation (Legal, Regulatory) | publishing signals as governed findings (validation processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Technology and industry signals"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed findings (context)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "legitimate competitive observations"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "regulatory trajectories"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Sourced, reliability-rated innovation signals, hypotheses, and watch items"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Early signals reaching innovation before they become obvious — labeled as signals, not facts."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20624"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop the R&D implementation plans that mobilize the innovation vision — programs, priorities, capability and partner needs, and resource requirements — as approval-ready recommendations into the applicable delegated authorities."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Planning step of the visioning lifecycle; review investment distinction verbatim in scope note — plans recommend, delegated authorities commit people, capital, and budget. APQC 'Develop IT transformation plans' is a FALSE lexical match (IT plans, not R&D plans)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop R&D Implementation Plans"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers R&D planning: translating the innovation vision and prioritized needs into implementation plans. Develops approval-ready implementation plans with resource estimates, capability needs, external-collaboration needs, dependencies, risks, and proposed sequencing. Delegated investment, portfolio, staffing, procurement, and partnership authorities decide commitments. Portfolio management of the resulting R&D is Lifecycle Management's (CM-1-3-4-5, batch 26); collaboration execution is R&D Collaboration's (CM-1-3-4-6, batch 26). Excludes investment, staffing, procurement, and partnership commitments (delegated authorities); portfolio management (CM-1-3-4-5); development execution (CM-1-3-4-3); collaboration execution (CM-1-3-4-6). Where concept work considers the proposed R&D plans and priorities, Develop R&D Implementation Plans (CM-1-3-4-1-3) informs Concept & Feasibility Study (CM-1-3-4-2).\nIn scope: Translate vision and needs into approval-ready R&D implementation plans | state resource estimates, capability and collaboration needs, dependencies, risks, and sequencing | submit plans to the applicable delegated authorities\nOut of scope: Investment, staffing, procurement, and partnership commitments (delegated authorities) | portfolio management (CM-1-3-4-5) | development execution (CM-1-3-4-3) | collaboration execution (CM-1-3-4-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Innovation vision (CM-1-3-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "capability and partner assessments"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "prioritized needs (CM-1-3-4-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approval-ready R&D implementation plans"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "R&D effort mobilized against the vision, with the right approvals."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16824"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-ff-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and evaluate product and service concepts — ideation from evidenced needs, research on candidate concepts, and feasibility assessment across market, technical, commercial, and regulatory dimensions — so only concepts that survive evidence and feasibility reach development."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one per-candidate concept lifecycle; horizon event-driven. Lifecycle per review: Ideation → Conduct Research → feasibility evidence and recommendation → gate/delegated approval, with Manage Research as a governance overlay, not a third sequential step. Feasibility-conditionality, Q2 rule, and refined Q3 gate (regulated-party, fact-dependent) verbatim in scope note. APQC 'Develop plan for new product/service development and introduction/launch' is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Concept & Feasibility Study"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the concept lifecycle: ideation from prioritized needs and signals (CM-1-3-4-2-1) and research on candidate concepts (CM-1-3-4-2-2), producing feasibility evidence and a concept recommendation for gate and delegated approval of development entry, with Manage Research (CM-1-3-4-2-3) as the governance overlay that commissions, prioritizes, tracks, and assures research across the cycle. Feasibility conclusions are conditional evidence for stage-gate decision-making; they are not regulatory classification, product approval, investment approval, launch authorization, or legal clearance. Feasibility spans market, technical, commercial, operational, and regulatory dimensions, including early screening for the fuel-product regulatory gate: Where a proposed product is subject to US EPA fuel or fuel-additive registration requirements under 40 CFR Part 79, the applicable manufacturer, importer, or other regulated party must satisfy the relevant registration and testing requirements before the product is introduced into US commerce. Regulatory, Legal, Quality, Product Stewardship, and designated business owners determine applicability, regulated-party responsibility, submission requirements, and readiness. Innovation processes consume governed findings from Marketing Analysis and may commission purpose-run research through approved research controls. They do not recreate Market, Consumer, Customer/Marketer, Competitor, or Company Analysis; maintain a competing evidence base; publish the enterprise demand forecast; or alter the governed forecast without the appropriate owner's process. Consumer concept research operates under the batch 21 privacy controls and aggregate/de-identified default. Excludes development (CM-1-3-4-3); the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); regulatory classification and registration (Regulatory, Legal, Product Stewardship); stage-gate and investment approval (CM-1-3-4-3-1, delegated authorities). Concept & Feasibility Study (CM-1-3-4-2) develops concepts informed by the innovation vision and needs set by Visioning And Implementation Planning (CM-1-3-4-1). Product & Service Development (CM-1-3-4-3) develops products and services from the approved concepts produced by Concept & Feasibility Study (CM-1-3-4-2).\nIn scope: Run the concept-and-feasibility lifecycle per candidate | ideate from evidenced needs | research and assess feasibility across market, technical, commercial, and regulatory dimensions with early gate screening | deliver feasibility evidence and concept recommendations to the gates\nOut of scope: Development (CM-1-3-4-3) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1) | regulatory classification/registration (Regulatory, Legal, Product Stewardship) | stage-gate/investment approval (CM-1-3-4-3-1, delegated authorities)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1-3"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Prioritized needs (CM-1-3-4-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "feasibility and regulatory screening inputs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed findings and purpose-run research"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Feasibility evidence and concept recommendations for the gates"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Concepts killed cheaply on evidence before development pays for them."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16824"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Generate and shape product and service ideas from the prioritized needs, sensing signals, and collaboration inputs — a managed idea pipeline with capture, enrichment, and screening — feeding candidate concepts to research and feasibility."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Pipeline step; periodic — a standing idea pipeline with screening cycles. Review external-idea boundary verbatim in scope note — no implied compensation, ownership, confidentiality, or evaluation obligations outside approved Legal/IP procedures; anticipates the batch 26 licensing/IP cluster. APQC candidate is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.2.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Ideation"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers ideation: running idea generation against prioritized needs (CM-1-3-4-1-1) and signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2); capturing ideas from employees, customers and partners (through the CM-1-3-4-6 collaboration channels and their controls), and market evidence; enriching and screening ideas against the innovation vision; and promoting screened ideas as candidate concepts to research (CM-1-3-4-2-2). Ideas from external parties, customers, suppliers, inventors, and partners must be accepted only through approved intake channels and confidentiality/IP controls. The process must not create implied compensation, ownership, confidentiality, or evaluation obligations outside approved Legal/IP procedures. Excludes concept research (CM-1-3-4-2-2); development selection (stage gates); IP framework and unsolicited-idea procedure ownership (CM-1-3-4-4, Legal).\nIn scope: Generate and capture ideas against needs and signals | accept external ideas only through approved intake channels and confidentiality/IP controls | enrich and screen ideas against the vision | promote screened ideas as candidate concepts\nOut of scope: Concept research (CM-1-3-4-2-2) | development selection (stage gates) | IP framework and unsolicited-idea procedures (CM-1-3-4-4, Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Prioritized needs (CM-1-3-4-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "collaboration inputs through approved channels (CM-1-3-4-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sensing signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Screened candidate concepts"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A pipeline of ideas worth researching, captured cleanly."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10108"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-ff-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct the research that tests candidate concepts — customer and consumer concept research, technical investigation, and market and commercial assessment — producing feasibility evidence with stated confidence for the concept recommendation."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Research step; review research-plan quality control verbatim in scope note (decision use, methodology, participant/data controls, evidence standard, reliability, documentation proportionate to the decision); b21 privacy controls inherited; Q3 gate screening as a feasibility factor only. APQC 'Conduct customer and market research' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.2.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct Research"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers concept research execution: designing and running concept tests and studies within the batch 21 privacy controls (consumer research through governed controls, aggregate/de-identified publication default); technical investigation of formulation, service, and delivery feasibility; market and commercial assessment using governed findings and cost evidence; early regulatory screening against the Q3 gate dimensions; and stating results with confidence. Research plans must define intended decision use, methodology, participant/data controls, evidence standard, reliability/confidence, and reproducibility or documentation requirements proportionate to the decision. Research on candidate fuel products flags the potential Part 79 registration pathway as a feasibility factor — applicability, classification, and execution stay with the accountable Regulatory, Legal, Quality, and Product Stewardship functions. Excludes the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); research program governance (CM-1-3-4-2-3); regulatory classification (Regulatory, Legal); development (CM-1-3-4-3).\nIn scope: Design and run concept tests within privacy controls and research-plan standards | investigate technical and delivery feasibility | assess market and commercial feasibility from governed evidence | flag potential regulatory-gate factors with stated confidence\nOut of scope: The analyses (CM-1-3-1) | research governance (CM-1-3-4-2-3) | regulatory classification (Regulatory, Legal) | development (CM-1-3-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/assuredBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Candidate concepts (CM-1-3-4-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed findings and research capacity"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "technical and regulatory screening inputs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Concept feasibility evidence with confidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Concept verdicts earned with evidence, not enthusiasm."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage the concept-research activity — commissioning, standards, quality, and completion of the studies the concept lifecycle runs — so research is governed, comparable, and compliant without this process performing the research itself."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Governance overlay of the concept lifecycle (review: not a strict third sequential step) — manages studies, never performs them; procurement/contracting boundary verbatim in scope note; scoped away from batch 26's Manage R&D Portfolios. APQC 'Manage routings' is a FALSE match (manufacturing routings)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.2.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Research"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers research management as the concept lifecycle's governance overlay: commissioning and prioritizing concept studies against the pipeline; setting study standards (method quality, documentation, evidence lineage per the batch 21 Document Findings discipline); ensuring studies operate within the privacy, consent, and competitive-information controls; tracking completion and spend against the research plan; and maintaining the concept-research record. Research procurement, supplier contracting, data licensing, and external-study execution follow Procurement, Legal, Privacy, and applicable delegated authorities. Manages concept/feasibility studies only: the governed subject analyses belong to CM-1-3-1, and R&D portfolio management to CM-1-3-4-5 (batch 26). Excludes performing research (CM-1-3-4-2-2); the subject analyses (CM-1-3-1); R&D portfolio management (CM-1-3-4-5); procurement, contracting, and data licensing (Procurement, Legal, Privacy, delegated authorities); privacy/ethics framework ownership (governance owners).\nIn scope: Commission and prioritize concept studies | set study standards with evidence lineage | ensure privacy and competitive-information compliance | track completion and spend\nOut of scope: Research execution (CM-1-3-4-2-2) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1) | R&D portfolio (CM-1-3-4-5) | procurement/contracting/data licensing (Procurement, Legal, Privacy) | privacy/ethics frameworks (governance owners)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Concept pipeline (CM-1-3-4-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "research plan and budget"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "study standards and controls"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The governed concept-research program and record"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Research that is governed and comparable across every concept."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19990"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-ff-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop new and improved downstream products and services from approved concepts — governed development programs, per-product development execution, and controlled product and service change — within the applicable regulatory and quality gates, so what reaches offers and launch is developed, compliant, and controlled."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — governed stage-gate development cycle (b03/08 per-variant pattern at the execution child); horizon tactical. Review statements verbatim in scope note: development completion is not launch authorization; product-versus-service distinction (gates vary by offering); refined Q3 gate (regulated-party, fact-dependent); adjacent gates determined by accountable functions; cross-functional execution qualifier (organizational neutrality, b10/15/16/20 line); Q2 rule. APQC 'Define product/service development requirements' 0.75 STRONG — genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Product & Service Development"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the development cluster: coordinating the development program and its stage gates (CM-1-3-4-3-1), conducting per-product and per-service development (CM-1-3-4-3-2), and managing product and service change (CM-1-3-4-3-3), as a stage-gate cycle (gates → development → evidence and readiness → gate outcome to iterate, hold, stop, or advance → controlled change) rather than a pure line. Development completion is not authorization to sell, manufacture, distribute, market, or launch. Commercial availability requires completion of all applicable regulatory, quality, product-master, supply, tax, pricing, legal, channel, offer, launch, and delegated approval controls. Product development may include fuels, additives, lubricants, blend components, packaged products, and related physical offerings. Service development may include commercial programs, convenience/retail services, digital services, loyalty propositions, and channel/customer services. Regulatory and quality gates vary by the nature of the offering. Where a proposed product is subject to US EPA fuel or fuel-additive registration requirements under 40 CFR Part 79, the applicable manufacturer, importer, or other regulated party must satisfy the relevant registration and testing requirements before the product is introduced into US commerce. Regulatory, Legal, Quality, Product Stewardship, and designated business owners determine applicability, regulated-party responsibility, submission requirements, and readiness. Applicable regulatory, quality, product-stewardship, tax, legal, environmental, and operational gate requirements are determined by the accountable functions for the specific product/service, market, and route to market. The capability is located in the Marketing product/service innovation branch because it governs market-facing offerings. Development execution may be performed by cross-functional product, R&D, quality, engineering, operations, digital, or partner teams according to the operating model. Innovation processes consume governed findings from Marketing Analysis and may commission purpose-run research through approved research controls. They do not recreate Market, Consumer, Customer/Marketer, Competitor, or Company Analysis; maintain a competing evidence base; publish the enterprise demand forecast; or alter the governed forecast without the appropriate owner's process. Downstream separation: offers assemble developed products (CM-1-3-3-1); launch runs through Planning and Execution (CM-1-3-5/6); portfolio and lifecycle decisions at CM-1-3-4-5 and licensing/IP at CM-1-3-4-4 (batch 26); product master data at CM-1-3-7-1; fuel quality operations with the quality management processes (batch 18 architecture). Excludes offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); launch planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6); portfolio/lifecycle decisions (CM-1-3-4-5); licensing/IP (CM-1-3-4-4); regulatory registration execution (Regulatory, Legal, Product Stewardship); quality operations (quality processes, batch 18); product master data (CM-1-3-7-1). Product & Service Development (CM-1-3-4-3) develops products and services from the approved concepts produced by Concept & Feasibility Study (CM-1-3-4-2). Product & Service Development (CM-1-3-4-3) provides development outcomes that inform Lifecycle Management (CM-1-3-4-5).\nIn scope: Coordinate the development program and stage gates | conduct per-product and per-service development within the applicable gates | manage controlled product and service change | hand developed products to offers, launch, and master data through their controls\nOut of scope: Offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | launch (CM-1-3-5/6) | portfolio/lifecycle (CM-1-3-4-5) | licensing/IP (CM-1-3-4-4) | regulatory registration execution (Regulatory, Legal, Product Stewardship) | quality operations (batch 18 processes) | product master data (CM-1-3-7-1) | authorization to sell or launch (downstream controls)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved concepts with feasibility evidence (CM-1-3-4-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "R&D implementation plans (CM-1-3-4-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "regulatory and quality gate requirements from the accountable functions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Developed, gate-reviewed products and services with controlled specifications"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Products and services that arrive developed, compliant, and controlled — not improvised."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19696"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate the product and service development program — evidence-based stage-gate reviews, development standards, cross-functional coordination, and program-level tracking — recording gate outcomes under the applicable delegation of authority."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Governance child; review authority qualification verbatim — coordinates reviews and records outcomes under delegated authority, grants no approval itself. APQC 'Govern and manage product/service development program' 0.8 STRONG — genuine anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.3.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Product/Service Development"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers development governance: coordinating evidence-based stage-gate reviews (concept entry, development, validation, pre-launch readiness) and recording outcomes under the applicable delegation of authority; setting development standards (documentation, specification control, testing evidence); convening the functions each gate requires (Regulatory, Quality, Legal, Product Stewardship, supply, operations, Finance); and tracking the program. Gate outcomes never substitute for regulatory, quality, investment, launch, or commercial approval by their accountable owners; where the Q3 gate applies, its requirements are built into gate criteria with readiness determined by the accountable functions. Excludes development execution (CM-1-3-4-3-2); investment, regulatory, launch, and commercial approval (their accountable authorities); regulatory and quality clearance (their owners); portfolio prioritization (CM-1-3-4-5).\nIn scope: Coordinate evidence-based stage-gate reviews with the required functions | record gate outcomes under delegated authority | set development standards and specification control | track the development program\nOut of scope: Development execution (CM-1-3-4-3-2) | investment/regulatory/launch/commercial approval (accountable authorities) | regulatory/quality clearance (their owners) | portfolio prioritization (CM-1-3-4-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved concepts (CM-1-3-4-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "function readiness inputs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "gate criteria and standards"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Recorded stage-gate outcomes and program status under delegated authority"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every development effort gated on evidence, with the right people at the gate."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11428"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-ff-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct the development of each product or service — specification, formulation or service design, testing and validation, and pre-launch readiness evidence — from gate entry to development completion under the program's standards."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Execution child — the b03/08 per-variant lifecycle; review test/clearance distinction verbatim — development generates evidence for, and coordinates with, the accountable functions; it owns no testing classification or submission. Change control applies during late development, validation, and after release (see CM-1-3-4-3-3 relation rule). APQC 'Conduct new product development process assessment' STRONG, no validator — adjacent (assessment vs execution); comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.3.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Conduct Product Development"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers per-product development execution: developing specifications and formulations (fuels, additives, lubricants, blend components, packaged products) or service designs (commercial programs, convenience/retail, digital, loyalty, channel/customer services); planning and executing testing and validation, including testing and evidence generation that may be required for an applicable fuel/additive registration or other regulatory pathway, coordinated with the accountable Regulatory, Quality, Product Stewardship, and Legal functions; assembling pre-launch readiness evidence for the gates; and documenting the developed product under specification control. Where the Q3 gate applies, the regulated party's registration precedes introduction into US commerce — applicability and readiness are the accountable functions' determinations. Excludes gate coordination and outcomes (CM-1-3-4-3-1); registration submission and regulatory clearance (Regulatory, Legal, Product Stewardship); quality operations (batch 18 processes); launch (CM-1-3-5/6); offer assembly (CM-1-3-3-1).\nIn scope: Develop specifications, formulations, and service designs | plan and execute testing and evidence generation coordinated with the accountable functions | assemble pre-launch readiness evidence | document under specification control\nOut of scope: Gate coordination (CM-1-3-4-3-1) | registration submission/regulatory clearance (Regulatory, Legal, Product Stewardship) | quality operations (batch 18) | launch (CM-1-3-5/6) | offer assembly (CM-1-3-3-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Gate-entered concepts (CM-1-3-4-3-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "development standards"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "testing and validation capacity"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Developed products and services with validation evidence under specification control"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Each product developed to spec, tested, and ready for its gates."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10061"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-epa-ff-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage controlled change to existing products and services by assessing specification, formulation, service-design, regulatory, quality, supply, customer, pricing, tax, data, offer, channel, inventory, and operational impacts; obtaining required approvals; and coordinating effective-dated implementation and transition."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 25 (2026-09-20). Change-control child; review definition adopted verbatim with the broadened impact domains and effective-dated transition. Regulated-characteristic changes are potential triggers — Regulatory and Legal determine the applicable action (review wording verbatim in scope note). Relation rule (the decision owner, review): change control 'governs-change-to' development outputs and 'may-follow' release rather than strictly following Conduct Product Development — these relation types are vocabulary-missing, so the strict precedes/follows chain is omitted per the batch 10 conditional-relation precedent and this rule is recorded verbatim: change control can apply during late development, validation, post-release maintenance, or service evolution. APQC 'Manage product and service portfolio' STRONG, no validator — adjacent match (portfolio is CM-1-3-4-5's); comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.3.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Product/Service Change"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers change control: capturing and classifying proposed product and service changes; assessing impacts across specification, formulation, and service design; regulatory and quality; supply, refining, inventory, terminal, and distribution; customer and contract commitments; pricing and taxation; labels, claims, and communications; product master data; offers and channels; digital and service support; and existing-stock, run-out, and transition management. Changes to composition, concentration, intended use, manufacturing source, specification, or other regulated characteristics may require regulatory-impact assessment, amended registration, further testing, revised labeling, or other approvals. Regulatory and Legal determine the applicable action. Routes changes through the applicable approvals and coordinates effective-dated implementation with the affected processes (offers CM-1-3-3-1, master data CM-1-3-7-1, quality processes, supply, channels). Change control is the development-side discipline and applies during late development, validation, post-release maintenance, and service evolution; portfolio decisions to retire or reposition products are Lifecycle Management's (CM-1-3-4-5, batch 26). Excludes portfolio/retirement decisions (CM-1-3-4-5); regulatory action execution (Regulatory, Legal); quality operations (batch 18); master data maintenance (CM-1-3-7-1).\nIn scope: Capture and classify product and service changes | assess the full impact domains including customer, pricing, tax, data, inventory, and transition | obtain required approvals | coordinate effective-dated implementation and transition\nOut of scope: Portfolio/retirement decisions (CM-1-3-4-5) | regulatory action execution (Regulatory, Legal) | quality operations (batch 18) | master data maintenance (CM-1-3-7-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Change proposals"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "approval requirements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "impact assessment inputs from the affected functions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Controlled, approved, effective-dated product and service changes with transition plans"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "No change sneaks past the gates the product already earned."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19696"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-uspto-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The capability to manage the company's intellectual assets and licensing on the business side — maintaining the intellectual-asset framework, coordinating registration, valuing assets for decisions, protecting assets operationally, exploiting them commercially, and stewarding the asset portfolio — with all IP legal work executed by Legal & Corporate Communications."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: capability — six concurrent, differently cadenced control functions failing the single-lifecycle test (b04/07/11/12/15/21 pattern); horizon continuous. Review ownership decision: cross-functional — the operating-model note verbatim in scope note and the responsible_domain set to a cross-functional value (b15 free-text precedent); the taxonomy location prescribes no single owner. IP legal boundary on the b14 prepare/coordinate-never-execute pattern, with the review's legal-determination exclusion verbatim. APQC 'Govern and manage product/service development program' is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Licensing & IP"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers six concurrent functions: the intellectual-asset framework (CM-1-3-4-4-1), registration coordination (CM-1-3-4-4-2), valuation for decisions (CM-1-3-4-4-3), operational protection (CM-1-3-4-4-4), commercial exploitation (CM-1-3-4-4-5), and portfolio stewardship (CM-1-3-4-4-6). Operating-model note: This capability is cross-functional. Legal & Corporate Communications owns legal IP policy, filings, prosecution, enforcement, agreement drafting, execution, and legal advice. Commercial, Marketing, Product, R&D, and Innovation functions own business opportunity identification, commercial valuation evidence, use cases, licensing-business input, brand alignment, and portfolio recommendations within delegated authority. The taxonomy location does not prescribe a single organizational owner. Business-side asset identification, business input, commercial valuation, operational protection, exploitation opportunity identification, and portfolio stewardship are in scope. Legal work—filings, prosecution, maintenance filings, enforcement, litigation, drafting, review, and execution of IP/confidentiality/license agreements—belongs to Legal. Business recommendations and delegated commercial choices do not constitute legal determinations regarding registrability, patentability, freedom to operate, ownership, inventorship, infringement, validity, enforceability, confidentiality obligations, or territorial protection strategy. Those matters are determined by Legal and its authorized IP counsel. Intellectual assets span patents, trademarks (central to the branded-marketer and brand-licensing model, batches 21/22), trade secrets and know-how, copyrights, and data assets where classified as intellectual assets. Licensing economics operate within the pricing and commercial approval frameworks (batch 23); brand licensing aligns with Brand Strategy (CM-1-3-2-1) and, where franchise arrangements are affected, the batch 22 fact-dependent PMPA statement. Excludes IP legal work of every kind (Legal, locked rule); accounting valuation and impairment (Finance lock); brand strategy (CM-1-3-2-1); development of the underlying products (CM-1-3-4-3); R&D portfolio management (CM-1-3-4-5). When R&D Collaboration handles intellectual assets or external-party intake under the approved business framework, Manage Licensing & IP (CM-1-3-4-4) maintains the business intellectual-asset handling, intake, and confidentiality framework within which R&D Collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6) operates; the recipient retains its other decisions and authorities.\nIn scope: Maintain the intellectual-asset framework | coordinate registration through Legal | value assets for business decisions | protect assets operationally | exploit assets commercially under delegated authority | steward the asset portfolio\nOut of scope: IP legal work and legal determinations (Legal, locked rule) | accounting valuation/impairment (Finance) | brand strategy (CM-1-3-2-1) | product development (CM-1-3-4-3) | R&D portfolio (CM-1-3-4-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/capability"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Development outputs (CM-1-3-4-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand direction (CM-1-3-2-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "legal advice and registrations status (Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed intellectual-asset decisions, coordination, and portfolio stewardship"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The company's ideas, marks, and know-how managed as assets, with Legal executing the law."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19696"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Establish and maintain the intellectual-asset framework — asset categories, identification and disclosure procedures, ownership and decision-rights principles, and handling rules — operationalizing approved Legal IP policy, so intellectual assets are recognized and handled consistently from creation."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Framework function of the IP capability; review element list adopted (categories, disclosure/intake, decision rights, classification/handling, confidentiality/trade-secret, external submissions, brand/trademark use guidance, documentation/provenance, retention/access, Legal escalation); operationalizes Legal policy, never sets it (b15 discipline); capitalization normalized in the queued label. APQC candidate is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Set up Intellectual Asset Framework"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers framework setup: defining asset categories (patentable inventions, marks, trade secrets/know-how, copyrights, data assets); establishing identification, disclosure/intake, and external idea/submission procedures; setting classification, handling, confidentiality and trade-secret handling, documentation/provenance, retention and access principles, and brand/trademark use guidance; setting business decision rights under the applicable delegation of authority; and defining escalation paths to Legal. The framework operationalizes approved Legal IP policy and business procedures — it does not set legal IP policy (batch 15 procedures-not-policy discipline). External-party intake follows the batch 25 idea-intake boundary. Excludes IP legal policy and its interpretation (Legal); the file/protect/exploit executions (sibling processes); HR and contractual IP terms (Legal, HR). Set up Intellectual Asset Framework (CM-1-3-4-4-1) maintains the intellectual-asset classification, confidentiality, handling, and decision-rights framework within which Protect Intellectual Assets (CM-1-3-4-4-4) operates; the recipient retains its other decisions and authorities.\nIn scope: Define asset categories and disclosure/intake procedures including external submissions | set classification, handling, provenance, retention, and access principles | set business decision rights under delegated authority | define escalation paths to Legal\nOut of scope: IP legal policy (Legal) | registration/protection/exploitation execution (siblings) | employment and contractual IP terms (Legal, HR)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Legal IP policies"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "development and collaboration activity"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "disclosure submissions"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/strategic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The maintained intellectual-asset framework and procedures"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every valuable idea recognized and handled correctly from the day it exists."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11049"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-uspto-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate the registration of registrable intellectual property — identifying registrable assets, preparing business input, and developing business recommendations for Legal-executed filings and maintenance — never filing, prosecuting, or making legal determinations itself."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Registration coordination on the b14 pattern; review decision-right qualification verbatim — business recommendations under the framework and delegated authority, with Legal and IP counsel determining legal viability, filing strategy, and execution. APQC 'Protect intellectual property' STRONG, no validator — adjacent (protection sibling); comparative only."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Register Intellectual Property"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers registration coordination: identifying registrable assets from disclosures and development outputs; preparing business input (commercial significance, markets, use evidence for trademarks). Develop and submit business recommendations regarding filing, trade-secret treatment, defensive publication, maintenance, or abandonment under the applicable framework and delegated authority; Legal and IP counsel determine legal viability, filing strategy, and execution. Coordinates filing, prosecution responses, and maintenance actions through Legal and its outside counsel, in the US (USPTO) and other jurisdictions per the business footprint. Registration effects and refusal risks (e.g., likelihood of confusion for marks) are Legal's assessment; the owner's enforcement responsibility is exercised through CM-1-3-4-4-4 and Legal. Excludes filing, prosecution, and maintenance execution (Legal, locked rule); legal viability and filing strategy (Legal, IP counsel); enforcement (CM-1-3-4-4-4 coordination, Legal execution); trade-secret handling (CM-1-3-4-4-4).\nIn scope: Identify registrable assets | prepare business input for filings | develop and submit file/secret/publish/maintain/abandon recommendations under delegated authority | coordinate Legal-executed filings and maintenance\nOut of scope: Filing/prosecution/maintenance execution (Legal) | legal viability and filing strategy (Legal, IP counsel) | enforcement (CM-1-3-4-4-4, Legal) | trade-secret handling (CM-1-3-4-4-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Disclosures and development outputs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Legal advice"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "framework decision rights (CM-1-3-4-4-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Registration recommendations and Legal-executed filings status"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The right assets recommended for registration, through Legal, in the right markets."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19696"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assess the commercial value of intellectual assets — their contribution, market relevance, and licensing potential — as decision evidence for protection, exploitation, and portfolio choices, without owning financial valuation policy."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Valuation function; review separation verbatim — commercial decision evidence only, never transfer pricing, tax, royalty, license-fee, or accounting determinations; Finance valuation lock applies. APQC candidate is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Value Intellectual Assets"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers commercial valuation for decisions: assessing asset contribution to products, brands, and channels; market relevance and remaining life; licensing potential and comparable evidence; and supplying value assessments to exploitation (CM-1-3-4-4-5) and portfolio stewardship (CM-1-3-4-4-6), stated with assumptions and confidence (b21 evidence discipline). The commercial assessment may inform licensing, product, partnership, or portfolio choices. It does not establish transfer prices, tax value, royalty rates, license fees, accounting value, impairment, capitalization, or financial-reporting treatment. The Finance lock governs accounting treatment of intangibles (batch 15 architecture). Excludes transfer prices, tax value, royalty rates, and license fees (their accountable processes and approvals); accounting valuation and impairment (Finance); the portfolio decisions themselves (CM-1-3-4-4-6, CM-1-3-4-5). Value Intellectual Assets (CM-1-3-4-4-3) provides asset valuations as decision evidence that informs Manage Intellectual Asset Portfolios (CM-1-3-4-4-6).\nIn scope: Assess commercial contribution, relevance, and licensing potential | state assumptions and confidence | supply value evidence to exploitation and portfolio decisions\nOut of scope: Transfer prices, tax value, royalty rates, license fees (accountable processes) | accounting valuation/impairment (Finance) | portfolio decisions (CM-1-3-4-4-6, CM-1-3-4-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Asset portfolio (CM-1-3-4-4-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market and licensing evidence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "usage in products and brands"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial value assessments with assumptions and confidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Knowing what the assets are commercially worth before deciding what to do with them."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11049"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-uspto-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Protect intellectual assets operationally — confidentiality and trade-secret practice, misuse monitoring, and coordination of enforcement through Legal — continuously, across everything the framework classifies as worth protecting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Protection function; continuous; enforcement on the b14 coordinate-never-execute pattern; review Security boundary verbatim — business handling discipline and escalation here, security frameworks and enforcement with their accountable owners; monitoring under the b21 legitimate-sources discipline. APQC 'Protect intellectual property' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Protect Intellectual Assets"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers operational protection: applying the framework's handling rules (marking, access discipline, need-to-know, secure collaboration practice per CM-1-3-4-6 channels); maintaining trade-secret discipline; monitoring for potential misuse, infringement, and unauthorized disclosure from legitimate sources; and preparing and coordinating enforcement responses through Legal — cease-and-desist, opposition, litigation, and settlement are Legal's to execute and the applicable authorities' to approve. This process applies business handling discipline and escalates potential misuse, unauthorized disclosure, or infringement. Security incident response, cybersecurity controls, access provisioning, forensic investigation, and data-governance enforcement remain with their accountable owners. Excludes enforcement execution and litigation (Legal); security incident response, cybersecurity controls, access provisioning, and forensic investigation (Security, Data Governance); registration (CM-1-3-4-4-2); confidentiality agreement drafting (Legal).\nIn scope: Apply handling and trade-secret discipline | monitor for misuse and infringement from legitimate sources | escalate and coordinate enforcement through Legal\nOut of scope: Enforcement execution/litigation (Legal) | security incident response, cyber controls, access provisioning, forensics (Security, Data Governance) | registration (CM-1-3-4-4-2) | agreement drafting (Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Framework handling rules (CM-1-3-4-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Legal advice"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "monitoring signals"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Operational protection and coordinated enforcement responses"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assets that stay protectable because they were handled as if they mattered."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19696"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exploit intellectual assets commercially — licensing out, brand and technology licensing arrangements, and contribution to products and partnerships — negotiating business terms within delegated authority while Legal drafts and executes every agreement."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Exploitation function; review commercial-terms boundary verbatim — proposals consistent with pricing, brand, product, franchise, competition-law, tax, export-control, and delegated-authority requirements; b20 Legal-coordinated execution and b22 PMPA fact-dependence where franchise arrangements are touched. APQC candidate is a WEAK false-direction match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Exploit Intellectual Assets"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers commercial exploitation: identifying exploitation opportunities from value assessments (CM-1-3-4-4-3); shaping licensing and partnership structures (brand licensing consistent with Brand Strategy CM-1-3-2-1 and brand standards CM-1-3-6-7; technology licensing consistent with R&D collaboration commitments); and negotiating business terms within delegated authority. Commercial proposals must be consistent with approved pricing, brand, product, franchise, competition-law, tax, export-control, and delegated-authority requirements. Legal drafts, reviews, negotiates legal terms, and executes agreements through authorized signatories. Where brand licensing touches franchise arrangements, the batch 22 fact-dependent PMPA statement applies. Excludes agreement drafting, legal-term negotiation, and execution (Legal, authorized signatories); approvals beyond delegated authority (commercial approvals); brand standards enforcement (CM-1-3-6-7); royalty accounting and collection (Finance, settlement processes).\nIn scope: Identify exploitation opportunities from value evidence | shape licensing and partnership structures consistent with brand and collaboration commitments | negotiate business terms within delegated authority and the applicable requirement set | coordinate agreements through Legal\nOut of scope: Agreement drafting/legal terms/execution (Legal, authorized signatories) | approvals beyond delegated authority (commercial approvals) | brand standards enforcement (CM-1-3-6-7) | royalty accounting/collection (Finance, settlements)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Legal and commercial approvals"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Value assessments (CM-1-3-4-4-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "brand and collaboration commitments"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/event-driven"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Negotiated, Legal-executed licensing and exploitation arrangements"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assets earning their keep, on terms Legal wrote."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19224"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-uspto-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Steward the intellectual-asset portfolio — the maintained inventory of assets and registrations, their cost and value balance, and recommendations to maintain, renew, license, or prune — coordinated through Legal for every registration action."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Portfolio function of the IP capability; review discontinuance-risk statement verbatim — abandonment recommendations consider contracts, claims, channel/franchise commitments, registrations, customer commitments, and live enforcement/defense matters; scoped against CM-1-3-4-5's portfolios. APQC 'Manage asset construction' is a FALSE match (construction assets)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.4.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Responsible domain detail: Cross-functional (Legal & Corporate Communications / Commercial & Marketing)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Intellectual Asset Portfolios"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers portfolio stewardship: maintaining the asset and registration inventory with status, markets, and renewal calendar; reviewing value-versus-cost using CM-1-3-4-4-3 assessments; recommending maintain/renew/license/abandon actions under the framework's decision rights and delegated authority; and coordinating resulting registration actions through Legal. Recommendations to abandon, lapse, or cease maintaining an asset must consider active contracts, product claims, channel/franchise commitments, regulatory registrations, customer commitments, and ongoing enforcement or defense matters. Portfolio here is the intellectual-asset portfolio; product, service, and R&D portfolios belong to Lifecycle Management (CM-1-3-4-5). Excludes renewal and abandonment filings (Legal); product/service/R&D portfolio management (CM-1-3-4-5); accounting for intangibles (Finance).\nIn scope: Maintain the asset and registration inventory with renewal calendar | review value versus cost | recommend maintain/renew/license/abandon under delegated authority with discontinuance risks assessed | coordinate registration actions through Legal\nOut of scope: Renewal/abandonment filings (Legal) | product/service/R&D portfolios (CM-1-3-4-5) | intangibles accounting (Finance)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Registration status (Legal)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "renewal costs"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "value assessments (CM-1-3-4-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The stewarded intellectual-asset portfolio with maintain/renew/prune recommendations"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A portfolio kept deliberately — nothing renewed by inertia, nothing lost by neglect."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Cross-functional"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16824"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage the lifecycle and portfolio of downstream products, services, and R&D initiatives by identifying technology needs, valuing and assessing portfolio elements, and developing evidence-based stage, stop, accelerate, extend, reposition, and retirement recommendations for the applicable delegated authorities."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one identify-value-assess-recommend portfolio cycle; horizon periodic. Review definition adopted verbatim (adds 'extend' — reinvestment, renovation, reformulation, repackaging, relaunch); portfolio split recorded (product/service vs R&D vs technology needs vs IP-separate); transition statement verbatim — recommendations become effective-dated transition plans through the accountable processes (the batch 25 change-control link made concrete). Lifecycle order: Identify Technology Needs/Opportunities → Value Projects/Portfolios → Assess Portfolios → Manage R&D Portfolios (develop recommendations and track decisions). APQC candidate is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Lifecycle Management"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the portfolio-and-lifecycle cycle: identifying technology needs and opportunities (CM-1-3-4-5-1), valuing projects and portfolio elements (CM-1-3-4-5-2), assessing portfolio composition and lifecycle status (CM-1-3-4-5-3), and developing portfolio recommendations and tracking delegated decisions (CM-1-3-4-5-4), with approved changes fed to change control, development, and operations. The portfolio split per review: the product and service portfolio (in-market offerings, lifecycle stage, performance, retire/reposition/extend decisions), the R&D portfolio (concept, research, and development programs; stage/stop/accelerate priorities), and technology needs (capability gaps feeding R&D planning) are managed here; the IP portfolio is separate under Licensing & IP (CM-1-3-4-4-6). Extension includes reinvestment, renovation, reformulation, repackaging, and relaunch candidates. Lifecycle recommendations affecting in-market products or services must be translated into effective-dated change, run-out, customer/partner communication, contract, pricing, tax, master-data, inventory, supply, quality, regulatory, and operating transition plans by the accountable processes. Commercial valuation evidence follows the b21 discipline; financial valuation policy is Finance's (lock). Excludes investment and portfolio approval (delegated authorities); change implementation (CM-1-3-4-3-3, accountable processes); development execution (CM-1-3-4-3); financial valuation policy (Finance); intellectual-asset portfolios (CM-1-3-4-4-6); enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream). Lifecycle Management (CM-1-3-4-5) provides lifecycle recommendations that inform Manage Product/Service Change (CM-1-3-4-3-3); change decisions follow the applicable delegated authorities. Lifecycle Management (CM-1-3-4-5) steers the portfolio informed by the outcomes of Product & Service Development (CM-1-3-4-3).\nIn scope: Run the portfolio-and-lifecycle cycle | identify technology needs and opportunities | value and assess the product, service, and R&D portfolios | develop stage/stop/accelerate/extend/reposition/retire recommendations and track delegated decisions\nOut of scope: Investment/portfolio approval (delegated authorities) | change implementation (CM-1-3-4-3-3, accountable processes) | development execution (CM-1-3-4-3) | financial valuation policy (Finance) | IP portfolios (CM-1-3-4-4-6) | enterprise KPI definition (KPI workstream)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-1-6"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Development and market evidence (CM-1-3-4-3, CM-1-3-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "portfolio performance data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sensing signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidence-based portfolio and lifecycle recommendations for the delegated authorities"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A portfolio that is composed on purpose, pruned on evidence."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16793"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify the technology needs and opportunities the product and R&D portfolios imply — capability gaps, emerging technologies worth evaluating, and renewal needs — feeding portfolio valuation and R&D planning."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). First step of the portfolio cycle; review boundary verbatim — business capability/research needs, never architecture or implementation (Process Excellence & IT ownership consistent, b24 line). APQC 'Identify restructuring opportunities' is a FALSE lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.5.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Identify Technology Needs/Opportunities"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers technology needs identification on the portfolio lens: reading portfolio assessments, development experience, sensing signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2, as signals not facts, per the batch 25 classification), and collaboration inputs (CM-1-3-4-6) for technology gaps and opportunities; framing them with evidence for valuation (CM-1-3-4-5-2) and R&D planning (CM-1-3-4-1-3). Technology needs are expressed as business capability/research needs, not solution architecture, product selection, infrastructure standards, or implementation decisions. Distinct from Market Sensing (forward scan) and from technology-architecture ownership (technology owners, batch 24 boundary). Excludes solution architecture, product selection, infrastructure standards, and implementation decisions (technology owners); R&D plan development (CM-1-3-4-1-3); the valuation (CM-1-3-4-5-2).\nIn scope: Read portfolio, development, sensing, and collaboration evidence for technology gaps and opportunities | express needs as business capability/research needs with evidence\nOut of scope: Solution architecture, product selection, infrastructure standards, implementation (technology owners) | R&D planning (CM-1-3-4-1-3) | valuation (CM-1-3-4-5-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Portfolio assessments (CM-1-3-4-5-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "collaboration inputs (CM-1-3-4-6)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sensing signals (CM-1-3-4-1-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-2"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced technology needs and opportunities as business capability/research needs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The portfolio's technology gaps named before they become surprises."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20664"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Value R&D projects and the product and service portfolios for prioritization — commercial value, strategic fit, risk, resource demand, and option value with stated assumptions and confidence — as decision evidence, not financial accounting."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Valuation step; review commercial-valuation statement and optionality/uncertainty dimensions verbatim; Finance valuation lock continued. APQC 'Prioritize IT projects' is a FALSE lexical match (IT projects)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.5.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Value Projects/Portfolios"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers portfolio valuation. Assess commercial value, strategic fit, risk, resource demand, and option value for portfolio prioritization, using stated assumptions and confidence. It does not determine accounting fair value, intangible-asset valuation, impairment, capitalization, or financial-reporting treatment. Valuation states evidence, commercial assumptions, dependencies, uncertainty, option value, resource demand, and downside risk, with methods kept consistent and comparable across the portfolio (b21 evidence discipline). Investment decisions are the delegated authorities'. Excludes accounting fair value, intangible valuation, impairment, capitalization, and financial reporting (Finance); investment decisions (delegated authorities); portfolio assessment against composition targets (CM-1-3-4-5-3).\nIn scope: Value projects and portfolio elements on commercial value, fit, risk, resource demand, and option value | state evidence, assumptions, dependencies, uncertainty, and downside risk | keep methods consistent and comparable\nOut of scope: Accounting valuation/impairment/capitalization (Finance) | investment decisions (delegated authorities) | composition assessment (CM-1-3-4-5-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Technology needs (CM-1-3-4-5-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "project and market evidence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "resource data"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Comparable commercial valuations with uncertainty, option value, and downside risk"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every project's worth stated the same way, so priorities compare honestly."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20819"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assess the product, service, and R&D portfolios against strategy — composition, balance, readiness, performance, and lifecycle position — producing the evidenced portfolio picture the recommendation step works from."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Assessment step; review readiness dimensions verbatim — maturity and readiness across the non-financial dimensions weigh alongside financial performance. APQC 'Assess IT remediation' is a FALSE lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.5.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Assess Portfolios"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers portfolio assessment: analyzing composition and balance against the innovation vision and approved strategies (horizon mix, risk mix, market coverage); assessing performance and lifecycle position of in-market products and services using governed evidence; identifying candidates for stage, stop, accelerate, extend, reposition, or retire recommendations; and stating findings with confidence. Portfolio assessment may consider technical maturity, regulatory readiness, supply readiness, customer evidence, channel fit, brand fit, capability readiness, and lifecycle performance—not only financial performance. Assessment informs; recommendations are the manage step's (CM-1-3-4-5-4) and decisions the delegated authorities'. Excludes the recommendations (CM-1-3-4-5-4); decisions (delegated authorities); performance measurement execution (CM-1-3-5-5, operating processes).\nIn scope: Analyze portfolio composition and balance against strategy | assess technical, regulatory, supply, customer, channel, brand, and capability readiness alongside lifecycle performance | identify decision candidates with confidence\nOut of scope: Recommendations (CM-1-3-4-5-4) | decisions (delegated authorities) | measurement execution (CM-1-3-5-5, operating processes)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Valuations (CM-1-3-4-5-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "market and performance evidence"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "strategy direction (CM-1-3-2, CM-1-3-4-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Evidenced portfolio assessments with decision candidates"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "An honest picture of what the portfolio is, before deciding what it should be."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Manage step of the portfolio cycle — conceptually 'Develop Portfolio Recommendations and Track Decisions' per review; the locked name 'Manage R&D Portfolios' is too narrow for its product/service/R&D scope, so the review's preferred label is queued prominently for the naming pass. Governance-safe wording (recommend/record/track, b22 pattern); execution routes through the b25 change-control discipline. APQC 'Manage routings' is a FALSE match (manufacturing routings — second occurrence). Step 3d naming pass, authority-risk category (2026-09-21, the decision owner's approval): renamed 'Manage R&D Portfolios' -> 'Develop Portfolio Recommendations and Track Decisions' — the 'Manage' step of the portfolio cycle develops recommendations and tracks decisions across product/service/R&D scope (governance-safe recommend/record/track wording)."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/11743"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage Product, Service, and R&D Portfolios"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manage R&D Portfolios"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop the portfolio recommendations and track delegated decisions — consolidating assessments into stage, stop, accelerate, extend, reposition, and retirement recommendations across the product, service, and R&D portfolios, submitting them to the applicable delegated authorities, and tracking execution of approved decisions through the accountable processes."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.5.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop Portfolio Recommendations and Track Decisions"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers portfolio management: consolidating valuations and assessments into portfolio recommendations; submitting recommendations through the applicable delegation of authority; recording approved decisions; and tracking their execution — development changes via the stage gates (CM-1-3-4-3-1), product retirement, extension, and repositioning via Manage Product/Service Change (CM-1-3-4-3-3) and the transition planning of the accountable processes (per the L4 transition statement). Scope spans the product, service, and R&D portfolios — the locked name understates this (preferred label queued). Recommends and tracks; never approves investments (delegated authorities) or executes changes (accountable processes). Excludes investment and portfolio approval (delegated authorities); change execution (CM-1-3-4-3-3, operating processes); development governance (CM-1-3-4-3-1); IP portfolio stewardship (CM-1-3-4-4-6). Develop Portfolio Recommendations and Track Decisions (CM-1-3-4-5-4) provides portfolio recommendations that inform Manage Product/Service Change (CM-1-3-4-3-3); change decisions follow the applicable delegated authorities.\nIn scope: Consolidate assessments into portfolio recommendations across product, service, and R&D portfolios | submit through delegated authority and record decisions | track execution through the accountable processes\nOut of scope: Investment/portfolio approval (delegated authorities) | change execution (CM-1-3-4-3-3, operating processes) | development governance (CM-1-3-4-3-1) | IP portfolios (CM-1-3-4-4-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Portfolio assessments (CM-1-3-4-5-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "delegated-authority requirements"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "execution status from accountable processes"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Portfolio recommendations, recorded decisions, and execution tracking"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Portfolio decisions made by the right authority, executed by the right process, tracked to done."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16824"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coordinate the collaboration channels through which product and service innovation works with manufacturing, customers and technical service, research partners, and marketing — consistent intake, IP, and confidentiality controls across all channels — so collaboration accelerates innovation without leaking assets or blurring operational boundaries."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — parallel collaboration variant set integrated at the L4 (batch 24 pattern); children continuous (standing channels). Review collaboration rule verbatim in scope note — no channel creates implied obligations outside the approved control set; strengthens the batch 25 external-idea boundary. APQC candidate is a WEAK broad match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "R&D Collaboration"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the collaboration channel set: manufacturing collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6-1), customer and technical-service collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6-2), research-partner collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6-3), and marketing collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6-4) — a parallel variant set integrated at this L4 (consistency of intake, IP, and confidentiality controls; prioritization; conflict resolution — the batch 24 integration pattern). No collaboration channel creates an implied confidentiality, ownership, compensation, exclusivity, procurement, licensing, co-development, publication, data-sharing, or evaluation obligation outside approved intake, Legal/IP, Procurement, Privacy, Security, and delegated-authority controls. All channels operate under the intellectual-asset framework (CM-1-3-4-4-1) with agreements drafted and executed by Legal and sourced through Procurement (batch 25 boundary), and the batch 21 privacy and competitor-information controls where customer or market information is involved. Excludes collaboration agreement drafting/execution (Legal, Procurement); the development work itself (CM-1-3-4-3); operational direction of any counterpart function (their owners, locked rules); IP framework ownership (CM-1-3-4-4-1, Legal). R&D Collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6) provides manufacturing, customer, research-partner, and marketing collaboration evidence to inform Product & Service Development (CM-1-3-4-3); the recipient retains its own decisions. R&D Collaboration (CM-1-3-4-6) provides governed collaboration results, real-use evidence, feasibility constraints, and timing to inform Concept & Feasibility Study (CM-1-3-4-2); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Coordinate the four collaboration channels with consistent intake, IP, and confidentiality controls | integrate collaboration input into the innovation processes | prioritize and resolve conflicts across channels\nOut of scope: Agreement drafting/execution (Legal, Procurement) | development execution (CM-1-3-4-3) | operational direction of counterpart functions (their owners, locked rules) | IP framework ownership (CM-1-3-4-4-1, Legal)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/governedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "IP and confidentiality framework (CM-1-3-4-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Innovation priorities (CM-1-3-4-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel inputs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed, integrated collaboration across the four channels"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaboration that speeds innovation up without giving its assets away."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/16819"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with refining, blending, and manufacturing on product innovation — developability, blend and formulation feasibility, scale-up, and trial production — informing development without directing any manufacturing operation."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Manufacturing channel; informs-and-requests, never directs — locked operational boundaries; review trial-approval statement verbatim (safety, quality, engineering, production-planning, scheduling, change-control approvals of the owning function). APQC 'Design for manufacturing' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.6.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with Manufacturing"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the manufacturing collaboration channel: engaging refining, blending, lubricants, and packaging operations on candidate-product developability and cost; blend and formulation feasibility within operational constraints; scale-up planning and trial coordination; and feeding manufacturing insight into concepts and development. Trial production, scale-up, blend trials, plant trials, and operational experiments require the owning operating function's safety, quality, engineering, production-planning, scheduling, and change-control approvals. The locked boundaries govern: refining, blending, terminal, and manufacturing operations are directed by their owners (Refining, Midstream locks, batch 20 architecture) — collaboration informs and requests, never directs. Excludes manufacturing/refining operational direction (their owners, locked rules); trial approvals (owning operating functions); production scheduling (operations); quality operations (batch 18); development decisions (CM-1-3-4-3). Collaborate with Manufacturing (CM-1-3-4-6-1) provides manufacturing developability, formulation feasibility, scale-up, and trial evidence to inform Conduct Product Development (CM-1-3-4-3-2); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Engage operations on developability, feasibility, and cost | coordinate scale-up and trials under the owning function's approvals | feed manufacturing insight into concepts and development\nOut of scope: Operational direction (Refining/Midstream locks) | trial approvals (owning operating functions) | production scheduling (operations) | quality operations (batch 18) | development decisions (CM-1-3-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Candidate products and concepts"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "operational constraints and cost data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "trial capacity (operations)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Manufacturing feasibility insight and coordinated, operations-approved trials"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Products designed with the plant, not thrown over its wall."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/20044"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with customers and technical service on product innovation — performance needs, field experience, and field trials — under the applicable privacy, confidentiality, and intake controls, feeding real-use evidence into concepts and development."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Customer channel; review field-trial readiness statement verbatim (suitability, safety, insurance/liability, privacy/confidentiality, product stewardship, consent, technical-service, contractual controls before use) — material for fuels, additives, lubricants, and services; b21 privacy/competitive controls and b25 intake rule govern. APQC 'Collaborate with customers' STRONG, no validator — genuine comparative anchor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.6.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with Customers/Technical Service"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the customer collaboration channel: engaging customers, marketers, and technical service on product performance needs and field experience; coordinating field trials with customer consent and clear IP/confidentiality terms (through approved intake channels and Legal-executed agreements — batch 25 rule); and feeding validated field evidence into concepts (CM-1-3-4-2) and development (CM-1-3-4-3). Customer or field trials require appropriate product suitability, safety, insurance/liability, privacy/confidentiality, product stewardship, consent, technical-service, and contractual controls before use. Customer data and feedback operate under the batch 21 privacy and counterparty-confidentiality controls; competitively sensitive information about other parties is never solicited (batch 21 prohibition). Technical-service delivery itself is Service & Support's (CM-1-3-9). Excludes technical-service delivery (CM-1-3-9); account management (CM-1-3-6); agreement drafting (Legal); trial-readiness control ownership (accountable functions); the analyses (CM-1-3-1-4). Collaborate with Customers/Technical Service (CM-1-3-4-6-2) provides validated customer performance needs, field experience, and concept-trial evidence to inform Conduct Research (CM-1-3-4-2-2); the recipient retains its own decisions. Collaborate with Customers/Technical Service (CM-1-3-4-6-2) provides validated field-trial results and customer performance needs to inform Conduct Product Development (CM-1-3-4-3-2); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Engage customers and technical service on performance needs and field experience | coordinate consented field trials only after the required readiness controls are satisfied | feed validated field evidence into concepts and development\nOut of scope: Technical-service delivery (CM-1-3-9) | account management (CM-1-3-6) | agreement drafting (Legal) | trial-readiness control ownership (accountable functions) | the analyses (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Customer and technical-service relationships"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "consented field data"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "field trial capacity"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Validated field evidence for concepts and development"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Products proven where they are actually used, safely and by consent."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10092"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with external research partners — universities, institutes, suppliers, and technology providers — on research and development of mutual interest, under agreements Legal executes and the IP framework governs."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Partner channel; review provenance requirement verbatim (provenance, permitted-use rights, confidentiality classification, IP allocation assumptions, publication/review controls, data-sharing restrictions before integration) — extends the b21 evidence-lineage discipline; b25 procurement/Legal boundary governs. APQC 'Collaborate on design with suppliers and external partners' is a WEAK adjacent match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.6.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with Research Partners"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the research-partner channel: identifying and engaging partners against the technology needs (CM-1-3-4-5-1) and R&D plans (CM-1-3-4-1-3); shaping collaboration scope, contributions, and IP positions within the intellectual-asset framework (CM-1-3-4-4-1); operating joint work under Legal-executed agreements sourced through Procurement (batch 25 boundary); and integrating partner results into concepts and development. Partner results must have defined provenance, permitted-use rights, confidentiality classification, IP allocation assumptions, publication/review controls, and data-sharing restrictions before integration into concepts or development. Partner selection and contracting follow Procurement and Legal; IP allocation positions are business input to Legal's drafting. Excludes partner contracting and agreement execution (Procurement, Legal); IP legal terms (Legal); the research/development work governance (CM-1-3-4-2-3, CM-1-3-4-3-1). Collaborate with Research Partners (CM-1-3-4-6-3) brings partner research and findings that inform Conduct Research (CM-1-3-4-2-2).\nIn scope: Engage partners against technology needs and plans | shape scope, contributions, and IP positions as business input | operate joint work under executed agreements | integrate results only with defined provenance, rights, and restrictions\nOut of scope: Contracting/agreement execution (Procurement, Legal) | IP legal terms (Legal) | research/development governance (CM-1-3-4-2-3, CM-1-3-4-3-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-5-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Technology needs (CM-1-3-4-5-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "executed agreements (Legal, Procurement)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "partner capabilities"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed partner collaborations and integrated results with provenance and rights"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Outside brains on inside problems, on paper Legal wrote."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/19553"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-4-6"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with the marketing strategy, design, and planning functions on product and service innovation — carrying market-facing requirements into R&D and innovation results back into offers, communications, and launch preparation."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 26 (2026-09-20). Internal marketing channel; review authority statement verbatim — provides inputs, timing, constraints, and readiness evidence; approves nothing the accountable processes own. Lowercase 'marketing' in the locked name — capitalization normalized in the queued label. APQC 'Collaborate with regulators' is a FALSE mapping (wrong counterpart entirely)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.4.6.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Collaborate with marketing"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the internal marketing channel: carrying proposition, offer, channel, and experience requirements (CM-1-3-2, CM-1-3-3) into concepts and development; returning innovation results, constraints, and timing into offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1), communications strategy (CM-1-3-3-5), and planning (CM-1-3-5); and keeping innovation and marketing calendars coherent. The collaboration interface does not approve offers, claims, campaigns, pricing, channel changes, launch readiness, or market release. It provides inputs, timing, constraints, and readiness evidence to those accountable processes. An internal collaboration interface: the counterpart processes own their decisions (three-layer rule, batch 22); launch remains Planning/Execution's (batch 25 boundary). Excludes the counterpart processes' decisions (their owners); offer, claim, campaign, pricing, channel, and launch approvals (accountable processes); offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1); launch planning/execution (CM-1-3-5/6); development decisions (CM-1-3-4-3). Collaborate with marketing (CM-1-3-4-6-4) provides innovation results, limitations, readiness evidence, and development timing to inform Marketing Communications Planning (CM-1-3-5-3); the recipient retains its own decisions.\nIn scope: Carry market-facing requirements into concepts and development | return innovation results, constraints, timing, and readiness evidence to offers, communications, and planning | keep innovation and marketing calendars coherent\nOut of scope: Counterpart decisions and approvals (their owners) | offer definition (CM-1-3-3-1) | launch (CM-1-3-5/6) | development decisions (CM-1-3-4-3)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Strategy and design requirements (CM-1-3-2/3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "development status (CM-1-3-4-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "planning calendars (CM-1-3-5)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/continuous"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Coherent innovation-to-marketing requirements, timing, and readiness flow"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Innovation and marketing moving on one calendar, not surprising each other."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Marketing sales & operations planning consist of processes that define the go-to-market approach to a level of detail that enables activity planning, forecasting, & performance review against each of the elements (customer offer, sales channel & operations, distribution network)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Marketing & Sales Operations Planning"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 3
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 27 (2026-09-20). Concept-type: process — one sales-planning cycle with a feedback loop; tactical. Review label decision: strategy direction is owned upstream (batch 22), so the preferred label 'Sales Planning' is queued prominently to prevent scope creep from the locked 'Sales Strategy & Planning' name. Canonical forecast-versus-targets rule verbatim in scope note. Glossary distinctions (review): demand forecast = governed prediction produced through Produce Demand Forecast; sales target = management commitment or plan expectation allocated to a segment, channel, account group, or period; quota = individual/team performance commitment in performance-management or incentive context; sales plan = planned actions, account priorities, resources, and commercial activity to pursue targets; actual = governed realized volume, margin, revenue, cost, or activity evidence from accountable systems/processes. Lifecycle: forecast-input agreement (enduring) enables targets and account planning → margin-gap analysis → next cycle. APQC 'Develop sales strategy' STRONG, no validator — genuine anchor, direction owned at CM-1-3-2. Step 3d naming pass, authority-risk category (2026-09-21, the decision owner's approval): renamed 'Sales Strategy & Planning' -> 'Sales Planning' — strategy direction is owned upstream (CM-1-3-2); the concept is sales planning, not sales strategy."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10103"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Sales Strategy & Planning"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Plan the sales effort that delivers the approved strategies — the agreed sales-input process into the governed demand forecast, allocated sales targets, account plans, and the margin-gap feedback loop — so sales execution runs against deliberate, evidenced plans rather than improvised quotas."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.5.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Sales Planning"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the sales-planning cycle: the enduring sales-side forecast-input operating agreement (CM-1-3-5-1-2), determining and allocating sales targets (CM-1-3-5-1-1), performing account planning (CM-1-3-5-1-3), and analyzing gaps between forecast, plan, targets, and actual margin performance (CM-1-3-5-1-4) as the feedback loop into the next cycle and forecast-input improvements. The enterprise demand forecast is produced, published, changed, versioned, and governed only by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1). The sales organization supplies agreed sales intelligence, account plans, pipeline evidence, promotion calendars, channel signals, and other approved inputs to that process. Sales targets are management-accountability commitments allocated from approved plans, not forecasts; they must never be relabeled, substituted for, or used to overwrite the governed demand forecast. Plans within approved direction: sales strategy direction is owned by the strategy branch (CM-1-3-2-4, CM-1-3-2-2, batch 22) — this cluster is sales planning, not strategy; sales force sizing assumptions come from the channel structure designs (CM-1-3-3-3-4, batch 23 headcount boundary — HR and management own headcount). Excludes sales strategy direction (CM-1-3-2, batch 22); the enterprise demand forecast (CM-1-1-1-1, locked); sales execution (CM-1-3-6-2); pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3); channel/partner management (CM-1-3-6-1); headcount and appointments (HR, management); quote/contract processes (CM-1-3-7-2). Sales Execution (CM-1-3-6-2) executes the sales effort against the plans and targets produced by Sales Planning (CM-1-3-5-1).\nIn scope: Run the sales-planning cycle | maintain the agreed sales input process into the governed forecast | allocate targets from approved plans | plan accounts | analyze forecast/plan/target/actual margin gaps as feedback\nOut of scope: Sales strategy direction (CM-1-3-2, batch 22) | enterprise demand forecast (CM-1-1-1-1, locked) | sales execution (CM-1-3-6-2) | pricing (CM-1-3-3-2, CM-1-3-6-3) | partner management (CM-1-3-6-1) | headcount (HR, management) | quotes/contracts (CM-1-3-7-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-source"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/enabledBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-3-6"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/informedBy": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-5"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved strategies (CM-1-3-2)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "channel and offer designs (CM-1-3-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed demand forecast (CM-1-1-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "margin actuals (governed sources)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Agreed sales plans: input process, targets, and account plans"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "A sales effort planned on evidence, measured against its own plan."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 4
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1-1",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/12900"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Determine and allocate sales targets — volume, margin, and mix commitments by segment, channel, account group, and period — from approved plans and the governed forecast, as managerial commitments under the applicable approvals, never as a substitute forecast."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 27 (2026-09-20). Target step; review validation statement verbatim; target-versus-quota distinction per the L4 glossary. APQC 'Determine inventory targets' is a FALSE lexical match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.5.1.1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Determine & Allocate Sales Targets"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers target setting: deriving target envelopes from approved commercial plans and the governed demand forecast (consumed, never adjusted); allocating targets by segment, channel of trade, account group, and period; reconciling allocations with account plans (CM-1-3-5-1-3); and maintaining targets under the applicable delegation of authority. Target allocation is validated against approved supply, inventory, channel, sales-capacity, offer, pricing, and promotion assumptions; it does not create supply commitments or override allocation decisions. Targets are accountability constructs distinct from the forecast and from quotas (glossary at the L4); quota setting and target-based incentive design belong to the performance-management and compensation processes (HR). Excludes the forecast (CM-1-1-1-1); quota and incentive/compensation design (HR, performance management); supply commitments and allocation overrides (accountable operating processes); target approval beyond delegated authority (management authorities); account-level execution (CM-1-3-6).\nIn scope: Derive target envelopes from approved plans and the consumed forecast | allocate by segment, channel, account group, and period | validate against approved supply, capacity, offer, pricing, and promotion assumptions | maintain under delegated authority\nOut of scope: The forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) | quotas and incentive design (HR, performance management) | supply commitments/allocation overrides (operating processes) | approvals beyond delegated authority (management) | execution (CM-1-3-6)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Approved plans (CM-1-3-2/5)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "account, capacity, and promotion assumptions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "governed forecast (CM-1-1-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1-3"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Allocated, feasibility-validated sales targets under delegated authority"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commitments people can be held to, derived from evidence they can see."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1-2",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10235"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop and agree the sales-side input process into the governed demand forecast — which sales intelligence, account plans, and pipeline evidence feed Produce Demand Forecast, in what form, cadence, and quality — never producing or adjusting the forecast itself."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 27 (2026-09-20). The batch's sharpest boundary row: the locked name could read as owning the forecasting process — the canonical rule (verbatim in scope note) fixes the reading: sales-side input process only, agreed with the forecast owner. Relation decision (review): an enduring operating agreement, so it enables targets and account planning rather than strictly preceding them each cycle. APQC 'Develop baseline demand forecasts' is a false-direction match (forecast production, exactly what this row must not do)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.5.1.2"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Develop & Agree Demand Forecasting Process"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers the forecast-input operating agreement: agreeing with Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1) what sales-side inputs the governed forecast consumes (account intelligence, pipeline evidence, promotional and campaign calendars, channel signals); defining input form, cadence, quality expectations, and accountabilities on the sales side; and maintaining the agreement as planning evolves — an enduring operating agreement rather than a recurring annual phase (review). The enterprise demand forecast is produced, published, changed, versioned, and governed only by Produce Demand Forecast (CM-1-1-1-1). The sales organization supplies agreed sales intelligence, account plans, pipeline evidence, promotion calendars, channel signals, and other approved inputs to that process. Sales targets are management-accountability commitments allocated from approved plans, not forecasts; they must never be relabeled, substituted for, or used to overwrite the governed demand forecast. The forecast process itself, its methods, and its publication are Produce Demand Forecast's; disagreements about forecast content follow that process's governance. Excludes forecast production, methods, publication, and adjustment (CM-1-1-1-1, locked); forecast-process ownership (CM-1-1-1-1); the inputs' downstream use (CM-1-1-1-1).\nIn scope: Agree the sales-input set, form, cadence, and quality with Produce Demand Forecast | define sales-side input accountabilities | maintain the enduring input agreement\nOut of scope: Forecast production/methods/publication/adjustment (CM-1-1-1-1, locked) | forecast-process ownership (CM-1-1-1-1) | downstream input use (CM-1-1-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-1-1-1"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-4-2"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-6-2-1"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Produce Demand Forecast's input requirements (CM-1-1-1-1)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "promotional calendars (CM-1-3-5-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "sales planning outputs"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planningLevel": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/planning-level/tactical"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The agreed, maintained sales-input process into the governed forecast"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The forecast fed well by sales, and never fought by sales."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1-3",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10728"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform account planning for the accounts and account groups the sales plan prioritizes — objectives, opportunity maps, action plans, and resource assumptions per account — feeding execution and the forecast-input process with account-level evidence."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 27 (2026-09-20). Account-planning step; review data restriction verbatim — approved access and privacy/confidentiality controls only, no improperly obtained competitor, supplier, or customer-confidential information (b21 discipline); b23 assignment boundary inherited. APQC 'Perform planning and management accounting' is a FALSE lexical match (accounting)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.5.1.3"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Perform Account Planning"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers account planning: building account plans (objectives, opportunity and risk maps, planned actions, service and support assumptions) for prioritized accounts and marketer relationships using governed counterparty evidence (CM-1-3-1-4) and cost-to-serve input (CM-1-2-6-1-3); aligning plans with targets and channel engagement models (CM-1-3-3-3-4); and feeding account intelligence into the forecast-input process (CM-1-3-5-1-2). Account plans may use customer, relationship, commercial, and performance data only through approved access and privacy/confidentiality controls. They must not incorporate improperly obtained competitor, supplier, or customer-confidential information. Planning, not execution: account interventions, negotiations, and relationship execution belong to Channel & Partner Management and Sales Execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2); credit decisions to the credit process (b11 boundary); individual account assignments follow the management processes (b23 boundary). Excludes account execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2); credit decisions (b11 boundary); account assignments (management processes, b23); pricing and quotes (CM-1-3-6-3, CM-1-3-7-2). Perform Account Planning (CM-1-3-5-1-3) supplies approved account objectives, opportunity maps, action plans, and resource assumptions that Sales Execution (CM-1-3-6-2) consumes in its defined work.\nIn scope: Build account plans from governed evidence under approved access controls | align with targets and engagement models | feed account intelligence into the forecast-input process\nOut of scope: Account execution (CM-1-3-6-1/-2) | credit decisions (b11 boundary) | account assignments (management, b23) | pricing/quotes (CM-1-3-6-3, CM-1-3-7-2)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/review-link"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Counterparty findings (CM-1-3-1-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "cost-to-serve (CM-1-2-6-1-3)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "engagement models (CM-1-3-3-3-4)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "targets (CM-1-3-5-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/precedes": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1-4"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Account plans with objectives, actions, and evidence"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Every priority account approached with a plan, not a habit."
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/responsibleDomain": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Commercial & Marketing"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/taxonomyLevel": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
    "@value": 5
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1-4",
  "@type": [
   "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/references": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/apqc-pcf-7.2.2/element/10025"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/src-apqc-pcf-001"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/source/step3c-definition-workbook"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Gaps Between Forecast, Plan, Targets, and Actual Margin Performance"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-5-1"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze the gaps between the demand forecast, sales plan, targets, and actual margin performance — where assumptions, plans, and commitments diverged from governed actuals, and why — producing the evidence the next planning cycle corrects from."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Batch 27 (2026-09-20). Feedback step of the sales-planning cycle; review terminology correction — forecast (demand/volume) and margin (financial expectation) are different objects, so the comparison set is spelled out and the corrected label queued; governed-actuals discipline (Finance data consumed, never produced). APQC returned NONE — 'Analyze demographics' is a false match."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
   {
    "@value": "CM 1.3.5.1.4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Analyze Gaps Between Forecast & Actual Margins"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Covers margin-gap analysis: comparing governed actual volume, mix, and margin (Finance and settlement data — consumed, never produced) against the demand forecast and sales-plan assumptions, targets, and margin expectations; building the margin bridge and decomposing variance drivers by segment, channel, account, and cause; distinguishing plan quality, input quality, execution, and market causes; and feeding findings to the next cycle, the forecast-input process, and Marketing Performance Analysis (CM-1-3-5-5). Terminology (review): the locked name compares objects of different kinds — the process compares demand forecast and sales-plan assumptions, targets, actual volume/mix/margin, and the margin bridge/variance drivers; the preferred label is queued. Analysis, not correction: pricing corrections follow the pricing processes; forecast-method questions follow Produce Demand Forecast's governance; findings with potential legal or compliance implications escalate to Legal/Compliance (b23 pattern). Excludes financial reporting production (Finance); forecast adjustment (CM-1-1-1-1); pricing corrections (CM-1-3-6-3); target changes (CM-1-3-5-1-1 with approvals); legal determinations (Legal/Compliance).\nIn scope: Compare governed actuals to forecast assumptions, plans, and targets | build the margin bridge and decompose variance drivers | distinguish plan, input, execution, and market causes | feed findings to the next cycle and performance analysis\nOut of scope: Financial reporting (Finance) | forecast adjustment (CM-1-1-1-1) | pricing corrections (CM-1-3-6-3) | target changes (CM-1-3-5-1-1) | legal determinations (Legal/Compliance)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqcMappingDecision": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/apqc-mapping-decision/no-candidate"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/conceptKind": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/concept-kind/process"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/dependsOnOutputOf": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/process/CM-1-3-6-2-7"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/keyInputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Governed actuals (Finance, settlements)"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "forecast and plan assumptions"
   },
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "targets (CM-1-3-5-1-1)"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operatingMode": [
   {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/operating-mode/periodic"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryOutputFlow": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Margin-gap findings with the bridge and causes, feeding the next planning cycle"
   }
  ],
  "https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/primaryPurpose": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Next year's plan built on why this year's plan missed."
   }
  ],
