   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "US federal regulatory-gate context for determining whether a motor-vehicle fuel or fuel additive may require EPA registration/testing under 40 CFR Part 79 before introduction into US commerce. Applicability depends on product classification, intended use, regulated-party role, composition, market, and other facts. Other EPA, state, federal, non-US, product-stewardship, tax, quality, labeling, and environmental requirements may apply. Regulatory classification, submission, testing obligations, and legal sufficiency are determined by accountable Regulatory, Legal, Quality, and Product Stewardship functions. RFS-related registration (§80.1450) is a separate regime. Does not determine internal process design. Evidence only, not text to copy."
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title": [
